<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/67734004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/59066005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/362884007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p3_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the cervical spine, focusing on the first seven vertebrae. On the left side, each vertebra is labeled with its name and number, from C1 (Atlas) to C7. The intervertebral discs are distinctly marked in blue. On the right, a side view of the entire cervical spine is displayed, extending from the base of the skull to the seventh cervical vertebra, with the intervertebral discs similarly highlighted in blue. The background is white, providing a clear contrast to the bone structures, and there are red curved lines on the right side, though their specific connection to the vertebrae is not indicated." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed cross-sectional view of the neck, with muscles colored in shades of red and pink, while bones and other tissues are depicted in lighter colors. Black lines connect labels to the corresponding anatomical parts. The infrahyoid muscles, including the thyrohyoid, omohyoid, sternohyoid, and sternothyroid, are shown extending from the hyoid bone towards the sternum and thyroid cartilage. Other structures like the inferior edge of the mandible, styloglossus, hyoid bone, thyroid cartilage, thyroid gland, trachea, clavicles, sternum, and scapula are also depicted, illustrating their spatial relationships within the neck." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/2fa2e0b77333> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/264042003> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p50_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomy of the neck region, highlighting various muscles, triangles, and other structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the human head and neck with various structures labeled. The supraorbital margin is located above the eye socket, and the infraorbital margin is situated below it. The trapezius muscle is depicted on the back of the neck, and the omohyoid's inferior belly is near the collarbone. The submandibular gland is shown under the jaw, and the thyroid cartilage is at the base of the throat. The clavicle and jugular notch are also labeled, along with the sternal and clavicular heads of the sternocleidomastoid muscle. The labels are connected to their respective parts using black lines, and the text is in black font against a white background, with red decorative elements framing the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/31764008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/69748006> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://snomed.info/id/263352000> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b15> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/6f7cf9cf4298> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.8"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/6f7cf9cf4298> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed anatomical illustration of the muscles of the head and neck, with a side profile view of a human head and upper torso." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p50_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the neck, with different muscles and triangles clearly labeled. The muscles are color-coded with green, pink, yellow, blue, and red shades to distinguish them. The m. mylohyoideus is positioned at the base of the tongue near the mandible, while the m. digastricus and the os hyoideum are also depicted. The m. scalenus medius and m. scalenus anterior are shown in the middle and front of the neck, respectively. The m. omohyoideus is divided into its superior and inferior parts, and the m. sternocleidomastoideus is visible on either side of the neck. The submental triangle is located below the chin, the submandibular triangle is beneath the mandible, the carotid triangle is between the sternocleidomastoid and omohyoid muscles, the muscular triangle is between the sternocleidomastoid, omohyoid, and clavicle, the occipital triangle is behind the ear, and the subclavian triangle is below the clavicle. The processus mastoideus and clavicular parts are also labeled. The labels are connected to the structures they identify with dashed lines. The orientation of the image aligns the left side of the depicted person with the left side of the image, and the right side with the right, with the head facing left and the back towards the viewer." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p50_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#figureRef> "c005" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a side profile of a human head and upper torso, with the scalp gradient transitioning from darker red at the base to lighter pink at the top, suggesting hair follicles. The face and neck are filled with various muscle groups, all shaded in red, showing intricate details of different layers and orientations, particularly around the eye, cheek, and jaw. The ears are light beige, contrasting with the red muscles, and positioned on either side of the head. The neck muscles, also in red, extend down to the shoulders, arranged vertically and horizontally. Several red lines extend from the neck area downward, possibly representing nerves or blood vessels, but without specific labels." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://snomed.info/id/263352000> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#located_in> <http://snomed.info/id/362649006> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
