<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a side profile view of the neck and shoulder area, with the sternocleidomastoid muscle positioned at the top and the trapezius muscle at the bottom. The clavicle forms the base of the subclavian triangle, which is marked in red and situated between these two muscles. Text labels such as \"processus mastoideus,\" \"m. sternocleidomastoideus,\" \"m. trapezius,\" and \"clavícula\" are connected to their respective anatomical structures with leader lines. The subclavian triangle is labeled within the red highlighted area. A partial view of the skull, including parts of the temporal bone and the mastoid process, is also visible. In the top left corner, there is a section labeled \"(CM),\" which seems to be part of a larger diagram." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/4a34b55686b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s2> .
