<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed cross-sectional view of the pelvic area, with various anatomical structures labeled and connected by leader lines. The transversalis fascia spans horizontally across the upper portion of the diagram in a translucent green. The anterior superior iliac spine is positioned on the left side, pointing to a bony prominence. The inferior epigastric artery is near the center-right, depicted as a red vessel running vertically. The deep inguinal ring is on the right, marking an opening in the transversalis fascia. The spermatic cord, shown in blue, runs downward from the deep inguinal ring on the lower right. The femoral artery and vein are in the lower central part, represented by two parallel blood vessels. The inguinal ligament is on the left, a horizontal band of tissue running between the anterior superior iliac spine and the pubic tubercle. The pubic symphysis is at the bottom right, indicating the junction of the two pubic bones. The colors used are primarily shades of green, red, blue, and beige to differentiate tissues and organs." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s11> .
