<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p19_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features the hypothalamus in light gray, labeled with structures like the prefrontal cortex, hippocampus, and arcuate nucleus. Within the hypothalamus, the Supraoptic nucleus (SON) is highlighted in green and the Paraventricular nucleus (PVN) in blue. Black arrows indicate magnocellular neuronal axons connecting to the posterior pituitary, while dotted lines represent parvocellular neuronal axons linking to other brain regions such as the dorsal vagal complex, spinal cord, sensory cortices, arcuate nucleus, and amygdala. The posterior pituitary is shown as a dark gray structure at the bottom, labeled with \"Oxytocin secretion to the periphery,\" and oxytocin molecules are depicted being released into the bloodstream. A legend in the lower right corner explains symbols: solid arrows for axonal release, dotted arrows for dendritic release, and an orange circle for endogenous oxytocin. Additionally, a simplified side profile of a human head and brain is positioned in the bottom right, with a black box highlighting the area corresponding to the hypothalamus in the main diagram." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/26173982196c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s7> .
