<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a cross-sectional view of the abdominal cavity, with the liver positioned at the upper left and the stomach at the upper right. The lesser omentum is depicted as a band-like structure connecting the stomach to the liver, while the duodenum, the first part of the small intestine, is shown below the stomach in a curved shape. The gallbladder is situated below the liver, and the epiploic foramen is represented as a small opening in the lesser omentum. Each structure is labeled with arrows pointing to their respective locations, with a yellow arrow specifically indicating the epiploic foramen." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s7> .
