<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p70_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents the human head and neck muscles in a side profile view, with the left side of the head facing forward. The skull's outer surface is rendered in light gray, providing a clear contrast to the red muscles. The muscles are intricately detailed, showing layers of muscle fibers that cover the face and neck. Red lines traverse the muscles, indicating the direction of muscle fibers, particularly prominent in the neck area. Facial features like the eye socket, cheekbones, and jawline are visible but less detailed compared to the muscles." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s7> .
