<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/31389004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p16_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the head and neck, with the nasal cavity positioned at the top within the skull. Above the nasal cavity are the paranasal sinuses. The nasopharynx is depicted as a larger space behind the nasal cavity, extending down to the level of the soft palate. The hard palate is shown as a horizontal structure separating the nasal cavity from the oral cavity, with the soft palate located below it. The tongue is positioned in the oral cavity below the hard palate, while the mandible, or lower jawbone, is visible at the bottom left. The hyoid bone is drawn below the mandible, connected to the larynx. The thyroid cartilage is illustrated as a large, butterfly-shaped structure at the front of the neck, just below the hyoid bone. The cricoid cartilage, a ring-shaped structure, is located below the thyroid cartilage. The epiglottis is shown as a flap of tissue at the top of the laryngopharynx. Vocal cords are depicted as two thin, vertical structures within the larynx. Blue arrows indicate the direction of airflow through the nasal cavity and nasopharynx." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/dbe463d255fd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s7> .
