<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p7_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure presents two diagrams of the hyoid bone. In Diagram A, the hyoid bone is displayed from a lateral perspective, with labels for the greater horn, lesser horn, fibrocartilage, and the body of the hyoid bone. The greater horn is positioned on the upper left side, the lesser horn on the upper right, and the fibrocartilage is at the bottom, connecting the body of the hyoid bone. Diagram B shows the hyoid bone from a right anterolateral view, featuring the same labeled anatomical features as Diagram A. Each label is accompanied by a leader line or arrow pointing directly to the corresponding part of the hyoid bone." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-sectional view of the pharynx and related structures, with the nasopharynx positioned at the top, above the soft palate. The oropharynx is centrally located between the soft palate and the epiglottis, while the laryngopharynx is at the bottom, continuous with the larynx. The cricoid cartilage is situated at the very bottom of the image. Different regions are highlighted in yellow, green, and blue to distinguish the nasopharynx, oropharynx, and laryngopharynx, respectively. The epiglottis is shown above the cricoid cartilage, and the soft palate is placed between the nasopharynx and the oropharynx." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s7> .
