<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/59820001> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p71_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The liver is positioned on the left side of the image, shown in a cutaway view to reveal its internal structure. To the right of the liver, the pancreas is depicted with its internal ducts and connections visible. At the bottom of the image, a section of the small intestine, the duodenum, is displayed, labeled with \"Major duodenal papilla\" and \"Minor duodenal papilla.\" A green tube-like structure, the bile duct, extends from the liver into the duodenum and is labeled at the top. A smaller green tube, the accessory pancreatic duct, and a larger yellowish tube, the main pancreatic duct, both extend from the pancreas into the duodenum and are labeled near the top of the image. The convergence of these ducts into the duodenum is labeled as the \"Hepatopancreatic Ampulla\" at the bottom of the image. Leader lines and arrows connect the labels to the corresponding anatomical structures in the liver, pancreas, and duodenum." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p63_b5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p70_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The kidneys are positioned laterally in the image, with the right kidney on the left side and the left kidney on the right side, both depicted in a pinkish-red color. Each kidney is divided into three sections: the head at the top, the body in the middle, and the tail at the bottom. The aorta is a large red vessel running centrally from the heart, curving upwards towards the kidneys. The inferior vena cava, shown in blue, extends from the kidneys and curves upwards towards the heart. The digestive tract components are situated below the kidneys, with the duodenum appearing as a yellowish structure beneath the head of the pancreas. The superior mesenteric vein is a blue vessel branching off from the inferior vena cava and extending towards the liver, while the superior mesenteric artery is a red vessel branching off from the aorta and extending towards the intestines. The jejunum is labeled as a section of the small intestine located below the superior mesenteric artery. Each anatomical structure is labeled with black text, connected by leader lines or arrows pointing to the corresponding part, with labels placed around the periphery of the image." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p71_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38848004> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p71_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/69930009> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/75a8c84d58f0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caused_by> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/7a6d4014d851> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p63_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the human large intestine, detailing its various components such as the right and left colic flexures, the ascending and transverse colon, and the cecum with the appendix." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/feea4ec7a7ec> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caused_by> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration shows a cross-section of a tubular organ, with a pinkish outer layer representing the mucosa and a yellowish inner layer for the submucosa. The organ is cylindrical and hollow, with two open ends at the top and bottom. Blood vessels are depicted in red, indicating their role in circulation. The term \"Vasa recta\" is written in black text on the right side, pointing to a network of small blood vessels running horizontally across the submucosa. Below this label, \"Arterial arcades\" is written in black text, pointing to a series of curved blood vessel networks forming an arch-like pattern within the submucosa. The illustration is labeled \"A\" in the bottom left corner." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p63_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/66754008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p72_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents an anterior view with the descending part of the duodenum positioned at the top-left, colored reddish-brown. The major duodenal papilla is a small, circular structure within this section, marked by a label. The main pancreatic duct, also yellowish, runs vertically to the right of the bile duct. The hepatopancreatic ampulla and sphincter, a more complex structure, is located at the bottom where the bile duct and main pancreatic duct join. Arrows and lines connect labels to the corresponding anatomical parts, illustrating the relationship between the ducts and sphincters." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p60_b12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
