<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p63_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents the large intestine in a relaxed state, with natural folds and curves. The right colic flexure is positioned at the upper left side of the image, pointing to the right, while the left colic flexure is at the upper right, pointing left. The transverse colon runs horizontally across the middle of the image. The ascending colon curves upwards on the left side. On the right side, the omental appendices are shown as a vertical line pointing downwards. The haustra of the colon are depicted as a series of pouches along the ascending colon, highlighted by a rectangular box. The taeniae coli appear as a band-like structure running along the ascending colon. The ileum, a section of the small intestine, connects to the cecum, which is a pouch-like structure at the bottom left. The sigmoid colon is a curved section located below the transverse colon, leading to the rectum, an elongated section at the bottom. Finally, the anal canal is shown as the final section of the rectum, leading to the anus. Labels are placed around the periphery of the image, pointing to specific parts of the intestine." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s13> .
