<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the head and neck, with the superior constrictor positioned at the top. The stylopharyngeus is on the left side, extending from the styloid process to the pharynx. The medial constrictor is centrally located, while the salpingopharyngeus is on the right. The palatopharyngeus is near the right side, and the thyropharyngeus is below the medial constrictor. The inferior constrictor is at the bottom, with the cricopharyngeus positioned at the very bottom. Each muscle is depicted in a distinct color: the superior constrictor in light blue, the stylopharyngeus in yellow, the medial constrictor in orange, the salpingopharyngeus in purple, the palatopharyngeus and thyropharyngeus in green, and the inferior constrictor and cricopharyngeus in orange. Leader lines connect labels to the respective muscles." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s10> .
