<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features two highlighted regions: the occipital triangle in green, situated at the back of the neck near the base of the skull, and the subclavian triangle in yellow, located below the clavicle towards the shoulder. Arrows point to these regions and to the omohyoid muscle, which is depicted with its superior belly in yellow and green above the clavicle and its inferior belly in red and green below the clavicle. The muscles are shown in a semi-transparent manner in a side view of the head and neck, revealing underlying structures. The background is white, and the diagram is credited to \"TeachMeAnatomy\" in the bottom right corner." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s10> .
