<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the muscles and ligaments related to the tongue and neck. The Hyoglossus Muscle is positioned on the left side, extending from the hyoid bone towards the base of the tongue. Near the back of the throat, the Middle Pharyngeal Constrictor Muscle is located at the upper middle part. Below the Hyoglossus Muscle, the Thyrohyoid Muscle stretches from the thyroid cartilage to the hyoid bone. The Genioglossus Muscle is prominently displayed in the center, extending from the mandible to the base of the tongue. The Greater Horn of the hyoid bone is on the right, while the Lesser Horn is on the left. At the bottom, the Geniohyoid Muscle, Mylohyoid Muscle, Sternohyoid Muscle, Omohyoid Muscle, and Digastric Muscle (Fibrous Loop) are all depicted, each extending from different origins to the hyoid bone. Leader lines or arrows connect each label to its corresponding anatomical structure, with labels placed around the periphery of the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the pharyngeal muscles, with the superior constrictor at the top in green, the stylopharyngeus below it in orange, the middle constrictor in the center in reddish-brown, and the inferior constrictor at the bottom in blue. The background features a simplified outline of the head and neck, with the skull and some bones visible. The muscles are displayed in cross-section, providing a clear view of their arrangement within the pharynx. The source of the image, \"teachmeanatomy,\" is labeled at the bottom right corner." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s10> .
