<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p47_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the chest area, with the ribcage framing the central structures. At the top-center, the trachea is depicted as a tube-like structure extending downward, with the esophagus positioned just below it. The left common carotid artery branches off from the arch of the aorta near the top-center, while the left subclavian artery extends downward from it. The brachiocephalic trunk is shown branching off from the arch of the aorta, also near the top-center. At the bottom of the image, the diaphragm is visible, separating the thoracic cavity from the abdominal cavity. Each structure is labeled with a leader line or arrow pointing to it." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s8> .
