<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p3_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diaphragm is colored red and its attachments to the ribs and spine are clearly marked. The ribs are depicted in blue and white, while the spine is shown in light beige. The abdominal muscles and other surrounding structures are visible but not labeled. The lateral arcuate ligament is positioned at the left side of the image, the esophageal opening is near the center, and the costal margin is along the lower edge of the rib cage. The median arcuate ligament is centered in the image, while the medial arcuate ligament is on the right side. The left crus is located on the left side of the diaphragm, and the right crus is on the right side. The quadratus lumborum muscle is positioned below the spine, and the psoas major is below the quadratus lumborum." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s8> .
