<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a series of curved lines at the top representing ribs, labeled from \"T7\" to \"T12.\" The spine is centrally positioned, extending from the ribcage to the lumbar region, with vertebrae labeled \"T10,\" \"T11,\" and \"T12.\" At the bottom, the pelvis is shown, including the sacrum and coccyx, with \"L1\" labeled below the sacrum. Several blue curved lines run horizontally across the image, dividing the torso into sections corresponding to the thoracic and lumbar vertebrae. The skin and muscles are depicted in light beige, covering the entire torso, with darker brown lines indicating abdominal muscles at the bottom." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s8> .
