<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p3_b10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p1_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two sections: the upper part displays the ribcage, while the lower part focuses on the abdominal and pelvic regions. The diaphragm is shown as a large, dome-shaped muscle at the top of the abdominal cavity. The inferior thoracic aperture is green-outlined, indicating the opening between the ribcage and the diaphragm. The abdominal wall is depicted in orange, surrounding the abdominal cavity. The iliac crest appears as a curved bone on the side of the pelvis. The pelvic inlet is outlined in blue at the top of the pelvic cavity. The lower limb bones, including the femur and tibia, are visible at the bottom of the image. Leader lines connect the labels to specific parts of the anatomy." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/7cbc284ee0da> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/5798000> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration provides a posterior view of the abdominal cavity, with the falciform ligament positioned at the top left. Near the center-left, the round ligament and para-umbilical veins are shown, while the parietal peritoneum is marked on the left side. A horizontal line across the middle indicates the level of section Figure 5.5A. The median umbilical fold is near the median line, and the medial umbilical fold is closer to the bottom. The lateral umbilical fold is near the bottom on the center-right, while the lateral inguinal fossa is on the lower right and the medial inguinal fossa is on the lower left. The supravesical fossa is at the bottom center. The diaphragm is marked at the top center, and the peritoneum is shown extending from top to bottom. The posterior layer of the rectus sheath is near the top on the center-right, and the arcuate line is on the upper right. The rectus abdominis is in the middle-right, and the inferior epigastric vein and artery are near the bottom on the center-right. The iliopubic tract is on the lower right, while the external iliac artery and vein are also near the bottom on the center-right. The ductus deferens is at the lower center." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/7cbc284ee0da> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/50230006> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s8> .
