<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p60_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image has a beige background with the text \"SUBMANDIBULAR SALIVARY GLAND\" centered at the top. Beneath the text, a light beige mandible with a darker outline is drawn, featuring teeth in a lighter purple shade. The molars are on the left, and the incisors and canines are on the right. To the right of the mandible, a pinkish-purple submandibular salivary gland is depicted, connected to the mandible by a thin, white, curved structure representing the duct, which extends from the bottom of the mandible towards the top left." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
