<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b13> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed anatomical illustration of a section of the human skull, with the temporal bone visible at the upper part and the mandible at the lower part. A large, pinkish-red muscle, the masseter, is prominently displayed, extending from the temporal bone towards the mandible. The masseter muscle is centrally located within the image, and its attachment to the mandible at its lower edge is clearly shown. The eye socket is positioned above the masseter muscle, while the mandible and teeth are below it. The teeth, specifically the lower molars and premolars, are depicted on the right side of the mandible. The rest of the image uses a neutral beige tone for the bone structure, making the pinkish-red muscles stand out." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
