<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a detailed anatomical cross-section of the shoulder and upper arm muscles, including the Deltoid, Pectoralis Major, Teres Major, and Latissimus Dorsi, along with the surrounding skin, subcutaneous tissue, and bones." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/370dca5f2bc5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed anatomical illustration of the shoulder and upper arm muscles, rendered in shades of red and orange. Some areas are highlighted in lighter colors, likely indicating different layers or depths. The muscles are shown in a cross-sectional view, revealing their arrangement and connections. Beneath the skin, the muscles are clearly defined, showing their texture and directionality. At the top of the image, parts of the skull and the clavicle are visible. There are faint lines and markings within the muscles, suggesting the presence of blood vessels and nerves, depicted in blue and white, respectively. The image is symmetrical, with the left and right sides mirroring each other." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
