<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration is a side profile view of the head and neck, with the head turned slightly to the right. Muscles are depicted in shades of red, with darker shades indicating depth and layering. Leader lines connect labels to their corresponding muscle groups. The epicranial aponeurosis is at the top of the head, the frontalis on the forehead, the occipitalis at the back of the head, the temporalis on the side near the temple, the orbicularis oculi around the eye, the zygomaticus near the corner of the mouth, the buccinator and orbicularis oris around the mouth, the masseter in the jaw area, the sternocleidomastoid along the side of the neck, and the platysma at the base of the neck." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/48fd16d09028> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/91609006> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
