<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b13> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the lower jaw and its surrounding structures. The mandible stands out as the main bone structure, while the temporal bone is visible at the top left, featuring the inner ear region with the semicircular canals and the cochlea. The zygomatic arch is positioned at the top right, forming the cheekbone. The teeth are displayed in the bottom right corner. Two muscles are highlighted in pink: the masseter muscle, located within the mandible, and another muscle below it, likely the medial pterygoid muscle, extending towards the chin area. The bones are rendered in a light beige color, while the muscles are shaded in a darker pink, providing a clear contrast. The image offers a cross-sectional view, focusing on the lower jaw and the muscles that control its movement." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
