<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a side profile view of a human head with various muscles highlighted and labeled. The frontalis muscle is labeled on the forehead, the temporalis on the temple area, the orbicularis oculi around the eye, the occipitalis at the back of the head near the neck, the orbicularis oris around the mouth, the masseter in the jaw, and the buccinator inside the cheek. Each label is connected to its corresponding muscle by a black arrow, and the muscles are depicted in shades of red and pink, showing their location and structure in relation to the skull and facial features." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s4> .
