<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the hypothalamus at the top, depicted as a purple structure, and a dashed arrow pointing downward. Below the hypothalamus is the anterior pituitary gland, shown as a pink structure, with a yellow circle labeled \"TRH\" connected by a dashed arrow from the hypothalamus. On the left side, the thyroid gland is represented as a pink, butterfly-shaped structure, with a solid arrow labeled \"TSH\" coming from the anterior pituitary gland. The circulatory system is a red, tube-like structure looping around, containing yellow circles labeled \"T4\" and \"T3\". At the bottom, the liver is an irregularly shaped brown structure, with solid arrows labeled \"T4\" and \"T3\" pointing from the thyroid gland. Another arrow from the liver to the circulatory system is labeled \"Conjugated T4 and T3\". The intestine, also at the bottom, is a pink, curved structure, with an arrow labeled \"T4\" and \"T3\" pointing from it to the liver. The legend, located at the bottom right, includes a plus sign for \"Stimulatory pathway\" and a minus sign for \"Inhibitory pathway\"." <urn:graph:endocrine/s6> .
