<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p63_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized into sections with different colors. At the top left, a yellow box labeled \"Stimuli\" lists \"Dehydration (↓ Blood volume)\" and \"Salt ingestion,\" both pointing downward to a pink box labeled \"↑ Blood osmolality.\" From this central pink box, arrows lead to \"Osmoreceptors in hypothalamus\" and \"Thirst.\" The hypothalamus section shows an arrow from \"Osmoreceptors in hypothalamus\" to a blue box labeled \"↑ ADH\" (Antidiuretic Hormone), representing the posterior pituitary. An arrow from \"↑ ADH\" points downward to \"Water retention by kidneys.\" At the bottom, a blue box labeled \"Negative feedback responses\" has arrows from \"Water retention by kidneys\" pointing to \"↑ Blood volume\" and \"↓ Blood osmolality.\" An arrow from \"Thirst\" leads to \"Drinking\" at the bottom right." <urn:graph:endocrine/s6> .
