<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p12_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into two sections. The first section shows an anterior view of a neck with the head slightly tilted back, featuring a photograph where an arrow points to the platysma muscle below the chin and down the neck. The second section provides a close-up side view of the neck, with arrows pointing out various anatomical features: the angle of the mandible, the external jugular vein, the sterno hyoid muscle, the laryngeal prominence, and the jugular notch. Additionally, the letters 'T', 'CI', and 'S' are near the sterno hyoid muscle without specific labels. Red borders frame the images, and text labels are positioned next to the corresponding anatomical features." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s6> .
