<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p58_b17> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a side view of the head and neck, with muscles displayed in shades of pink and red. The processus mastoideus is marked near the top of the image as a bony prominence behind the ear. The m. scalenus medius is situated in the middle of the neck, between the m. sternocleidomastoideus and the m. scalenus anterior. The m. scalenus anterior is located closer to the front of the neck, below the m. sternocleidomastoideus. The m. omohyoideus (venter inferior) is shown at the base of the neck, below the m. scalenus anterior. The Occipital triangle is highlighted in red and is located at the back of the neck, near the base of the skull, marked by a red box. The m. trapezius is displayed at the back of the neck and shoulder, extending down to the clavicle. The clavícula is a curved, flat bone at the bottom of the image. Leader lines connect the labels to specific parts of the muscles and bones, pointing to the relevant areas in the image. The muscles are depicted as elongated, rectangular shapes with striations representing the muscle fibers. The Occipital triangle is a triangular region outlined in red, with its apex at the base of the skull and its base extending down to the neck." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p58_b17> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/50755001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s6> .
