<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b13> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the neck, with muscles and triangles color-coded for clarity. The m. mylohyoideus is situated at the base of the mandible, while the m. digastricus is positioned below the mandibula. The os hyoideum, or hyoid bone, is prominently displayed, with the m. omohyoideus (venter inferior) located below it. The m. scalenus medius and m. scalenus anterior are depicted in the upper back region, and the m. sternocleidomastoideus is shown as a large muscle on either side of the neck. The submental triangle is located at the chin area, and the submandibular triangle is situated below the mandible. The carotid triangle is positioned between the sternocleidomastoideus and the omohyoideus muscles, while the muscular triangle is delineated by the sternocleidomastoideus, omohyoideus, and trapezius muscles. The occipital triangle is at the back of the neck, and the subclavian triangle is near the clavicle. Text labels are connected to the corresponding structures with dashed lines." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s6> .
