<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a green tube-like structure at the top left, labeled as the intralobular duct. Small, round structures branching off from the intercalated ducts are labeled as pancreatic acini. Near the base of these acini, a cluster of cells is labeled as centroacinar cells, while the cells within the acini are labeled as pancreatic acinar cells. A small blood vessel near the base of the acini is labeled as a venule, and tiny blood vessels surrounding the acini are labeled as capillaries. A cluster of cells with different colors, labeled as a pancreatic islet, is also present. Within this islet, specific cells are labeled as alpha cells and beta cells." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s8> .
