<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The histological section is organized with labels on the left side, each connected by lines to corresponding structures within the image. At the top left, an intercalated duct is indicated, while the connective tissue capsule is positioned on the left. Near the center-left, a pancreatic islet is marked, appearing as a darker, denser cluster of cells. The bottom-left highlights centroacinar cells, situated centrally within acini. Secretory acini are located towards the right, appearing filled with secretions, and capillaries are marked on the right side, representing a network of blood vessels." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s8> .
