<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two sections by a vertical line. At the top left, an intercalated duct is labeled, appearing as a narrow channel surrounded by cells. On the left side, endocrine cells of the pancreatic islet are labeled, showing clusters with darker nuclei and less cytoplasm. Also on the left, capillaries are labeled, highlighted in red as small, thin-walled blood vessels scattered throughout the tissue. On the right, a group of centroacinar cells in serous acinus is labeled, featuring large, round nuclei and abundant cytoplasm. The connective tissue capsule is labeled on the right, appearing as a thin, fibrous layer surrounding the tissue. At the bottom right, another group of centroacinar cells is labeled, similar to those on the right." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s8> .
