<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/db0f4b57dc0b> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/276654001> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the abdominal wall, with the superficial inguinal ring positioned at the base of the scrotum and the deep inguinal ring situated deeper within the abdominal wall. The inguinal triangle is depicted as the area between these two rings. The inguinal ligament is shown as a horizontal band running across the lower abdomen. The transversalis fascia is portrayed as a layer surrounding the abdominal contents, while the peritoneum is shown lining the abdominal cavity. Additionally, the illustration includes the median, lateral, and medial umbilical folds near the umbilicus." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/422543003> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p87_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A black dashed line runs horizontally across the chest area, just below the ribs, indicating the boundary between the liver and the diaphragm. A dotted red line extends from this costal margin towards the lower right side of the abdomen, representing the edge of the liver. The area between the costal margin and the liver edge is shaded in light pink, indicating mild liver enlargement. Further down, another dotted line marks the boundary for moderate enlargement, shaded in a darker pink. Below this, a darker shade indicates marked enlargement. A blue arrow points downwards from the liver edge towards the marked enlargement area, emphasizing the progression of liver enlargement." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The table is divided into three sections: a header row labeled \"Characteristics\" that spans the top, and two columns titled \"Direct (Acquired)\" and \"Indirect (Congenital)\". The header row's first cell is yellow, while the cells beneath \"Direct (Acquired)\" are green and those under \"Indirect (Congenital)\" are pink. The text within the cells is black on a white background, and there are no arrows or leader lines." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p87_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/10200004> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
