<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is vertically oriented, with the top representing the superior part and the bottom the inferior part. At the top, the inferior epigastric vessels are labeled, depicted in blue and red. Near the upper right, the deep inguinal ring is labeled, pointing to an opening in the extraperitoneal fascia. On the right, the extraperitoneal fascia is labeled, indicating the outermost layer, while the parietal peritoneum is labeled on the left as the innermost layer. The conjoint tendon is labeled near the middle left, and a peritoneal bulge is shown as a protrusion in the parietal peritoneum. The superficial inguinal ring is labeled near the bottom center, and the testis is depicted as an oval shape at the bottom, extending into the scrotum. Color-coding is used: parietal peritoneum is light blue, conjoint tendon is yellow, extraperitoneal fascia is green, and the inguinal rings are marked with dashed lines. A red arrow points downward from the inferior epigastric vessels. The text \"Fig. 4.49 Direct inguinal hernia\" is written at the bottom." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates two labeled diagrams of the anterior view of the lower abdomen and scrotum, highlighting various anatomical structures and their relationships." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/414403008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
