<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A diagram of the lymphatic system is presented, featuring color-coded regions. The axillary lymph nodes are highlighted in red on the left side of the chest, near the armpit, with a black rectangular box surrounding this area. A leader line with an arrow points from the bottom of the box to the red-highlighted region, indicating the location of the axillary lymph nodes. The superficial inguinal lymph nodes are shown in blue in the lower abdomen, near the groin, with a leader line and arrow pointing to this area. Green lines represent lymphatic vessels extending from these highlighted areas towards other parts of the body, though these are not labeled. The background is white, and the person depicted is shirtless, showing the torso and lower abdomen." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
