<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure consists of two labeled diagrams, both providing an anterior view of the lower abdomen and scrotum area. In Diagram A, the semilunar line is marked on the left side of the abdominal wall, while the inferior epigastric artery is shown as a red branching structure near the lower abdomen. The inguinal triangle is labeled below the deep inguinal ring, and the superficial inguinal ring is marked as a larger circular area above the deep inguinal ring. Diagram B focuses on different structures, with the anterior superior iliac spine labeled on the upper right side of the pelvis. The inguinal ligament is shown as a horizontal line connecting the anterior superior iliac spine to the pubic tubercle. The superficial inguinal ring is again labeled, this time near the pubic region, and a hand is depicted with fingers inserted into the loose skin above the scrotum. Both diagrams use leader lines to connect labels to specific parts of the body, providing a clear visual reference." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s12> .
