<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p81_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a microscopic view of tissue stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E). The cells are densely packed, with the nuclei appearing dark purple and the cytoplasm a lighter pink. Numerous small, round nuclei are scattered throughout the field, alongside some larger, more irregularly shaped nuclei. The background reveals a dense network of intercellular spaces filled with a pale, granular substance. In the bottom left corner, there is a lowercase \"f\" in black, and in the bottom center, a large letter \"M\" also in black." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/fd36e2e3d425> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#located_in> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s1> .
