<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/21483005> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a table with four main columns: Hormone, Composition, MW (kDa), and Major Functions. Additional text below the table describes the extension of the CNS, storage and release of secretory products, composition, and functions related to the hypothalamus and pituitary structures, such as herring bodies and pituicytes." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a microscopic view of cells with large, round nuclei centrally located within the cells, stained dark purple. The surrounding cytoplasm appears granular and is stained a lighter blue or pinkish hue. Red blood cells, smaller and biconcave in shape, are visible in the background, stained bright red." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with several labeled areas. Near the upper middle, the label 'N' points to a cluster of cells with dark blue nuclei. Towards the upper right and lower right, the label 'S' indicates lighter areas, possibly spaces or cystic structures. In the lower middle, the label 'P' marks another cluster of cells with dark blue nuclei. The tissue exhibits a variety of cell types, with nuclei distributed throughout and pinkish-red cytoplasm typical of H&E staining." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p81_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s1> .
