<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p84_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A green, teardrop-shaped gallbladder is positioned at the top left of the image. Extending downward from the gallbladder is the cystic duct, also green. The right hepatic duct branches off to the right side of the image, while the left hepatic duct branches off to the left, both in green. The common hepatic duct, another green tube, combines these two hepatic ducts and continues downward to merge with the bile duct. The bile duct is pinkish-orange, starting from the confluence of the common hepatic duct and curving slightly to the right. The descending part of the duodenum, a large, curved pinkish-orange tube, loops around the bile duct and is labeled at the bottom. The main pancreatic duct, colored yellow-green, runs alongside the descending part of the duodenum and connects to the bile duct. Each structure is labeled with a black line pointing to it." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s10> .
