<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p84_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents the gallbladder as a teardrop-shaped structure, with the narrowest part at the top labeled as the neck, the middle section labeled as the body, and the widest part at the bottom labeled as the fundus. Green is used to represent the gallbladder and its ducts, with arrows indicating the direction of bile flow. The cystic duct, common hepatic duct, and common bile duct are all labeled with their respective dimensions, showing how they connect and branch off from each other. The bile flow is indicated by arrows moving from the gallbladder into the common hepatic duct and then into the common bile duct." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s10> .
