<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p72_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The liver is positioned at the top of the image, with an arrow pointing to its upper portion. The right and left hepatic ducts are shown branching off from the liver, with arrows indicating their downward extension. The cystic duct is situated below the common hepatic duct, marked by an arrow pointing to its connection with the gallbladder. The gallbladder itself is located below the cystic duct, with an arrow pointing to its body. The common hepatic duct is shown merging with the cystic duct, labeled with an arrow at the confluence of the two ducts. The bile duct is positioned below the common hepatic duct, indicated by an arrow pointing downward. The main pancreatic duct is located on the right side of the image, with an arrow pointing to the duct running parallel to the descending part of the duodenum. The descending part of the duodenum is at the bottom of the image, labeled with an arrow pointing to its lower part. The illustration uses white lines and arrows to connect labels to the anatomy, which is depicted in grayscale." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p81_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/15776009> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s10> .
