<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The large intestine is shown in a light pink color, while the small intestine is depicted in a slightly darker shade. The labels are written in black text and connected to specific parts of the intestine by thin lines. The taeniae coli are labeled at the top left, indicating three parallel bands running along the colon. The pre-ileal label is near the upper right, pointing to a section before the ileocecal valve, while the post-ileal label is slightly below, indicating the section after the valve. The ileum label is near the lower right, pointing to the terminal part of the small intestine that joins the colon. The retrocecal label is on the left, indicating the area behind the cecum. The cecum label is near the bottom center, marking the start of the large intestine where it connects to the small intestine. The pelvic label is on the right, pointing to the pelvic region of the colon, and the subcecal label is at the very bottom, indicating the area below the cecum. The overall layout shows the large intestine in a somewhat curved position, with the cecum and ileocecal valve being prominent features." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s10> .
