<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p19_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a green triangle, representing the nonsteroid hormone, pointing towards a pink square labeled \"Receptor protein\" on the plasma membrane. The plasma membrane is depicted as a light blue area, framing the cell's components. Near the receptor protein, a purple sphere labeled \"Activated enzyme\" is positioned, with a yellow starburst shape labeled \"ATP\" nearby. A yellow oval labeled \"cAMP\" is connected to the activated enzyme by an arrow, indicating the flow of the process. The beige background within the cell is labeled \"CYTOPLASM.\" At the bottom right, text describes the outcome of the signaling pathway as affecting cellular functions, such as glycogen breakdown." <urn:graph:endocrine/s3> .
