<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p92_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure presents an anterior view of the human torso, with various internal organs displayed in a cross-sectional layout. The liver is positioned on the right side of the upper abdomen, above the stomach. The stomach is shown below the liver and slightly to the left. The kidneys are situated on both sides of the spine, just below the diaphragm. The intestines are depicted in a coiled pattern, with the large intestine labeled with several spinal nerve levels. The bladder is located at the lower part of the abdomen, below the intestines. The spinal nerves that innervate each organ are indicated by labels such as \"T6-T9\" for the liver and \"S2\" for the bladder. Additionally, a network of blood vessels and nerves is visible, though not specifically labeled." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s5> .
