<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p28_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The table is organized into four columns and five rows, with the header row divided into distinct colors: yellow, purple, orange, and beige. The first column lists the names of the nerves, such as Thoraco-abdominal, Subcostal, Iliohypogastric, and Ilio-Inguinal, all aligned to the left. The second column describes the origin of each nerve, also aligned to the left. The third column details the course of each nerve, and the fourth column outlines the distribution of each nerve, both aligned to the left." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s5> .
