<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p3_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents an anatomical illustration of the neck area, with a human face partially visible showing the lower part of the nose and mouth. Below the mouth, the neck is depicted with labeled structures: the larynx in gray positioned just above the thyroid gland, the thyroid gland in pink below the larynx, the parathyroid glands indicated by small yellow dots within the thyroid gland, and the trachea at the bottom extending downward from the thyroid gland. On the right side, a detailed back view of the thyroid gland shows its butterfly-like shape in pink, with the parathyroid glands marked by small yellow dots on either side. Labels are placed near the corresponding structures with lines or arrows pointing to specific parts, providing a clear and organized layout of the neck's internal structures." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p5_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/309150002> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The diagram illustrates a thyroid gland with two lobes connected by an isthmus, featuring small pinkish areas marked by black dots." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/1313fa2702dd> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/113192009> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/83aeca8f4ed0> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/90780006> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The thyroid gland is depicted in orange with a smooth, slightly irregular surface. It consists of two distinct lobes connected by a narrow isthmus at the bottom. Each lobe contains a small, round, pinkish area marked by a black dot with a leader line pointing to it. The diagram is simple, lacking additional details such as blood vessels, nerves, or surrounding structures." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s1> .
