<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top of the image, the text \"Thyroid gland (back view)\" is displayed. The thyroid gland itself is portrayed as a butterfly-shaped organ, featuring two lobes connected by a narrow isthmus. Near the upper part of this depiction, two small, yellowish structures are positioned on either side, representing the parathyroid glands. Above these structures, the label \"Parathyroid glands\" is placed, with leader lines extending downward to point to each of the parathyroid glands, one on the left and one on the right." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s1> .
