<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p19_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The main image displays the dorsal surface of the tongue with various labeled structures, including the lingual tonsil at the back, the sulcus terminalis, and the apex of the tongue. Close-up views of the vallate papilla, taste bud, and histology of a taste bud are provided, each connected by leader lines and arrows from the main image. The close-up of the vallate papilla shows the epithelium and sensory nerve endings, while the taste bud close-up highlights gustatory cells, supporting cells, basal cells, and the taste pore. Text labels appear directly above or below the corresponding areas, detailing the structures such as the epithelium, stratified squamous epithelium, gustatory cells, and sensory nerves." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/9eaa1e0970d9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
