<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/426215008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed microscopic view of tongue tissue. At the top left, small, rounded projections known as fungiform papillae are visible. Below these, elongated, thread-like structures called filiform papillae extend downward. In the middle section, bundles of skeletal muscle fibers run horizontally. Blood vessels, including both arteries and veins, appear as thin, circular structures, with veins being slightly larger than arteries. Towards the bottom right, the anterior lingual glands are located, featuring interlobular ducts, mucous acinus, and serous acinus. The excretory duct of the lingual gland is visible at the bottom right." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/181769001> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/5319eeffae32> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#located_in> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/cb80bdc7475a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/e6d4e18872c2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Negated> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/3ed9642313e0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed microscopic cross-section of tongue tissue, showing various anatomical structures such as fungiform and filiform papillae, skeletal muscle, blood vessels, connective tissue, anterior lingual glands, nerve fibers, and the mucosa." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/298225002> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the mechanisms of taste perception on the tongue, focusing on bitter, sweet, umami, sour, and salt tastes." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://snomed.info/id/368729003> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#located_in> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram provides a detailed view of the tongue, with specific areas dedicated to illustrating the mechanisms for detecting bitter, sweet, umami, sour, and salt tastes. Each taste modality is represented in a distinct section, likely with labels and possibly arrows indicating the direction of signal processing. The layout is organized to show how each taste is processed, potentially with different shapes or colors to distinguish between the types of taste receptors involved." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/8001006> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/3ed9642313e0> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p19_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/255551008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#figureRef> "c016" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a histological section with a layered structure. At the top left, a small opening represents the taste pore, above which are the microvilli, appearing as tiny, finger-like projections. Beneath the microvilli, elongated supporting cells are situated. At the base, smaller basal cells are positioned, and at the bottom, a bundle of fibers likely represents a nerve." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/e34f553ca797> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p19_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the dorsal surface of the tongue and the structures involved in taste perception, including the lingual tonsil, sulcus terminalis, apex of the tongue, and the four types of papillae: filiform, fungiform, vallate, and foliate." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/f09d13dc67d9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
