<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/256913008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/f3d94374c192> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/49690003> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A detailed diagram of a taste bud is presented, with the stratified squamous epithelium appearing as a pinkish layer of cells at the top right. The taste bud itself is a blue, oval-shaped cluster centrally located beneath the epithelium. Within the taste bud, neuroepithelial cells are elongated and interconnected, while sustentacular cells are smaller and more rounded, positioned near the bottom left. A yellow, circular taste pore is situated at the bottom of the taste bud, and microvilli, fine hair-like structures, extend from the neuroepithelial cells on the right side." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/936bf1db0359> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed microscopic cross-section of tongue tissue, showcasing various anatomical structures such as the stratified squamous epithelium, lingual epithelium, lamina propria, taste buds, furrows, serous glands, secondary papillae, blood vessels, and skeletal muscles." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/e6d4e18872c2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#located_in> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/217219> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/3b21243192ee> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/49475008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
