<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/3ed9642313e0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/28273000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The tongue is depicted in a pinkish-red color with a detailed texture that includes small bumps and ridges. A green oval shape indicates the bitter area at the back of the tongue. Two yellow sections labeled \"SOUR\" are positioned on the left and right sides of the tongue, near the middle and slightly towards the front. A pink section labeled \"UMAMI\" is situated in the center of the tongue, extending from the middle towards the front. Two blue sections labeled \"SALT\" are located at the bottom of the tongue, on either side, closer to the front. An orange section labeled \"SWEET\" is at the very front of the tongue, also closer to the bottom." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/9eaa1e0970d9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/4421005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section of the tongue's surface stained with hematoxylin and eosin, showing foliate papillae, taste buds, ducts, serous glands, and striated muscle." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p20_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#figureRef> "c016" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/9eaa1e0970d9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/113343008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p106_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A diagram is presented with a central vein shown as a blue shaded area in the middle, encircled by a dashed pink outline. Extending from this central vein are pink lines representing the portal canals, reaching towards the outer edges of the diagram. The label \"central vein\" is positioned in black text on the right side, pointing to the blue area, while \"portal canals\" is written in black at the bottom, directing attention to the pink lines." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed microscopic cross-section of tissue, likely from the tongue. At the very top, there is a pinkish-red, multi-layered structure representing the stratified squamous epithelium. Just beneath it lies the lingual epithelium, also pinkish-red but slightly less distinct. Beneath the lingual epithelium, the lamina propria appears as a lighter pink, mesh-like structure. Within the lamina propria, small, oval-shaped, darker pink areas represent taste buds. A groove or depression, known as a furrow, is visible as a darker line separating regions. Thin, elongated excretory ducts of the serous (von Ebner glands) extend into the lamina propria from the glandular area, where rounded, cluster-like serous secretory acini are located. Dark red, tubular blood vessels are scattered throughout the lamina propria. Skeletal muscles are depicted with elongated, parallel longitudinal fibers running along the tissue and shorter, circular transverse fibers. The labels are positioned on the left side of the image, pointing to the corresponding structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/65750006> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/410678000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/65067005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
