<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/bfacd4b01182> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed microscopic view of the tongue's surface, with labels positioned to the left and right of the image pointing to various structures. The lingual epithelium is situated at the top left, appearing as a stratified squamous epithelium with cells that have nuclei and cytoplasm. Below it lies the lamina propria, which consists of connective tissue containing blood vessels and sustentacular cells. Blood vessels are visible within the lamina propria, and the taste pore is a small opening on the surface of the taste bud. Basal cells are located at the base of the taste buds, and a furrow is depicted as a groove or depression in the lingual epithelium." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/99826bd2746d> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p20_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays several conical structures labeled as \"filiform papillae,\" arranged in a row and embedded within a layer of tissue. These structures are pinkish-purple in color, indicating staining with a dye like hematoxylin and eosin (H&E). Below the filiform papillae, there is a layer of connective tissue with a more granular appearance, having a lighter pink hue compared to the papillae. The label \"filiform papillae\" is positioned at the top left corner of the image, pointing to the conical structures on the surface of the tissue." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/936bf1db0359> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/60692007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
