<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p24_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a cross-section of the tongue, focusing on the circumvallate papilla region. At the top left, taste buds are visible as small, elongated dark purple dots within the epithelial layer. The circumvallate papilla is the central feature, appearing as a raised, circular structure with a pinkish hue, surrounded by the taste buds. Beneath the epithelium, serous glands are scattered around the papilla, appearing as small, rounded structures with a lighter pink color compared to the surrounding tissue. Arrows in the image point directly to these corresponding structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s5> .
