<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a labeled illustration of the human endocrine system, with each gland and organ positioned to reflect their anatomical locations. The hypothalamus is shown at the base of the brain, connected to the pituitary gland, which is situated just below it. The thyroid gland is depicted in the neck region, with the parathyroid glands located on its posterior surface. The liver is shown in the upper right quadrant of the abdomen, while the adrenal glands are positioned atop the kidneys. The kidneys are illustrated in the lower back, behind the abdominal cavity. The testes are placed in the scrotum, and the ovary is shown in the pelvic cavity. The uterus is also located in the pelvic cavity, and although the placenta is not depicted, it is implied to be connected to the uterus. The stomach is positioned in the upper left quadrant of the abdomen. Each gland and organ is labeled with its corresponding hormones and functions." <urn:graph:endocrine/s2> .
