<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A cross-section of the brain is shown, with the hypothalamus positioned at the top right and connected to the pituitary gland via the hypothalamic-pituitary stalk. The anterior lobe of the pituitary gland is displayed below the hypothalamus, linked by the superior hypophyseal artery. The primary capillary plexus is depicted surrounding the base of the pituitary gland, with hypophyseal portal veins connecting it to the secondary capillary plexus within the anterior lobe. The secondary capillary plexus is situated at the bottom of the pituitary gland. Text labels identify the \"anterior lobe of pituitary\" at the top left, the \"superior hypophyseal artery\" pointing to the blood vessel, and the \"hypothalamus\" at the top right." <urn:graph:endocrine/s2> .
