<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p18_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized into sections, each containing a visual representation of a biological component. At the top left, an intestine is depicted with a label pointing to the right that reads \"Increases Ca²⁺ uptake in intestines.\" A curved arrow leads from the intestine to the center region, where a kidney is labeled \"Stimulates Ca²⁺ uptake in kidneys.\" From the kidney, another curved arrow points to the right center region, where the parathyroid gland is shown with the label \"PTH\" (Parathyroid Hormone). A curved arrow extends from the parathyroid gland to the bottom center, where a bone is displayed with the label \"Stimulates Ca²⁺ release from bones.\" A curved arrow then leads from the bone to the bottom left, where a box reads \"Blood Ca²⁺ level rises.\" Another curved arrow connects this box to the bottom right section, which contains the text \"Homeostasis: Blood Ca²⁺ level (about 10 mg/100 mL).\" Finally, a green arrow points upwards from the \"PTH\" section towards the \"STIMULUS: Falling blood Ca²⁺ level\" section at the top right." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s3> .
