<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The table has a light blue background with black text. There are no leader lines or arrows connecting the text to other parts of the image." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the process of iron absorption by enterocytes, showing the movement of heme and its breakdown into porphyrin and Fe²⁺, as well as the transport of Fe²⁺ via ferroportin and the role of DMT1." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram provides a visual representation of the pancreas, with distinct sections dedicated to the exocrine and endocrine components. The exocrine portion is prominently displayed, likely showing its ductal structure and acinar cells, while the endocrine portion highlights the islets of Langerhans. Arrows and labels guide the viewer through the different parts, emphasizing the functional differences between these two key pancreatic regions." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s6> .
