<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the liver's functions and its interactions with other bodily systems, detailing the flow of substances into and out of the liver." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the lumen on the left, marked by an arrow pointing towards the center. A large blue box in the center represents the enterocyte. The extracellular fluid, or ECF, is positioned at the top right corner of the enterocyte. Within the lumen, a dark blue circle labeled \"Heme\" is connected by an arrow pointing towards the enterocyte. Inside the enterocyte, there is a label \"Porphyrin + Fe²⁺\" connected by a dashed arrow pointing to the right. A dark blue circle labeled \"Fe²⁺\" is on the right side of the enterocyte, linked by a dashed arrow from \"Porphyrin + Fe²⁺\". The label \"Ferroportin\" is within the enterocyte, connected by a dashed arrow pointing to the right. \"DMT1\" is also labeled within the enterocyte, connected by a dashed arrow pointing downwards. Another dark blue circle labeled \"Fe²⁺\" is within the enterocyte, connected by a solid arrow pointing downwards from \"DMT1\", alongside an \"H⁺\" label connected by a similar arrow." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s6> .
