<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p83_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing densely packed cells with round to oval nuclei and varying staining intensity." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-sectional view of a developing tooth. The primordium of enamel is positioned at the top right, appearing as a curved, pinkish region forming the outer layer. The oral epithelium is situated on the left, depicted as a thin, pinkish layer surrounding the developing tooth structure. The primordium of pulp is located at the bottom, shown as a darker, more central region within the tooth structure. The overall shape of the developing tooth is roughly oval, with the primordium of enamel forming the outer boundary and the primordium of pulp occupying the inner core." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
