<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p118_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/421028007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p12_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed cross-section of skin tissue with various structures labeled. At the top left, the transition zone marks the boundary between the epidermis and dermis. Small, oval-shaped sebaceous glands are situated in the upper central region of the dermis. A thin, elongated arector pili muscle is positioned in the middle left area, alongside a tubular hair follicle associated with the sebaceous gland. The lower left area features a circular orbicularis oris muscle, two distinct blood vessels labeled as an artery and a vein, small round adipose cells, a layer of oral epithelium, and small, oval-shaped mucus-secreting labial glands. In the upper right, desquamating surface cells are visible, along with the outermost epidermis layer, another sebaceous gland, an arector pili muscle, the dermis layer, a hair follicle, and a small, oval-shaped sweat gland. The lower right area mirrors the lower left with an orbicularis oris muscle and additional mucus-secreting labial glands." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/0059b1984614> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/260715004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/cd96a90fdf6c> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/60692007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/38185112741e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/38185112741e> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p18_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a cross-sectional view of the tongue, with labels positioned above the corresponding parts and connected by black lines. The epiglottis is situated at the top left, pointing towards the back of the tongue. Near the top middle, the palatine tonsil is located, pointing to the right side of the tongue. Slightly below the palatine tonsil, the lingual tonsil is positioned, pointing to the left side. The circumvallate papillae are small, round structures in the center of the tongue. Fungiform papillae are scattered across the tongue's surface, while the median sulcus runs down the center as a groove. Filiform papillae, appearing as tiny, hair-like structures, cover the entire surface, contributing to the tongue's texture." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/113279002> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p118_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two main sections, both displaying densely packed tissue. In the top section, the tissue is organized with areas labeled \"A,\" \"D,\" and \"I,\" each appearing multiple times. The bottom section mirrors this density but includes larger, lighter areas labeled \"V,\" alongside \"A\" and \"D.\" The labels are placed directly next to the corresponding areas without any connecting lines or arrows." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/da323941c7a7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#located_in> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A diagram showing a cross-section of a developing tooth, with the primordium of enamel, oral epithelium, and primordium of pulp labeled." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/da323941c7a7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s2> .
