<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized with the hypothalamus at the top, represented by a yellow box. Below it, two green boxes are placed side by side, labeled \"DA\" on the left and \"TRH\" on the right. The pituitary gland is shown as an orange oval directly beneath these two boxes. An upward arrow labeled \"+\" connects the hypothalamus to the pituitary gland. From the DA box, an arrow labeled \"-\" points to the pituitary, while an arrow labeled \"+\" extends from the TRH box to the pituitary. To the left of the pituitary, there is a green box labeled \"OESTROGENS,\" and below the pituitary, a green box labeled \"PRL\" is positioned. At the bottom of the diagram, a red box labeled \"mammary glands & other cells\" is present, with an arrow labeled \"+\" pointing from the PRL box to it. On the far right, a small black square with a minus sign indicates a negative feedback loop connected to the pituitary gland." <urn:graph:endocrine/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/1ae2aeb8a63c> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:endocrine/s8> .
