<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p51_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the hypothalamus at the top left, depicted as a red diamond shape. Below it, the anterior pituitary is shown as another red diamond. Near the hypothalamus, a blue square represents GnRH, with an arrow indicating its release from the hypothalamus. The anterior pituitary releases FSH and LH, each represented by purple squares with arrows pointing from the anterior pituitary. The testes are centrally positioned as a large oval, containing smaller shapes for Sertoli and Leydig cells, spermatogonia, and spermatocytes. Sertoli cells are connected by arrows to a blue square for the second messenger. Leydig cells are linked by an arrow to the production of Testosterone, shown as a purple square near the testes. Inhibin is also a purple square, with an arrow indicating its production from the testes." <urn:graph:endocrine/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/62583b479b35> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:endocrine/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/ab92ac46b112> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/6383> <urn:graph:endocrine/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is structured into three main sections. The first section focuses on follicular development, where small, round follicles are depicted becoming increasingly complex from day 0 to day 14. The third section illustrates the endometrial cycle, showing the endometrium as a layer of tissue with folds and crevices that thickens until day 14 and then thins out. The bottom axis is labeled with \"days of menstrual cycle\" ranging from 0 to 28 days, and the top is divided into the follicular and luteal phases, with key events like menstruation and ovulation marked. The source of the image is credited to Encyclopædia Britannica, Inc., dated 2013." <urn:graph:endocrine/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/14235f01cc41> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/227518> <urn:graph:endocrine/s8> .
