<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p65_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a side-by-side comparison, with the normal function of the pituitary gland and kidneys on one side and the condition of Central Diabetes Insipidus on the other. The normal side likely features diagrams of the pituitary gland and kidneys, possibly with labels or arrows indicating their typical roles. Visual elements such as arrows, labels, or distinct sections might be used to differentiate between the normal and affected states." <urn:graph:endocrine/s8> .
