<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a detailed view of the male perineal region, with the transverse perineal muscles positioned at the base of the penis, extending horizontally across the perineum. The crus of the penis is depicted as two curved structures on either side of the urethra, forming the main body of the penis. The corpus spongiosum is shown as an elongated structure running below the urethra. Color-coded regions are displayed: the deep perineal pouch in purple, situated between the deep perineal fascia and the perineal membrane; the perineal membrane in red, separating the superficial perineal pouch from the deep perineal pouch; the superficial perineal pouch in yellow, lying above the perineal membrane; the deep perineal fascia in green, beneath the deep perineal pouch; and the superficial perineal fascia in blue, beneath the superficial perineal pouch. A legend in the top-right corner explains the color-coding, and arrows point to specific structures with labels placed nearby. The layout is a cross-sectional view of the perineal region, with the urethra centrally positioned and surrounding structures labeled accordingly." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p7_b6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p7_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents two distinct views of the human sacrum. On the left, there is an anterior view, which shows the front side of the sacrum. On the right, a posterior view is displayed, illustrating the back side of the sacrum." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s3> .
