<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a detailed cross-sectional view of the male perineal region. The crus of the penis is illustrated as two curved structures on either side of the urethra, forming the main body of the penis. The corpus spongiosum is depicted as an elongated structure running along the length of the urethra, situated below it. The urethra is shown as a central tube running through the corpus spongiosum and the crus of the penis. Color-coded regions are included: the deep perineal pouch is in purple, located between the deep perineal fascia and the perineal membrane; the perineal membrane is in red, a thin layer separating the superficial perineal pouch from the deep perineal pouch; the superficial perineal pouch is in yellow, situated above the perineal membrane; the deep perineal fascia is in green, beneath the deep perineal pouch; and the superficial perineal fascia is in blue, beneath the superficial perineal pouch. A legend explaining the color-coding is placed in the top-right corner of the diagram. Arrows point to specific structures, with text placed near these structures for clarity." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the upper portion of a human femur, focusing on the hip joint area." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s3> .
