<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1b17fe2695c8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/280211001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the internal laryngeal nerve at the top, shown in light pink, directing attention to the upper part of the larynx. Below it, the glossopharyngeal nerve is positioned in yellow, pointing towards the middle section. An overlapping nerve supply area spans the lower part of the larynx, divided into pink and blue sections. On the left side of this overlap, the lingual nerve is colored pink, while on the right, the chorda tympani is in blue. Arrows and lines connect these labels to the corresponding regions of the larynx, which is presented in a cross-sectional view with different colors indicating the presence of various nerves." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/59820001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1b17fe2695c8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/d19df716f989> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/27612005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/56052001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p18_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a side view of the head, showing the front and part of the side. Muscles are displayed in shades of pink and orange, with intricate patterns indicating their texture and layering. Nerves are represented by yellow lines branching out from a central point near the ear, extending towards various parts of the face and head. The ear is partially visible, with the outer ear and part of the inner ear structure shown. The overall layout emphasizes the relationship between the muscles and the nerves, illustrating their complex network within the head." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/1284836000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a detailed anatomical view of the head and neck, highlighting muscles, blood vessels, and nerves." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/b8e867f0b134> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/27612005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/37b8754722d8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p18_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a side view of the head with the left side facing forward. Different nerves are represented by colored lines: purple, orange, yellow, green, blue, and red. The purple nerve originates from the brainstem and branches into the forehead area. The orange nerve extends from the brainstem and branches into the cheek and jaw area. The yellow nerve starts near the ear and travels down to the lower jaw. The green nerve runs along the side of the face, branching into the cheek and mouth area. The blue nerve extends from the brainstem and branches into the lower jaw and neck area. The red nerve originates from the brainstem and branches into the neck area. The text \"Temp\" is located at the top right corner, pointing to the purple nerve, while \"From\" is written below it, indicating the origin of the purple nerve. At the bottom right, the text \"Cerv\" points to the red nerve, followed by \"Pla,\" likely standing for \"Plateau.\" The diagram also shows various muscles and structures of the head and neck, including the eye socket, cheekbones, and jaw." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/618a7f20ab64> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/245546007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/d61af2fafae6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/27612005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the head and neck region, with muscles displayed in shades of pink and red, blood vessels in red, and nerves as thin white lines. The external structure of the ear is prominently visible on the left side. The skin and underlying tissues are rendered in green and blue shades, contrasting with the warmer colors of the muscles and blood vessels. Each structure is labeled with a number, and leader lines or arrows connect these labels to the corresponding parts, indicating their spatial relationships and distribution." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/618a7f20ab64> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/71616004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/0681c83ef228> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b23> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/244783001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/37b8754722d8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/27612005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/774007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b23> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a detailed anatomical cross-section of the pharynx, highlighting various muscles and structures such as the tensor veli palatini, auditory tube, levator veli palatini, salpingopharyngeus, superior constrictor, soft palate, palatopharyngeus, middle constrictor, mucous membrane, epiglottis, palatoglossus, and vallecula." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/211a4e478e61> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/280211001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/618a7f20ab64> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized with a series of rectangular boxes connected by straight arrows, each box containing black text on a white background. The first box, labeled \"Inferior salivatory nucleus,\" is positioned at the top-left of the image. Directly below it, centered horizontally, is the box labeled \"Tympanic branch of 9th cranial nerve.\" This pattern continues with each subsequent box: \"Tympanic plexus,\" \"Lesser petrosal nerve,\" \"Otic ganglion,\" \"Auriculotemporal nerve,\" and finally, \"Parotid gland,\" all aligned vertically in the center of the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
