<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration is divided into several color-coded areas representing different nerve distributions. Near the eye, the lacrimal nerve is labeled in the top-left region. Above the eye, the supratrochlear and supraorbital nerves are indicated in green. Below the eye, the infratrochlear nerve is labeled. In the nasal area, the nasal nerve is marked in pink, along with the afraoral nerve around the mouth and the buccal nerve in the cheek area. The mandibular area is highlighted in yellow, with the mental nerve labeled in the chin area. The temple area features the temporal branch of the temporo-malar nerve in blue, while the cheek area has the malar branch also in blue. The ear area shows the auriculo-temporal nerve in purple. Finally, the neck area indicates the superficial cervical plexus in light purple." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://snomed.info/id/27612005> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <http://snomed.info/id/25238003> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
