<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the distribution of facial nerves and their branches in the head, with different colors representing various nerve distributions." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/307013006> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b23> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the pharynx, with labels pointing to different anatomical structures. At the top left, the tensor veli palatini is indicated near the auditory tube, which is shown just below it. The levator veli palatini is labeled on the right side, near the soft palate. The salpingopharyngeus muscle is positioned in the middle, running horizontally across the pharynx, followed by the superior constrictor below it. The soft palate is depicted below the superior constrictor, appearing as a fleshy, horizontal structure. The palatopharyngeus is shown below the soft palate, with the middle constrictor beneath it. The mucous membrane is indicated below the middle constrictor, representing the inner lining of the pharynx. The epiglottis is located at the bottom right, appearing as a leaf-shaped structure. The palatoglossus is labeled at the bottom left, and the vallecula is at the very bottom, shown as a small V-shaped depression between the epiglottis and the soft palate." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/d61af2fafae6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/362465002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/5fdf4dfdd3f4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/52b7f98ef4b0> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/27612005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The trigeminal nerve is positioned at the top left of the image, with an arrow pointing to its main trunk. The ophthalmic branch extends from the top center, indicated by an arrow from the main trunk. The maxillary branch is located near the middle right, with an arrow pointing downward and curving to the right from the main trunk. The mandibular branch is at the bottom left, with an arrow extending downward and curving to the right from the main trunk. The superior alveolar nerve is situated near the middle right, below the maxillary branch, with an arrow pointing downward from it. The lingual nerve is near the bottom right, with an arrow pointing downward from the mandibular branch. The inferior alveolar nerve is at the bottom center, with an arrow pointing downward from the mandibular branch. The lower teeth are depicted in light blue across the bottom, while the upper teeth are in white above them. The jawbone is shown in pink with teeth embedded, and the skull structure is visible around the top and sides, providing context for the nerves." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s5> .
