<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p24_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed anatomical illustration of the pharynx with various structures labeled and highlighted by arrows. At the top, the pharyngeal tonsil is marked by a green box and an arrow. On the right side, the choanae are labeled in a green box with arrows pointing to two red rectangular areas. The palatine tonsils are indicated in blue text on the left, with arrows pointing to two reddish structures on either side of the nasopharynx. The oropharyngeal opening is marked by a yellow circle and an arrow, situated below the choanae and above the laryngeal inlet. The laryngeal inlet is labeled in a green box on the right, with an arrow pointing to a yellow circle. The piriform recess is also labeled in a green box on the right, with an arrow pointing to the area below the laryngeal inlet. The illustration uses colors to differentiate between soft tissues and bony structures, providing a clear depiction of the nasal cavity, nasopharynx, oropharynx, and laryngopharynx." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/a44a1d509865> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/405737000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
