<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p20_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the human oral and pharyngeal regions, with labels and leader lines pointing to specific anatomical structures. At the top left, the nasal cavity is indicated, with the upper lip positioned just above it. Below the nasal cavity lies the hard palate, followed by the soft palate. The nasopharynx is situated above the soft palate, while the uvula hangs below it. The oral cavity is positioned below the upper lip, and the tongue is centrally located within the mouth. The vestibule is found at the bottom left, and the hyoid bone is at the very bottom. The epiglottis is shown below the hyoid bone, and the oropharynx is located between the nasopharynx and the epiglottis. The laryngopharynx is positioned at the bottom right." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
