<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/75573002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p19_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the human pharynx and its surrounding structures. At the top left, the nasal cavity is depicted in pink. Above it, the torus tubarius is shown as a small, rounded protrusion. Near the back of the nasal cavity, the pharyngeal tonsil appears as a small, pinkish mass. Above this recess, the torus levatorius is a raised, rounded structure. Extending from the torus levatorius is a thin, elongated structure known as the fold overlying levator veli palatini. On the side of the pharynx, the palatoglossal fold is a curved structure. The nasopharynx, shown in pink, is the uppermost part of the pharynx, located above the soft palate. The oropharynx, in orange, is the middle section between the soft palate and the epiglottis. The laryngopharynx, depicted in blue, is the lower part below the epiglottis. The palatopharyngeal arch, which overlies the palatopharyngeus muscle, is a curved structure on the side of the pharynx. At the bottom of the image, the tongue is positioned." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/55940004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/a388ce566828> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/738948007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed anatomical illustration of the posterior view of the pharynx. At the top left, the cuneiform tubercle is labeled, pointing to a small, triangular-shaped structure on the left side. Slightly below this, the corinicate tubercle is positioned, indicating another small, rounded structure. The posterior surface over the arytenoid cartilage is labeled centrally in the pharynx. The lateral wall of the piriform sinus is indicated on either side, while the medial wall is marked at the center. A prominence over the cricoid cartilage is noted near the bottom, and the esophagus is labeled at the lower part of the pharynx. The trachea is also labeled at the lowermost part where it meets the pharynx. The laryngopharynx (hypopharynx) is labeled on the right side, indicating the lower portion of the pharynx." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/0e2783a25287> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#finding_site> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/5fcc7c1968a4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
