<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/a388ce566828> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the human pharynx and surrounding structures. At the top, the pharyngeal tonsil is positioned above the choanae. Within the nasal cavity, the inferior nasal concha are curved structures. Below the mandible, the submandibular gland is situated. The root of the tongue is shown at the base, and the epiglottis, a flap of tissue, is located above the larynx. Each structure is labeled with a leader line or arrow pointing to its corresponding anatomical feature." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/cb81d7c9541d> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#finding_site> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p24_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a detailed anatomical cross-section of the pharynx, highlighting key structures such as the pharyngeal tonsil, choanae, palatine tonsils, oropharyngeal opening, laryngeal inlet, and piriform recess." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s8> .
