<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A simplified diagram of the human pelvis, highlighting the pubic symphysis and the structural layout of the bone." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/5b8259e73210> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/280608008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large, light yellow bone structure represents the pelvis, featuring a curved upper portion and a more rounded lower section. Below the pelvis, a femur is depicted in light yellow, positioned within the pelvic region. The hip joint is indicated by a blue circular shape where the femur meets the pelvis, containing a smaller green circle at its center, likely representing the femoral head. On the right side, text reading \"Illustration by Smart-Servier Medical Art\" is written vertically and connected to the image by a thin black line." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/be607428901d> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/12921003> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
