<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b17> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the human pelvis, with each structure labeled by a black line pointing directly to the corresponding part. The labels are positioned around the periphery of the image, ensuring clarity and easy reference. The sacrum is situated at the top, forming the back portion of the pelvis, while the ilium, shaped like large wings, forms the sides. The ischium is depicted at the lower part, completing the back and bottom of the pelvis. Various openings such as the greater and lesser sciatic foramina and the obturator foramen are clearly shown, indicating pathways for nerves and blood vessels. Ligaments, including the posterior sacroiliac, sacrospinous, sacrotuberous, and others, are illustrated connecting different bones, emphasizing their roles in stabilizing the pelvis. The ischiopubic ramus is shown extending towards the ischium from the pubis." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/4429da7fcd52> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
