<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p3_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The pelvis is illustrated in light yellow, with the ilium positioned at the top and the sacrum and coccyx forming the lower part. The femur is shown in a darker yellow, extending downward from the pelvis. At the center, two blue structures represent the femoral head and acetabulum, with the femoral head smaller and positioned within the larger, cup-shaped acetabulum. A small green area is visible between them, likely depicting articular cartilage. On the right side, a vertical black line runs along the edge with the text \"Illustration by Smart-Servier Medical Art\" in white, not connected to any part of the illustration." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
