<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large, curved yellow structure at the top represents the pelvic bone, with a smooth, rounded surface and a slight indentation on its upper part. Below this, a blue structure represents the femoral head, connected to the pelvic bone by a joint. The area between the blue femoral head and the yellow pelvic bone is green, suggesting cartilage or ligaments. On the right side, vertical black text reads: \"Illustration by Smart-Servier Medical Art.\"" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
