<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The pelvis is depicted in a light yellow color, with a darker blue area at the center representing the pubic symphysis. The pelvis is divided into two symmetrical halves by this central blue area, which is positioned at the bottom. The upper part of the pelvis has a curved, bowl-like shape with a hollowed-out center, while the lower part is more solid and forms a triangular base with a rounded bottom edge." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s2> .
