<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/743> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#catalyzes> <http://snomed.info/id/2331003> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a cross-section of a biological structure, with a pinkish-red outer layer at the top and bottom, appearing wavy and smooth. Red downward-pointing arrows near the top and bottom indicate movement from the outer to the inner layers, while black upward-pointing arrows in the middle suggest flow from the inner to the outer layers. The blurred background shows green and yellow hues, possibly representing the surrounding environment. The image is divided into three sections: the outer layer, the inner layers, and the background, with arrows indicating interactions between these sections." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure presents a series of cross-sectional views of a tube-like structure, divided into four distinct sections. The leftmost section displays a white, granular substance, likely blood cells, tightly packed together. Moving to the second section from the left, a greenish, more fluid substance is shown, possibly representing plasma. The third section from the left contains a yellowish substance with a granular texture, resembling fat cells. Finally, the rightmost section has light brown, granular content, suggesting another type of cell or tissue. Each section is separated by a darker, wavy boundary, representing the walls of the tube. Black arrows with triangular heads are present in each section, pointing towards the center of the tube, indicating flow or movement. Additionally, red arrows point downwards at the top of each section, possibly indicating pressure or force acting on the contents." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/a7131a94b968> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into two main sections. In the top section, there is a graph with the vertical axis labeled \"Membrane potential (mV)\" and the horizontal axis labeled \"Time.\" The graph displays two types of waves: \"Slow wave\" appears as small, rounded peaks, while \"Action potential\" is represented by larger, sharper peaks surpassing a dashed horizontal line labeled \"Threshold.\" A red box highlights the area where action potentials occur above the threshold, accompanied by the text: \"Action potentials fire when slow wave potentials exceed threshold.\" The bottom section features a second graph with the vertical axis labeled \"Force of muscle contraction\" and the horizontal axis labeled \"Time.\" This graph shows fluctuations in force over time corresponding to the action potentials above the threshold. A blue box in this section states: \"The force and duration of muscle contraction are directly related to the amplitude and frequency of action potentials.\"" <urn:graph:digestive_system/s3> .
