<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p7_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into three sections, each labeled with a different type of muscle contraction. At the top, the \"Phasic Contractions\" section features a graph with sharp, brief peaks separated by flat lines. In the middle, the \"Tonic Contractions\" section displays a smooth, continuous curve that remains above a baseline. At the bottom, the \"Tonic + Phasic Contractions\" section combines elements from both previous graphs, showing both sharp peaks and a sustained curve. Each graph has a dashed horizontal line serving as a baseline reference. The labels for each contraction type are written in black text above their respective graphs. The website \"BasicPhysiology.org\" is mentioned in the bottom right corner." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s3> .
