<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p58_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a side view of the head and neck, with the parotid gland situated at the top-left near the ear, the lacrimal gland positioned above the eye slightly to the right, and the submandibular gland located at the bottom-right below the chin. An arrow points to the parotid gland from the left, another to the lacrimal gland from the top-right, and a third to the submandibular gland from the right. The posterior sulcus label is on the left, indicating the area behind the ear and neck. Arrows in the diagram show the flow of fluid from the glands to various regions of the face and neck, delineating the drainage paths." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s8> .
