<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the oral cavity, with labels pointing to different anatomical structures. At the top, the superior lip is indicated, followed by the gingivae just below it. Near the center-top, the superior labial frenulum is marked, and slightly below that, the palatine raphe is shown. The hard palate is positioned above the teeth, while the soft palate is below it, with the uvula hanging at the back. On either side of the uvula, the palatine tonsils are labeled. At the bottom of the tongue, the sublingual gland is indicated, and near the bottom of the image, the duct of the submandibular gland is shown. Near the center-bottom, the plica fimbriata, deep lingual vein, and lingual frenulum are all labeled." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/2d46c4f4b2bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s8> .
