<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a detailed depiction of the submandibular region, with the parotid gland shown as a large, lobulated structure in light pink near the ear, positioned above the parotid duct. The submandibular gland appears as a smaller, compact structure in light pink below the mandible, while the sublingual gland is a small, rounded structure situated beneath the tongue, close to the submandibular gland. The opening of the submandibular (Wharton's) duct is a small depiction on the floor of the mouth, indicating where the duct exits into the mouth. The body of the mandible is a curved, bony structure forming the bottom boundary of the mouth. Leader lines connect labels to the corresponding anatomical structures, with labels placed around the periphery of the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s8> .
