<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p65_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a side view of the head and neck region, with the ear positioned on the left side and the nose and mouth at the top right. The parotid gland is placed behind the masseter muscle, with the submandibular gland below the tongue and the sublingual gland under the tongue. The anterior facial vein is depicted as a blue line running from the lower jaw towards the neck, while the lingual artery is shown as a red line extending from the neck towards the tongue. The zygomatic arch is positioned above the masseter muscle, and the accessory part of the parotid gland is near the main body of the parotid gland. Each structure is labeled with a leader line connecting it to the corresponding part in the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s8> .
<http://snomed.info/id/75535001> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#composed_of> <http://snomed.info/id/45289007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p53_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The parotid gland is shown as a large, pinkish, lobulated structure near the ear, positioned above the submandibular gland. The submandibular gland appears as a smaller, pinkish, lobulated structure located below the parotid gland and slightly behind the lower jaw. The sublingual gland is depicted as a small, pinkish, lobulated structure beneath the tongue. The image includes a skeletal outline of the skull and neck, providing context for the location of the glands. The glands are illustrated in a simplified, anatomical style, emphasizing their relative positions and shapes." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s8> .
