<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p12_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features the hypothalamus at the top, labeled in red text, with a green arrow labeled 'Thyrotropin-releasing hormone (TRH)' pointing downward to the anterior pituitary gland, also labeled in red text. From the anterior pituitary gland, a red arrow labeled 'Thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH)' points to the thyroid gland, depicted as a pinkish structure at the base of the neck. The thyroid gland has a blue arrow labeled 'Thyroid hormones (T3 and T4)' extending downward, followed by blue arrows labeled 'Increased metabolism', 'Growth and development', and 'Increased catecholamine effect'. A blue arrow labeled 'Negative feedback' points back from the thyroid gland to the hypothalamus, completing the feedback loop." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the vascular and neural structures in the neck region, including the external and internal carotid arteries, various thyroid-related vessels, and key nerves such as the vagus nerve and right recurrent laryngeal nerve." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s8> .
