<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a detailed anatomical illustration of the neck region, with the hyoid bone positioned at the top of the image in the upper central region. The thyroid cartilage is centrally located near the middle of the image and is highlighted with a yellow box. The omohyoid muscle (superior belly) and the sternohyoid muscle are both labeled on the left side of the image. The median cricothyroid ligament is highlighted with a purple box at the center, while the cricoid cartilage is highlighted with a cyan box also at the center. The trachea is highlighted with a green box at the bottom center of the image. The trapezius muscle is located at the bottom left corner, and the omohyoid muscle (inferior belly) points to the bottom left. The stylohyoid muscle, digastric muscle (anterior belly), mylohyoid muscle, and hyoglossus muscle are all labeled on the right side of the image. The digastric muscle (posterior belly) and the fibrous loop for the intermediate digastric tendon are also on the right. The sternothyroid muscle and cricothyroid muscle are positioned on the right side as well. The oblique line of the thyroid cartilage is also labeled on the right side of the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/52082005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s8> .
