<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into three sections. In the top-left, a photograph of a person's neck area is displayed, with the individual having short hair and wearing a light-colored shirt. The thyroid gland is highlighted by a red circle. At the center, there is a detailed anatomical diagram of the thyroid gland and surrounding structures, with labels such as thyroid cartilage, thyrohyoid muscle, common carotid artery, superior thyroid vessels, left and right lobes of the thyroid gland, isthmus, trachea, inferior thyroid artery, and inferior thyroid veins. Arrows connect these labels to their corresponding parts in the diagram. On the right, a close-up anatomical photograph shows the thyroid gland and surrounding tissues, providing a realistic view of the gland's texture and position within the neck." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s8> .
