<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a pink thyroid gland positioned below the larynx, with a blue trachea running vertically through the center. The superior thyroid artery is depicted as a red vessel branching off from the common carotid artery, accompanied by the superior laryngeal nerve, shown as a yellowish nerve. The internal and external laryngeal nerves are also yellowish and are shown running within and on the surface of the larynx, respectively. The right and left vagus nerves, depicted as yellowish nerves, run alongside the trachea. The inferior thyroid artery is a red vessel branching off from the subclavian artery. The right and left recurrent laryngeal nerves are yellowish and are shown looping around the trachea." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s8> .
