<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is split into two sections by a vertical line, with the top section featuring a curved pink structure labeled \"inner enamel epithelium\" and the bottom section showing a darker blue structure labeled \"dental papilla,\" which has a lighter blue band running through it. The \"inner enamel epithelium\" text is positioned at the top left corner and connects to the pink structure via a leader line, while the \"dental papilla\" text is at the bottom left corner, pointing to the blue structure with another leader line. The inner enamel epithelium is situated above the dental papilla, depicting a side profile of the developing tooth." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
