<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/9b703a0cc4bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/5aec01ed611e> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/26671000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure shows a detailed cross-sectional diagram of a tooth, including the crown and root portions with various labeled structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p47_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a vertical cross-section of a tooth, with the crown at the top and the apex at the bottom, giving the tooth a conical shape. The labels are strategically placed to point to their corresponding parts. Enamel is at the top, followed by the dentinoenamel junction and dentin." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/9b703a0cc4bc> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a detailed cross-section of a tooth, with the crown portion featuring a thin layer of enamel at the top and a thicker striped layer of dentin beneath it. The root section displays odontoblasts lining the dentin, a lighter-colored pulp near the center, and a hollow red root canal. The root extends into the jawbone, surrounded by yellowish-brown alveolar bone, with a darker periodontal ligament between the bone and the yellowish-brown cementum. Above the bone is light pink gingiva. A small red circle marks the apical foramen at the root tip. Arrows and circles highlight specific areas: a black circle on the crown, a red arrow pointing to the pulp, and a blue arrow indicating the alveolar bone. Each part is labeled with text connected by leader lines." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/9b703a0cc4bc> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p46_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a symmetrical object with a pointed tip at the bottom and a broader end at the top. At the top left, an arrow labeled \"E\" points to the outermost layer. Near the center, an arrow labeled \"P\" indicates a darker, central region. On the right side, an arrow labeled \"D\" points to another darker area within the structure." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p51_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a detailed view of a tooth, with leader lines extending from labeled parts to specific areas. The tooth's crown is visible above the gum line, with enamel forming the outermost layer. At the center, the dental pulp is situated within the pulp cavity, surrounded by dentin. The gingiva, a pink tissue, surrounds the base of the tooth. To the right side of the image, a cartoon unicorn character, wearing a white coat and stethoscope, is smiling near the bottom right corner, unconnected to the anatomical diagram." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/129143008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/260521003> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a cross-sectional view of a developing tooth, highlighting the inner enamel epithelium and the dental papilla." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
