<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/84540008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-sectional view of a tooth, with the enamel forming the outermost layer at the top. The crown, the visible part of the tooth above the gum line, is predominantly composed of dentin, a pinkish layer beneath the enamel. The dental pulp, shown in a darker pink, resides within the pulp cavity at the tooth's center. Surrounding the base of the tooth is the gingiva, depicted as pink tissue. The root canal, a hollow space within the root, is visible, along with the cementum, a yellowish-brown layer covering the root. The dental alveolus, the socket in the jawbone that holds the tooth, is also illustrated. Leader lines with black text label each component, providing clear identification." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/5aec01ed611e> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
