<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/a3b25aed77e0> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/4421005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is split into two main sections. On the left, the vermilion border is at the top, with accessory salivary glands positioned in the middle and the gingiva below them. Dark brown lines represent skeletal muscle extending downward from the gingiva, while hair-bearing skin is at the bottom, featuring darker, hair-like structures. The labial sulcus is a curved line below the gingiva, and the body of the mandible is a large, irregular shape at the bottom left. On the right, the tooth structure is shown with enamel as a white layer at the top, dentine as a gray layer beneath, and the pulp chamber as a red area within the dentine. The gingival crevice is a small gap between the tooth and gum, and the periodontal membrane is a thin, orange layer around the tooth base. The root canal is a narrow channel through the root, with cementum as a light brown layer on the outer root surface. The apical foramen is a small opening at the root tip, and the genioglossus muscle is a dark brown structure at the bottom right. Black labels accompany each part, and the layout presents a cross-sectional view." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/d13721c7b3c3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#composed_of> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
