<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p47_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p51_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed anatomical diagram of a tooth, including its internal and external structures, with labels and a cartoon unicorn character." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two main sections. On the left, there's a detailed cross-sectional diagram of a tooth with labels pointing to different parts. The \"Alveolar bone\" label is on the left side, indicating the outermost layer of the bone. The \"Periodontal ligament\" label is in the middle, showing the area between the alveolar bone and the cementum. The \"Cementum\" label is on the right, pointing to the layer covering the tooth's root, while \"Sharpeys Fibers\" is at the bottom, indicating fibers connecting the cementum to the alveolar bone. On the right, a simplified diagram of a tooth shows a white outer surface and a darker inner core. A small rectangular box is drawn over the cross-section, likely highlighting a specific area, corresponding to the \"Periodontal ligament\" and \"Cementum\" regions in the left diagram." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
