<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/52082005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p53_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/07410f30ecc7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/26671000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into three distinct sections. At the top, there's a detailed diagram of tooth enamel and dentin, with labels pointing to the dentinoenamel junction, interglobular spaces, dentin tubules, dentin matrix, enamel, enamel tufts, and enamel rods. In the middle, a microscopic image displays a tooth cross-section, with arrows labeled \"E\" and \"D\" indicating specific areas within the dentin, showing its texture with distinct layers and patterns. On the bottom right, an animated unicorn character, resembling a doctor, stands upright with a cheerful expression, wearing a white coat, an orange tie, and a stethoscope." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p46_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/255292000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed anatomical diagram of a tooth, illustrating its various internal and external components." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure consists of three labeled diagrams arranged vertically. The top left diagram, labeled \"C,\" shows a cross-section of a developing tooth with labels for the stratum intermedium, stellate reticulum, and dental papilla. The top right diagram, labeled \"D,\" also presents a cross-section, highlighting the inner enamel epithelium, outer enamel epithelium, enamel, dentin, and bone. The bottom center diagram, labeled \"H,\" provides a more detailed view, including labels for ameloblasts, enamel, dentin, odontoblasts, outer enamel epithelium, stellate reticulum, and dental papilla. Each diagram uses leader lines to connect labels to the corresponding structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/80541002> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-section of a tooth, with distinct layers and structures clearly marked. At the top, the outermost layer is labeled as Enamel. Below this, the Dentinoenamel junction marks the transition to the Dentin layer. Within the Dentin, small gaps are labeled as Interglobular spaces. The central space within the tooth is labeled as the Pulp cavity. Fine lines in the Enamel are labeled as Lines of Retzius and Lines of Schreger, both pointing towards the center. Small, tuft-like structures in the Enamel are labeled as Enamel tufts. A channel extending from the Pulp cavity into the root is labeled as the Root canal. Near the Cementum, a granular texture is labeled as the Granular layer (of Tomes). At the tip of the root canal, an opening is labeled as the Apical foramen. Each label is connected to its corresponding area on the diagram by leader lines or arrows." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a detailed cross-section of a tooth, with labels pointing to different parts. Enamel is positioned at the top, forming the outermost layer. Dentin, the main body of the tooth, is shown with concentric layers, and interglobular spaces are visible within it. Lines of Retzius and Schreger are depicted in the enamel and dentin, respectively. Leader lines connect each label to its corresponding part, with labels placed around the periphery of the image." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/63d0e1e8f018> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/113279002> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p53_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is composed of six labeled diagrams arranged in two rows. Diagram a is in the top-left corner, showing a cross-section of a developing tooth with labels for \"oral epithelium,\" \"primordium of enamel,\" and \"primordium of pulp.\" Diagram b is in the top-center, displaying a more developed tooth with \"inner enamel epithelium\" and \"dental papilla\" labeled. Diagram c is in the top-right, featuring additional layers with labels for \"stratum intermedium,\" \"stellate reticulum,\" \"inner enamel epithelium,\" \"outer enamel epithelium,\" and \"dental papilla.\" Diagram d is in the bottom-right, depicting a more mature tooth with \"enamel,\" \"dentin,\" \"bone,\" \"dental pulp,\" and \"vessels and nerves\" labeled. Diagram e is in the bottom-center, showing a cross-section with \"oral epithelium,\" \"odontoblastic layer,\" and \"periodontal ligament\" labeled. Diagram f is also in the bottom-right, illustrating a fully developed tooth with \"enamel,\" \"dentin,\" \"gingiva,\" \"dental pulp,\" \"bone,\" and \"vessels and nerves\" labeled." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/5aec01ed611e> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/181769001> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/5aec01ed611e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/84540008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/61415007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is oriented vertically, with the crown positioned at the top and the root at the bottom. The outermost layer of the crown is marked as enamel, with lines of Retzius visible within it. Beneath the enamel, dentin is shown with its dentinal tubules and interglobular spaces. The clinical crown is labeled on the left side, showing the portion of the tooth visible above the gum line, while the anatomic crown extends from the clinical crown down to the cementoenamel junction. In the root region, the gingival sulcus is depicted as the space between the tooth and the gums, with the epithelium of the gingiva covering the gum tissue. The cementoenamel junction marks where the enamel meets the dentin, and the epithelial attachment shows how the epithelium connects to the tooth. Fibers of the periodontal membrane are shown, anchoring the tooth, while noncellular cementum forms the outer layer of the root." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed cross-sectional diagram of a tooth, labeled with various anatomical features." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/9b703a0cc4bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/113279002> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/fa84ae7bf12e> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#located_in> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s4> .
