<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/36451009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the mouth, with the superior lip positioned at the top, followed by the superior labial frenulum just below it. The gingivae are labeled on both sides, framing the teeth. Near the center-top, the palatine raphe is shown, while the hard palate is situated above the teeth. The soft palate is positioned below the hard palate, with the uvula hanging at the back. On either side of the uvula, the palatine tonsils are visible. Behind the soft palate, the posterior wall of the oropharynx is depicted. The tongue is centrally located, and the lingual frenulum is at the bottom-center. The duct of the submandibular gland is on the left side, while the vestibule is at the very bottom. The inferior labial frenulum is located at the bottom, completing the detailed layout of the oral cavity." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/9a3b46d48292> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.8"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p51_b12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://snomed.info/id/75573002> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#associated_with> <http://snomed.info/id/90176007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomical structures of the human throat and upper respiratory tract, including the uvula, soft palate, palatoglossal arch, palatine tonsils, hard palate, oral cavity, tongue, lingual tonsils, oropharynx, epiglottis, laryngopharynx, hyoid bone, esophagus, and trachea." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/74262004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/28777000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed cross-section of the human throat and mouth, with the oral part situated at the top right, displaying the upper mouth area including teeth and gums. The teeth are depicted with white enamel, and the gums are pink, while the roof of the mouth is shown as a curved structure above the teeth. The tip of the tongue is labeled at the frontmost part within the oral section. Below this, the pharyngeal part extends into the throat, featuring the soft palate, uvula, and the back wall of the throat. The pharynx is portrayed as a tube-like structure connecting the oral cavity to the larynx and esophagus, with the base labeled at the lowermost part near the neck. The spinal column is partially visible on the left side, with vertebrae stacked vertically. Various tissues and muscles are differentiated by shading in different colors, including skin tones, pink for mucous membranes, and yellow for bone structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/40880001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the oral cavity, with the hard palate positioned at the upper right, featuring the incisive papilla near the central incisors and transverse folds running horizontally across it. Beneath the mucosa of the hard palate, palatine glands are depicted as small clusters, with mouths of ducts visible on the hard palate. The soft palate, located behind the hard palate, is shown as a flexible, muscular structure, with the uvula hanging down from its back. The mandible is illustrated on the left side, with the parotid gland situated below it, near the jaw's angle. The palatoglossus muscle extends from the soft palate to the tongue in the lower middle part of the image. All structures are labeled with lines or arrows pointing to their respective anatomical locations." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/123851003> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
