<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the oral cavity, with the hard palate displayed in pink and the soft palate in a lighter shade. The incisive papilla is positioned at the front of the hard palate, near the central incisors, while transverse folds extend horizontally across the middle of the hard palate. The soft palate is shown in a lighter pink, and the palatoglossal arch is a fold of tissue separating the soft palate from the base of the tongue. The palatine tonsil, a darker pink lymphoid tissue mass, is located in the posterior part of the mouth. The mandible and parotid gland are both depicted in light yellow, with the parotid gland situated below the mandible. Leader lines with arrows point to specific anatomical parts, and labels are written in black text next to these lines." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
