<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed cross-section of the tongue, with various muscle fibers indicated by arrows. The longitudinal muscle fibers are shown at the top right, pointing towards the central part of the tongue. Transverse fibers are positioned near the top left, indicating the horizontal direction across the middle of the tongue. Vertical fibers are also near the top left, pointing towards the base of the tongue. The genioglossus muscle is located at the bottom left, while the geniohyoid is at the bottom right. The tongue's muscular structure is depicted with texture, and the surrounding areas, including the gums and inside of the cheeks, are shaded in yellow. Muscles are colored in shades of red and orange, emphasizing their fibrous nature, with the tongue centrally placed within the oral cavity." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/bece64cc0ab6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
