<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/72914001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p47_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "An open mouth is displayed with the tongue extended, showing a slightly pinkish-red color with darker areas. The teeth are visible at the top and bottom of the image. The focus is entirely on the mouth and tongue, with no labels, text, or additional markings present." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The lingual artery and vein are positioned at the top-left, represented by intertwined red lines with a red arrow pointing downward from the label. Near the top-center, the dorsal lingual artery and vein are similarly depicted as intertwined red lines, also with a downward-pointing red arrow. At the bottom-left, the hypoglossal nerve is shown as a yellowish line running horizontally across the lower part of the image, with a red arrow pointing upward from the label. The deep lingual vein is located at the bottom-right, shown as a blue line extending from the bottom right towards the center, with a red arrow pointing upward from the label." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a cross-sectional view of the human throat and mouth, highlighting the oral and pharyngeal parts along with the surrounding anatomical structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/ef56b0c7503e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/70925003> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/75573002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration is a detailed cross-sectional view of the human throat and upper respiratory tract, with various anatomical structures labeled and connected by leader lines. The uvula is positioned at the top, hanging from the soft palate, which is just below it. The hard palate is above the oral cavity, with the tongue situated within the oral cavity. The epiglottis is at the top of the laryngopharynx, and the laryngopharynx connects the pharynx to the larynx. The hyoid bone is positioned below the laryngopharynx, and the esophagus is below the hyoid bone, while the trachea is situated below the esophagus. The diagram uses colors to differentiate tissues and organs, with reds for muscles and other structures in shades of yellow and orange." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s7> .
