<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is composed of blue rectangular boxes connected by arrows. The first box is positioned at the top left corner and reads \"Allergic or auto-immune diseases,\" with an arrow pointing to the right. Directly below this is a box labeled \"Water Absorption disrupted,\" which has an arrow pointing downward. The third box, located below the second, reads \"Unabsorbed osmotically active solute that hold water in lumen (undigested lactose and sorbitol, a sugar alcohol from plants)\" and has an arrow pointing to the right. The fourth box, directly below the third, reads \"Diarrhea\" and has an arrow pointing upward to the second box. On the left side, below the fourth box, is a box labeled \"Bacterial toxin occurred,\" with an arrow pointing to the right. Directly below this is a box reading \"Enhance colonic Cl- & fluid secretion,\" with an arrow pointing downward. The seventh box, located on the left side below the sixth, reads \"Psychogenic diarrhea,\" with an arrow pointing to the right. Directly below this is a box labeled \"Stimulation of parasympathetic nervous system ↑↑,\" with an arrow pointing to the right. Finally, the ninth box, directly below the eighth, reads \"Motility & secretion of mucus ↑↑\" and has an arrow pointing upward to the fourth box." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s10> .
