<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is composed of several blue rectangular boxes connected by arrows, indicating the sequence of events. The first box is positioned at the top left, describing various stimuli from the body. Below this, the third box mentions the vomiting center located in the area postrema of the brain stem. The fourth box, to the right of the third, describes the efferent signal involving nerves V, VII, IX, and XII. The fifth box, positioned below the fourth, explains the wave of reverse peristalsis and abdominal contraction. The sixth box, directly below the fifth, indicates an increase in abdominal pressure. To the left of the sixth box, the seventh box states that the stomach relaxes. Below the seventh box, the eighth box notes that pressure forces in the gastric area increase. The ninth box, situated below the eighth, describes the intestinal content moving back into the esophagus. Finally, the tenth box, to the left of the ninth, concludes with vomiting. Arrows connect these boxes, guiding the reader through the vomiting process." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s10> .
