<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p66_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration is divided into two parts: a small inset image at the top-left and a larger main illustration at the bottom-right. The inset shows a simplified drawing of a human head and neck from behind, with the thyroid gland highlighted in red on the back of the neck. The main illustration provides a detailed anatomical view of the neck and upper thoracic area from the back. The thyroid gland is depicted as two large, symmetrical, pinkish structures located on either side of the trachea. The esophagus is a tube-like structure running vertically through the middle of the neck, slightly to the left of the trachea. The muscles of the neck are shown in a reddish-pink color, forming a layered structure around the trachea and esophagus. Labels in the illustration include \"Thyroid gland\" above the thyroid gland, \"Parathyroid glands\" above the small structures on the thyroid, \"Esophagus\" above the esophagus, \"Trachea\" above the cylindrical structure, and \"Posterior view\" at the bottom right corner." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s6> .
