<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p69_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with a central area labeled \"AC,\" which is lighter in color and surrounded by darker-staining cells. Below the \"AC\" label, the \"oxyphil\" region spans across a larger area, appearing more densely packed with nuclei and less cytoplasmic material. On either side of the \"oxyphil\" region, the \"principal\" label points to areas with a more uniform appearance and a higher concentration of darker nuclei. On the left side, the \"Cap\" label marks a circular, lighter-colored area, likely a capillary, while on the right, the \"BV\" label indicates another circular, lighter area, representing a blood vessel. The overall layout divides the image into sections by the \"oxyphil\" region, with \"principal\" regions on either side, and \"Cap\" and \"BV\" positioned at the edges." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s6> .
