<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/7ee9b326e732> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/1427222> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p72_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a histological section of thyroid tissue with various labeled structures. At the top left, follicles with colloid are visible as spherical structures filled with a pale-staining substance. In the middle left, connective tissue trabecular forms a network of fibrous tissue. The lower central region features chief cells with larger, more basophilic nuclei, while capillaries, indicated by red staining, extend from this area into the right side. Oxyphil cells, with smaller, denser nuclei, are positioned in the lower left corner among the chief cells. The thyroid gland occupies the upper half of the image, consisting of multiple follicles with colloid and surrounded by connective tissue. On the right side, extending from the middle to the bottom, is connective tissue providing support to the glandular structures. In the lower right corner, the parathyroid gland is a distinct cluster of cells with round nuclei." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/27d2a3fe3bcb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s6> .
