<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the larynx and trachea, with the epiglottis positioned at the top. Below it, the hyoid bone is depicted, followed by the thyroid cartilage, which is shown as the largest cartilage in the larynx. The laryngeal prominence, or Adam's apple, is visible as a protrusion of the thyroid cartilage. The cricothyroid ligament is situated below the thyroid cartilage, with the cricoid cartilage beneath it. The cricotracheal ligament connects the cricoid cartilage to the trachea, which is represented by a series of stacked, C-shaped tracheal rings. The colors in the illustration differentiate between tissues and cartilages, with the tracheal rings in light blue, the larynx structures in darker blue, and the ligaments in pink." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s4> .
