<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure provides a detailed anatomical view of the larynx and related structures, including the thyroid cartilage, epiglottis, vocal folds, and cricoid cartilage." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a close-up view of the larynx with a black background, making the structures stand out clearly. The superior horn of the thyroid cartilage is positioned at the upper left portion of the thyroid cartilage, while the main body of the thyroid cartilage is the larger, more robust part of the larynx. The cricoid cartilage is a ring-shaped structure located below the thyroid cartilage. The inferior horn of the thyroid cartilage is at the lower part of the thyroid cartilage, while the corniculate cartilage is near the arytenoid cartilage." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s4> .
