<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/9a5eb60ebaff> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/3716002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a central white cylindrical tube representing the trachea, surrounded by blood vessels and nerves. At the top, a yellow nerve bundle labeled \"Superior laryngeal nerve\" points to the superior aspect of the larynx. On the left side of the trachea, the \"Left vagus nerve (CN X)\" is positioned and labeled, while on the right side, the \"Right vagus nerve (CN X)\" is similarly placed. Below the trachea, the \"Right recurrent laryngeal nerve\" is positioned on the right and the \"Left recurrent laryngeal nerve\" on the left, both pointing towards the respective sides of the trachea. The esophagus is depicted as a red tubular structure located below the trachea. The labels are connected to their respective structures with leader lines, and the color scheme uses red for blood vessels, yellow for nerves, and white for the trachea and esophagus." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p3_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#figureRef> "c013" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/44567001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s4> .
