<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p19_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features the external oblique muscle on the outer side of the abdomen, depicted in orange on both sides of the body. The rectus abdominis muscle is centrally located, shown in a lighter blue, and divided into segments by a white tendinous intersection. Behind the rectus abdominis, the posterior wall of the rectus sheath is light blue. The internal oblique muscle is positioned on the inner side of the abdomen, also in orange, with the arcuate line, a curved light blue line, at its lower border. Below the internal oblique muscle lies the transversalis fascia, shown in green. The pyramidalis muscle, in darker blue, is situated at the base of the rectus abdominis. The skeletal structures of the pelvis and ribcage are depicted in light gray, providing context for the muscle placement. Leader lines connect labels to the corresponding anatomical parts." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s3> .
