<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The external oblique muscle is positioned on the outer side of the abdomen and is depicted in orange, with its fibers running diagonally from the lower ribs to the upper pelvis. Beneath it, the internal oblique muscle is shown in a darker red, with fibers running diagonally in the opposite direction. The aponeurosis of the external oblique is rendered in a lighter shade of red, while the linea alba appears as a vertical white line running centrally down the abdomen. The anterior superior iliac spine is marked with a label, and a specific rib near the lower part of the ribcage is also labeled. The pelvic bones are visible at the bottom of the image, with the anterior superior iliac spines clearly highlighted. The rectus abdominis muscle is implied by the central white area between the external and internal oblique muscles, though not explicitly labeled." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s3> .
