<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with various labeled regions. Near the upper central part, the label 'SD' indicates a small duct-like structure surrounded by cells. The label 'A' appears twice: once near the upper left and again near the lower center, pointing to acini, which are glandular structures. In the middle of the image, 'CT' marks a region of connective tissue, which appears less densely packed compared to the surrounding tissue. The nuclei of the cells are stained purple, while the cytoplasm and extracellular matrix have different shades of pink." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
