<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p110_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with a layered structure typical of mucosal tissues. At the top left, the label 'LP' points to the upper portion of the tissue, indicating the lamina propria. Centrally, the label 'M' points downward, indicating the muscularis layer. At the bottom right, the label 'A' points upward, indicating adipose tissue. Multiple arrows guide the viewer: one near the top left points to the lamina propria, another near the center-left also points within the lamina propria, a third near the center-right points within the muscularis layer, and a fourth near the bottom right points to the adipose tissue. The coloration is characteristic of H&E staining, with nuclei appearing dark blue/purple and cytoplasm appearing pink." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p106_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a central triangular region labeled as the \"central vein\" surrounded by six hexagonal regions, with each hexagon featuring a central point labeled as \"portal canals.\"" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
