<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays several raised structures labeled as \"fungiform papillae,\" which are small, rounded projections on the surface of the tongue. The label \"fungiform papilla\" is positioned at the top of the image, with two black arrows pointing downward, directing attention to the deeper structures beneath these papillae. These papillae have a central core that extends into the underlying tissue, which appears to be composed of connective tissue and possibly some nerve fibers. The bottom portion of the image shows a layer of connective tissue, likely the lamina propria, supporting the papillae." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
