<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p58_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed microscopic cross-section of a tooth, illustrating various structures involved in tooth development." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/298225002> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1e99f5229c58> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section of the tongue, stained with H&E, focusing on the fungiform papillae." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p58_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed microscopic view of a tooth, with the oral epithelium positioned at the top left and right corners, appearing as a thin, stratified squamous layer. Deeper within the tissue, the dental lamina is visible, serving as a precursor to tooth formation. Surrounding the dental lamina is the external enamel epithelium, which plays a role in enamel formation. The hard outer layer of the tooth, the enamel, is depicted as a translucent, layered structure. At the bottom left, a dense, pinkish region represents bone tissue. The epithelial root sheath, also known as Hertwig's sheath, is visible at the bottom of the image, associated with the root of the tooth. Beneath the enamel, dentin appears as a dense, pinkish material. Another stellate reticulum is seen in the middle section, involved in the development of dentin. Blood vessels are visible within the connective tissue of the dental sac. Finally, the dental alveolus, the socket in which the tooth resides, is partially shown." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/31b1b82eba42> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/5486> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p110_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38888009> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
