<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top of the image, the dermis appears as a layer with a pinkish hue, indicating the presence of collagen fibers. Below the dermis, the corium/connective tissue has a lighter pink color, suggesting a different composition. At the bottom left, the periosteum/membrane is a darker, more granular area, with a red arrow pointing towards it. On the right side, the bone is a darker, more compact area, separated from the periosteum by a thin layer of connective tissue. The black arrow points to the bone on the right side of the image." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
