<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p16_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with distinct layers. Near the bottom, label A points to a darker, more compact area, likely the basement membrane or subepithelial layer. On the left, label B indicates a lighter, more granular area within the uppermost layer, possibly the stratum corneum. In the middle, label C highlights a region with a network of fibers or connective tissue, potentially the lamina propria. Label D is over a cluster of yellowish-brown structures in the middle layer, which might represent glands or secretory cells." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section of the tongue's surface. Filiform papillae are situated on the left side, appearing as small, conical projections. The stratified squamous epithelium covers the top of the image, transitioning in thickness from the outermost to the inner layers. Near the top right, taste buds are visible as small, oval-shaped structures within the epithelium. Below the epithelium lies the lamina propria, occupying the central and lower portions of the image and consisting of connective tissue with fibers and scattered cells. Leader lines connect each labeled structure to its corresponding location in the image, with labels placed to the left and right." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s6> .
