<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two main sections. On the left, labeled \"parathyroid gland,\" there are two horizontal bars. The first bar is labeled \"precursors\" with numbers 31, 1, and 84. Below it, another bar labeled \"pre-pro-PTH\" has the same numbers. A downward arrow points from \"pre-pro-PTH\" to \"pro-PTH,\" which also has numbers 6, 1, and 84. On the right, labeled \"plasma,\" there is a horizontal bar labeled \"intact PTH\" with numbers 1, 34, and 84. An arrow points from \"pro-PTH\" to \"intact PTH.\" Below \"intact PTH,\" a smaller bar labeled \"N-terminal fragment\" has numbers 1 and 34. The term \"active sites\" is written above an arrow pointing to the \"N-terminal fragment.\" Another arrow from \"intact PTH\" leads to \"C-terminal fragments\" and \"middle molecule fragments,\" both labeled with the number 84. The terms \"active\" and \"inactive\" are written next to these fragments, respectively." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s2> .
