<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays four sequential illustrations of a bone arranged horizontally. Each illustration shows a cross-section of the bone, with the upper portion rounded and the lower portion elongated. The first illustration on the left has a smooth upper part and a textured lower part with a honeycomb-like pattern. Moving to the second illustration, the bone appears slightly more elongated overall, with the texture in the lower part becoming more pronounced and the cells more defined. In the third illustration, the bone is further elongated, and the lower part's texture features large, irregularly shaped cells that are more distinct. Finally, the fourth illustration on the right shows the most elongated bone, with the lower part's texture being the most intricate, featuring highly defined cells. Black arrows separate each illustration, pointing to the right to indicate progression." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s6> .
