<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a cross-sectional view of a bone, likely a long bone such as the femur. The outermost layer is a light beige color, representing the compact bone, which forms a continuous shell around the entire bone. Inside this compact layer, a darker orange region indicates the spongy bone, characterized by numerous small, interconnected spaces filled with red marrow. The cross-section of the bone is circular with a central cavity, and the shape is slightly irregular, showing variations in thickness and curvature. Dark orange areas within the spongy bone represent red marrow, while lighter areas may represent yellow marrow." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s6> .
