<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The upper portion of the image displays a sectioned view of the skull, including parts of the mandible and maxilla, with teeth visible within the mandible. Below the skull, several reddish-pink muscles are depicted, likely part of the neck and jaw area. The common carotid artery is labeled with an arrow pointing to its main trunk, and it branches into the external and internal carotid arteries. The vertebral artery is labeled twice with arrows, indicating different segments, and runs alongside the spinal column, which is visible in the center-right of the image. Vertebrae are labeled, and the vertebral arteries are shown running along the spinal column. Arrows point to specific parts of the blood vessels and the spinal column, with text labels such as \"V1,\" \"V2,\" \"V3,\" \"Vertebral a.,\" \"External carotid a.,\" and \"Internal carotid a.\" placed near the corresponding blood vessels. At the bottom of the image, the left subclavian artery is indicated by a label pointing to it." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/42ccd297dd10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
