<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/0cd96c1353af> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a detailed depiction of the neck region, with labels for cranial nerves IX and X positioned at the top left, pointing to the upper cervical area. The superior cervical ganglion is highlighted near the top center, while the cervical vertebrae C1 through C8 are sequentially labeled from top to bottom, followed by the first thoracic vertebra, T1. The carotid sinus nerve is shown near the carotid artery, and the superior cardiac nerves are indicated near the heart." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/422045004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
