<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p66_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the neck, with different anatomical structures labeled. The mandible is positioned at the top left, while the facial nerve (CN VII) cervical branch is near it. The external jugular vein and the great auricular nerve are prominently displayed, along with the transverse cervical nerve and the supraclavicular nerves. The platysma muscle is shown as a superficial layer on the neck, and the anterior jugular vein is visible. The jugular venous arch completes the depiction. Muscles are colored pink, nerves are yellow, and veins are blue, with the layers of fascia distinctly highlighted." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
