<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A cross-sectional anatomical diagram of the neck region, illustrating the carotid sheath, common carotid artery, internal jugular vein, vertebrae, spinal cord, vagus nerve, and prevertebral fascia." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/71616004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://snomed.info/id/63190004> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#located_in> <http://snomed.info/id/49370004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p65_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration prominently features the sternocleidomastoid muscle on both sides of the neck, with the omohyoid muscle at the base. The scalene muscles are visible in the upper part of the neck. Nerves are labeled throughout, with the brachial plexus near the shoulder, the phrenic nerve running along the front, the ansa cervicalis near the middle, the accessory nerve (CN XI) near the back, the vagus nerve (CN X) down the side, the hypoglossal nerve (CN XII) near the base of the tongue, and the facial and vestibulocochlear nerves near the ear. Blood vessels are also highlighted, including the internal and external carotid arteries, the common carotid artery near the carotid bifurcation, the superior and inferior thyroid arteries, the internal jugular vein on the right, and the superficial cervical artery near the surface. Other structures such as the carotid body, carotid bifurcation, thyroid gland, sympathetic trunk, and parathyroid glands are labeled, with the parathyroid glands inferred to be near the thyroid gland." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p67_b18> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/59820001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
