<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p65_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/45048000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p67_b18> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the neck and upper chest region, with the parotid gland situated at the top left near the cheek. Below it, the mylohyoid muscle extends towards the chin, while the hypoglossal nerve runs alongside. The digastric muscle's anterior belly is positioned below the hypoglossal nerve, near the jawline. On the right side, the external carotid artery runs vertically along the neck, with the internal carotid artery located deeper and parallel to it. The ansa cervicalis is depicted branching from the vagus nerve, and the internal jugular vein is shown as a large vein running near the carotid arteries. The sterno hyoid muscle lies below the internal jugular vein, with the sternothyroid muscle situated further down beside it. The vagus nerve passes through the neck region, and the vertebral artery runs along the vertebral column at the bottom of the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#figureRef> "c009" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/7098a6320480> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/49370004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/bdf5bc9c7dcb> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/bdf5bc9c7dcb> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is a cross-section with the carotid sheath positioned at the top left, appearing green and surrounding the common carotid artery, which is shown in red. The internal jugular vein is depicted in blue, also within the carotid sheath, at the top right. Vertebrae are displayed as a series of stacked, dark gray structures forming the central column of the image on the left side. The spinal cord is shown as a pinkish-purple structure extending through the vertebral canal, labeled below the vertebrae. The vagus nerve is a yellow structure extending from the spinal cord, located on the right side. The prevertebral fascia is a purple structure surrounding the vertebrae and spinal cord, positioned at the bottom left." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a detailed anatomical view of the neck, focusing on the blood vessels, muscles, and bones." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s3> .
