<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features three blue rectangular boxes stacked vertically against a white background. Below it, the middle box explains that intestinal contents are propelled forward by segmental and peristaltic contractions. The boxes are separated by thin white spaces, with no arrows or connecting lines." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/256674009> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is structured with a cross-section of the intestinal wall, featuring an outer blue layer and an inner light blue layer. At the top left, a box labeled \"Proteins\" has an arrow pointing downward to a \"Peptides\" box. Below this, three smaller boxes are labeled: \"Di- and tripeptides cotransport with H⁺ on PepT1,\" \"Amino acids cotransport with Na⁺,\" and \"Small peptides are carried intact across the cell by transcytosis.\" Arrows connect these boxes, indicating pathways. Small peptide molecules are depicted within the intestinal lumen, with arrows showing their movement through the wall into intestinal cells. At the bottom, red arrows labeled \"Blood\" and \"To the liver\" point left and right, respectively. Additional labels like \"H⁺,\" \"Na⁺,\" \"K⁺,\" and \"ATP\" are near the intestinal cells, with dotted lines and arrows indicating ion flow and peptide movement." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s4> .
