<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a centrally positioned liver in light brown, connected to several blood vessels. At the top left, a text box explains the liver's role in filtering nutrients. On the left side of the liver, blue capillaries are labeled. A blue hepatic vein extends to the right, and a larger blue vein, the inferior vena cava, rises upwards. The hepatic artery, shown in red, enters from the bottom right, while the hepatic portal vein, also blue, enters from the bottom left. At the bottom, a network of red digestive tract arteries and blue capillaries, with yellow dots symbolizing nutrients, is depicted. The aorta, a large blue vessel, is positioned at the top right." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s4> .
