<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized with the Hypothalamus at the top, depicted as a light blue rectangle with rounded corners. Two arrows extend downward from the Hypothalamus: one to SRIF and another to GHRH, both represented by light blue rectangles. SRIF is positioned directly below the Hypothalamus, while GHRH is to the right of SRIF. The Anterior Pituitary is centrally located, shown as an orange cloud-like shape, with arrows pointing to it from both SRIF and GHRH. GH is situated below the Anterior Pituitary in a light blue rectangle, with an arrow pointing downward to IGF-I, also in a light blue rectangle. Somatic Growth is at the bottom, represented by an orange oval, with arrows pointing to it from both GH and IGF-I. Green plus signs indicate positive effects, while blue minus signs indicate negative effects or feedback loops." <urn:graph:endocrine/s9> .
