<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p65_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a central, irregularly shaped structure with multiple smaller compartments radiating outward, resembling a starburst pattern. The central structure has a lighter pinkish hue, while the surrounding compartments are darker pinkish-red. Within these compartments, several dark blue, oval-shaped structures, resembling nuclei, are visible. The outermost layer of the structure is outlined in a darker pinkish-red color, likely representing the basement membrane or the outer boundary of the acinus. A black line points to one of the smaller compartments, indicating a specific area within the mucous acinus. The word \"Mucous acinus\" is centered at the bottom of the image." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s11> .
