<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p97_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a microscopic view of liver tissue, with the label \"Slide 88 Liver\" at the top left corner. The tissue is stained, showing numerous small, dark circular cells scattered throughout, surrounded by lighter regions. Blue arrows point to irregular, winding channels within the tissue, labeled as \"Sinusoids.\" In panel (a), Kupffer cells appear as black cells in a liver lobule from a rat injected with particulate India ink. Panel (b) shows Kupffer cells in the sinusoid between two groups of hepatocytes, appearing larger than the flattened endothelial cells." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed anatomical illustration of the gingiva surrounding a tooth, with labels identifying various structures and fibers." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/3603368200ea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
