<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p115_b12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p98_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/1186703007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a central section featuring the dental pulp, which is colored greenish-blue and positioned centrally. It is surrounded by the pinkish-purple dentin on both sides, with the elongated odontoblasts lining the outermost layer of the dentin. The predentin appears as a lighter, more translucent area between the dentin and odontoblasts. Two insets are included: the left inset provides a close-up of the dentin and odontoblasts, while the right inset focuses on the predentin layer. Leader lines connect labels to the corresponding parts of the image, clearly indicating the location of each component." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/1abf12d6e07e> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/181769001> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://snomed.info/id/181769001> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#connects_to> <http://snomed.info/id/38888009> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/4421005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed anatomical illustration of a tooth cross-section, labeling various components such as enamel, dentin, pulp cavity, and root structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed cross-section of a tooth, with the outermost layer, enamel, positioned at the top left. Within the dentin, small gaps known as interglobular spaces are visible. At the center of the tooth, the pulp cavity is depicted as a hollow space, extending towards the root. The root of the tooth is surrounded by a layer called cementum, located at the bottom left. Fine lines, known as the lines of Retzius, are shown running through the enamel near the top right, while similar lines, the lines of Schreger, are situated deeper within the dentin, pointing to the middle right. Small protrusions of enamel, termed enamel tufts, are seen near the top right. The root canal, a hollow channel, extends from the pulp cavity to the bottom right, with the granular layer of Tomes at its base. Finally, the apical foramen, an opening at the tip of the root, is marked at the very bottom right." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p115_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/308763007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p115_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/12710003> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/49530007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/37887671cad1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/312239001> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure shows a detailed cross-sectional diagram of a taste bud, illustrating its various components such as the taste pore, surface epithelial cells, microvilli, sensory cells, supporting cells, afferent nerve fibers, and basal cells." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/7add27623396> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/31610004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/cbf0a8995f2a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/76caa698be94> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/38888009> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/37887671cad1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/4421005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p70_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with two main labeled structures. Arrows point to areas within the tissue, highlighting adipose cells that appear lighter compared to the surrounding tissue. Another arrow indicates the excretory duct, which is darker and more tubular. The adipose cells are scattered throughout the tissue, while the excretory duct is situated near the bottom left of the image. An inset on the right side provides a magnified view of a portion of the tissue, focusing on the cellular details." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/3603368200ea> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p95_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p97_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure shows a microscopic view of liver tissue with labeled sinusoids and Kupffer cells." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p87_b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p106_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates a diagram of the \"Classical liver lobule,\" highlighting its structure with a central vein and color-coded elements." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p119_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/62035001> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a rectangular histological section stained with shades of pink and purple. Nuclei are stained dark purple, while cytoplasm and extracellular matrix are pink. The image features labels \"L,\" \"CT,\" \"C,\" and \"T\" distributed throughout. \"L\" labels are spread across the image, appearing in the upper left, middle, and lower right sections. \"CT\" labels are concentrated in the central and upper regions, indicating areas with a more fibrous appearance. \"C\" and \"T\" labels are less prominent, with \"C\" in the upper right and \"T\" in the lower left corners. The tissue shows a dense network of cells and fibers, with lighter areas suggesting spaces between cells or different tissue types." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A microscopic view of tissue, likely a histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E), showing various structures that could represent different types of cells and connective tissues." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p106_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/15878004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/76caa698be94> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p100_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A microscopic view of cells with a yellowish-orange background, featuring small red structures and labeled elongated structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/59820001> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/2e77288de078> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p96_b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/49690003> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of a tooth and its surrounding tissues, with labels pointing to specific features. At the top left, the gingival sulcus is indicated, showing the space between the tooth and the gum tissue. Near this, the margin of gingiva is labeled, highlighting the edge where the gum meets the tooth. Below this, the free gingiva is marked, pointing to the unattached portion of the gum tissue. Further down, the attached gingiva is labeled, showing the part of the gum tissue firmly attached to the tooth. At the bottom left, the alveolar mucosa is labeled, pointing to the inner lining of the alveolus. On the right side, the junctional epithelium is labeled, indicating the thin layer of cells at the junction of the free gingiva and the tooth. Below this, circular fibers are shown, surrounding the tooth. The dento-gingival fibers are indicated further down, showing the fibers connecting the tooth to the gingiva. The dento-periosteal fibers are labeled next, pointing to the fibers connecting the tooth to the periosteum. The cementum is labeled below, indicating the layer surrounding the root of the tooth. At the very bottom, the dentin is labeled, showing the main part of the tooth's structure beneath the enamel. A magnified inset on the right provides a close-up view of the junctional epithelium and surrounding structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/2338009> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p92_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing densely packed cells with round to oval nuclei and pinkish cytoplasm." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#figureRef> "c001" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p115_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a microscopic view of cells arranged in an organized pattern. The nuclei are dark purple, while the cytoplasm appears lighter. The cells vary in size and shape, with some nuclei more rounded and others elongated. A black line extends diagonally from the right side of the image towards the upper right corner, not connected to any specific feature." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p119_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E). The cells are densely packed and exhibit a pinkish-purple color, indicating the presence of nuclei and cytoplasm. The nuclei are round to oval and vary slightly in size, with some appearing darker than others. The cytoplasm is less distinct but can be seen surrounding the nuclei. There are also areas that appear lighter, possibly representing extracellular matrix or other non-cellular components. There are no visible labels, text, or arrows within the image." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p97_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/256887000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p115_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/28273000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/9e8f424f0c11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/4421005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/49475008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p85_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a microscopic view of irregularly shaped cells with varying sizes. Some cells contain large, light-colored vacuoles, while others have darker, more granular contents. The labeled areas include 'A', positioned near a cell with a large, light-colored vacuole in the upper right section, 'B', over a cell with darker, granular material in the middle-right, and 'C', pointing to a cell with a large, light-colored vacuole in the lower left, with an arrow directly at the vacuole. The background has a textured, granular appearance." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/84540008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/113277000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38199008> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p101_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The interlobular septum is situated at the top left corner, appearing as a thin, fibrous layer that separates the lobules. Endothelial cells line the sinusoids, forming a distinct lining throughout the image. Kupffer cells are marked by arrows and are scattered irregularly within the hepatic plates, near the sinusoids. The bile duct is positioned at the bottom left, appearing as a tubular structure lined with epithelial cells. Sinusoids are found throughout the central and upper regions of the image, appearing as irregular spaces between hepatocytes where blood flows." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/09009d8dff4c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed microscopic cross-section of a tooth, with the oral epithelium positioned at the top left and right corners, appearing as a thin, stratified squamous layer. In the middle left section, the dental lamina is visible as a slightly darker area. Within the dental lamina, the external enamel epithelium is a thin layer, and below it, the stellate reticulum displays a network-like structure. The outermost layer of the tooth is the enamel, which appears translucent and layered. At the bottom left corner, bone is shown as a dense, compact structure. The epithelial root sheath (of Hertwig) is a thin layer at the bottom left. The enamel and stellate reticulum are also labeled at the top right and bottom right corners. Within the dentin, odontoblasts are elongated structures, and the dentin itself appears as a dense, calcified tissue beneath the enamel." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p119_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
