<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The left side of the image displays a histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E), featuring a cross-section of an organ or tissue. The labeled areas include \"G\" at the top-left, indicating a glandular region; \"M\" in the middle, pointing to a muscular layer; \"F\" near the top-right, marking a fibrous area; \"S\" on the right, highlighting another fibrous or connective tissue area; \"V\" at the bottom, indicating a vascular area; and \"OM\" on the far left, pointing to the outermost membrane or layer. On the right side, a cartoon character dressed as a doctor stands upright and smiles. The character has orange hair styled into a mane, a yellow horn, and wears a white coat with a stethoscope around his neck." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
