<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p106_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram comprises three hexagonal shapes, each symbolizing a liver lobule. These hexagons are subdivided into smaller sections, resembling a honeycomb pattern, and are filled with a pinkish-red color to represent the liver lobule's parenchyma. At the center of each hexagon, a blue circle signifies the central vein, connected to the surrounding tissue, indicating its role in draining blood. Red and green circles are also present within the lobule, likely representing other vascular structures or connections. The text \"Classical liver lobule: the unit drained by a central vein\" is positioned in the bottom right corner of the image, written in black font." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p101_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/256887000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
