<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-section of a tooth, with different anatomical structures clearly delineated. The layout of the image allows viewers to see the arrangement of these structures within the tooth, providing a visual understanding of their spatial relationships." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p70_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing adipose cells and an excretory duct within a dense connective tissue network." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p85_b5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/62650009> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p119_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing densely packed cells with pinkish-purple nuclei and cytoplasm, organized into irregular clusters." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a rectangular histological section with a central lighter area, flanked by darker regions on either side. Two yellow circles are positioned symmetrically on either side of this central area, each enclosing a region with a dense network of cells and fibers. The nuclei of cells are stained dark purple, while the cytoplasm and extracellular matrix are stained pinkish-red." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p87_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/10200004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
