<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into three sections. At the top, there's a labeled diagram of a tooth cross-section, where the outermost layer is marked as enamel, followed by dentin with visible tubules, and the white cementum at the base. The middle section presents a microscopic image of a tooth, displaying the same layers in a stained format. On the bottom right, a cartoon character dressed as a doctor stands next to the microscopic image, featuring orange hair, a yellow horn, and a white coat with a stethoscope, smiling and seemingly presenting the images." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
