<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p92_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E). The cells are densely packed, with round to oval nuclei that are darkly stained. The cytoplasm appears pinkish, and the nuclei are stained a deep purple, contrasting with the lighter pink cytoplasm. A network of thin, pale-staining structures is visible in the background, possibly representing blood vessels or connective tissue. A black arrow points towards a specific area in the lower left portion of the image, directing attention to that location." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
