<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a microscopic cross-section of a taste bud, with a small circular area labeled \"taste pore\" at the top left. Fine, hair-like projections labeled \"microvilli\" extend from the top of the sensory cells. Elongated cells labeled \"supporting cells\" surround the sensory cells, positioned beneath the microvilli. The sensory cells, labeled as such, are situated within the taste bud, surrounded by the supporting cells. A smaller, rounder cell labeled \"basal cell\" is located at the base of the sensory cells. A darker, more compact structure labeled \"nerve\" extends from the bottom into the deeper layers of the tissue." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p96_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section of liver tissue stained with a method that highlights different structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
