<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a circular cross-section of tissue, with myoepithelial cells positioned around the periphery. An arrow points downward from the label \"Myoepithelial cells\" at the top, directing attention to the central area. This central region appears lighter and more homogenous, contrasting with the surrounding cells. The depiction is monochromatic, using shades of gray to differentiate cellular components." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
