<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p85_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a microscopic view of cells with an oval shape, set against a pale yellowish background. Three red arrows are present: the first points to an area on the upper right side, the second to an area near the center and slightly to the left, and the third to an area towards the bottom right of the image." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a histological section with a light-colored matrix separating cells. At the top-center, the 'SD' label points to small, irregularly shaped cells with pale cytoplasm and darker nuclei. Larger, polygonal cells with densely packed nuclei, labeled 'A', are scattered throughout the image. At the bottom-center, the 'ID' label indicates smaller, round cells similar to the SD cells but smaller. The cells are clustered, with some areas denser than others, and the nuclei are stained dark purple, while the cytoplasm has a lighter, granular texture." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p86_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is split into two sections. On the left, there is a diagram labeled (a) Hepatic lobules. On the right, there is a microscopic image labeled (b) Hepatocytes and sinusoids." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
