<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/569ead6a3e7a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/91727004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing various tissue components with labeled regions and arrows highlighting specific areas." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/64033007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p70_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/12710003> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a vertical cross-section of a taste bud, with a light pink background symbolizing the surrounding tissue. At the top-center, the taste pore is depicted as a small opening. Surface epithelial cells are positioned on the left side, extending from the surface towards the sensory cells. Supporting cells, shown in a lighter color, are centrally located within the taste bud, beneath the surface epithelial cells. Sensory cells, darker in color, are situated deeper, surrounding the supporting cells. Microvilli, hair-like structures, extend from the top of the sensory cells. Yellow lines represent afferent nerve fibers extending from the bottom, connecting the sensory cells to the nervous system. Black text labels are connected by leader lines to each part of the diagram." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p101_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/256002> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/4421005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/37887671cad1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/3057000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/15878004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed microscopic cross-section of a tooth, showing various labeled structures such as the oral epithelium, lamina propria, dental lamina, enamel, dentin, and more." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/76993005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/b8f6f0bf4ccc> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://snomed.info/id/91727004> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <http://snomed.info/id/80891009> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a cross-section of dental tissue with distinct layers and regions. Beneath it lies the oral epithelium, also appearing as a thin layer. The stratum intermedium is situated between the outer and inner enamel epithelia, showing a clear layering pattern. Within the central area, the dental sac is surrounded by the stellate reticulum and the inner enamel epithelium, appearing as a rounded, darker region. The dental papilla, a small, rounded structure, is located within the dental sac and appears lighter and more cellular compared to the surrounding stellate reticulum. The inner enamel epithelium is at the bottom, forming a continuous layer in contact with the dental papilla. The overall appearance is that of a stained histological slide, with tissues stained in varying shades of purple and pink." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p92_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/62035001> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p98_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing a field of cells with nuclei and cytoplasmic structures, featuring two large, darkly stained areas labeled \"K\" in the central region." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p115_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-sectional view of glandular tissue, with the lamina forming the outermost layer at the top left corner. Inside the lamina, multiple small, branching structures called acini are depicted. Centroacinar cells are situated centrally within these acini, while the intercalated ducts are shown branching out from the main body of the glandular structure near the upper right section." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p100_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-sectional view of a taste bud with a gradient pink background. At the top-center, the taste pore is positioned as the entry point for substances. On the left, surface epithelial cells are depicted surrounding the taste pore, forming the outer layer. Microvilli extend from the sensory cells, pointing towards the taste pore, and are shown on the right side. Sensory cells, which contain taste receptors, are located near the microvilli and are labeled on the right. Supporting cells are illustrated on the left, surrounding the sensory cells. Afferent nerve fibers extend from the bottom, connecting to the basal cells, and are labeled on the right. Basal cells are situated at the base, where the afferent nerve fibers connect, and are labeled on the right side." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p73_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/362938003> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://snomed.info/id/91727004> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <http://snomed.info/id/82280004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/9f4bb65b1fb8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/1186703007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with varying shades of pink and purple, typical of H&E staining. In the top-left region, there is a small, darker-stained area, possibly indicating a nucleus or a dense region of the tissue. Center-right, a larger, lighter-stained area is visible, potentially representing cytoplasm or a less densely packed region. Another darker area is present in the bottom-left, similar to the top-left, suggesting another nucleus or dense region. The bottom-center region shows a lighter area, consistent with the central region but slightly more spread out. The image lacks labels or text and is a single frame without additional annotations or arrows." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/2e77288de078> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p95_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a magnified view of cells and tissues, with the structures stained using hematoxylin and eosin. The staining highlights the nuclei in dark blue and the cytoplasm and other structures in pink, allowing for clear visualization of the tissue architecture." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing a dense network of cells and fibers with labeled structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
