<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section of dental tissue, likely from an embryo or developing tooth, showing various labeled structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a complex arrangement of tissues with tubular structures appearing pinkish, suggesting the presence of cytoplasmic material. Surrounding these tubular structures are areas with a more granular appearance, possibly representing connective tissue or interstitial spaces. Blue arrows are scattered throughout the image, pointing to specific areas of interest within the tissue sections, but they lack accompanying text or labels. The nuclei of cells are stained dark blue/purple due to the hematoxylin stain, while the cytoplasm and other extracellular components are stained pink/red due to the eosin stain. The image is divided into several distinct regions, with the central area containing a cluster of tubular structures, while the surrounding areas show more diffuse tissue." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
