<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing various tissue components under a microscope, likely from an organ such as the kidney." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p87_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top left, endothelial cells are small and irregularly shaped with dark outlines. Centrally, the darker, elongated central vein is surrounded by tissues. Near the bottom left, bile canaliculi appear as small, branching structures. At the top right, hepatic plates are larger, rectangular structures composed of closely packed cells. Also near the top right, bile canaliculi are smaller branching structures within the hepatic plates. At the bottom right, sinusoids are irregular, thin-walled spaces between the hepatic plates, appearing lighter compared to the surrounding tissue. Each component is labeled with a number and an arrow pointing to its corresponding location in the image." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s1> .
