<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents an anatomical view of the human body, focusing on the endocrine system. The hypothalamus is positioned at the base of the brain and is labeled at the top left. Directly below it is the pituitary gland, also labeled at the top left. Near the center of the brain, the pineal gland is shown and labeled at the top right. In the neck area, the thyroid gland is depicted with a label at the top right, alongside the parathyroid glands, which are located on the posterior surface of the thyroid gland. The thymus is positioned behind the sternum and is labeled at the top right. The heart is located in the chest cavity and is labeled at the top left. Above the kidneys, the adrenal glands are shown and labeled at the top left." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s1> .
