<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p61_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/264198001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The liver is positioned at the top-left of the image, with an arrow pointing to the right lobe. The right and left hepatic ducts are depicted as white tubes branching from the liver, each labeled with an arrow. The cystic duct is shown as a small tube connected to the gallbladder, indicated by an arrow. The gallbladder appears as a green, pear-shaped organ below the liver, with labels pointing to its neck and head. The neck is the narrow part of the gallbladder, while the head is the wider part, both labeled with arrows. The bile duct is a white tube extending from the liver, labeled with an arrow. The common hepatic duct is a white tube that combines with the cystic duct, labeled with an arrow. The accessory pancreatic duct is a small tube connected to the pancreas, labeled with an arrow. The pancreatic duct is a larger tube that merges with the accessory pancreatic duct, also labeled with an arrow. The tail of the pancreas is at the lower end, the body in the middle, and the head at the upper end, each labeled with an arrow. The duodenum, the first part of the small intestine, is labeled with an arrow. The minor duodenal papilla is a small protrusion on the duodenum, labeled with an arrow. The plicae circulares are the circular folds inside the duodenum, labeled with an arrow. The major duodenal papilla is a larger protrusion on the duodenum, labeled with an arrow." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s1> .
