<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p1_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a male figure with different glands and organs highlighted in color. The pineal gland is positioned at the top of the head, near the back of the brain, while the hypothalamus is just below it. The pituitary gland is situated at the base of the brain, below the hypothalamus. The thyroid gland appears as a butterfly-shaped organ at the front of the neck, with the parathyroid glands shown as small, pinkish structures on its dorsal aspect. The thymus gland is an elongated organ located behind the sternum, above the heart. The adrenal glands are depicted as two small, yellowish structures positioned on top of the kidneys. The pancreas is a long, curved organ situated behind the stomach, extending from the upper to the lower abdomen. The testis is shown as a single, red, oval-shaped structure in the lower abdomen, near the pelvic area. Each gland or organ is connected by a leader line or arrow pointing to its corresponding label, which is placed to the left of the figure." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s1> .
