<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p63_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The pancreas is rendered in a light brown hue, with its internal structure exposed in a cross-section, and the main pancreatic duct running through it. The gallbladder, colored green, is situated on the left side of the pancreas and is divided into three sections: Fundus, Body, and Neck. The duodenum is depicted in cross-section, showing its internal structure, with labels for the superior, descending, ascending, and inferior parts. The pyloric orifice is labeled at the junction where the stomach meets the duodenum, and the jejunum and ileum are also labeled, indicating the continuation of the small intestine. Leader lines guide the viewer to specific anatomical parts, such as the fundus, body, and neck of the gallbladder, and the various sections of the duodenum." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s1> .
