<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p60_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The celiac trunk is positioned centrally in the image, appearing as a large, cylindrical structure that branches into several smaller vessels. The gastroduodenal artery extends to the right from the left side of the celiac trunk, while the right gastroepiploic artery branches off to the left from the right side. The dorsal pancreatic artery extends towards the pancreas from the left side, and the splenic artery extends towards the spleen from the front. The spleen is depicted as a dark, kidney-shaped organ with a network of red blood vessels on the right side of the image. The pancreas is shown as a light pink, elongated organ with a network of red blood vessels, located below the spleen and to the left of the duodenum. The duodenum is a curved tube at the bottom of the image, extending from the stomach to the small intestine. The aorta is a large, red, cylindrical structure at the bottom, extending upwards. Each artery and organ is labeled with text pointing to specific parts of the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/6d548607ffa9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1be107d9151e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/434912009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p60_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The pancreas is the central structure, colored in orange-brown, with its head, body, and tail clearly defined. The surrounding vasculature is shown in blue, forming a network around the pancreas. The labels are written in black text, with leader lines or arrows pointing to the corresponding veins. The left gastric vein is at the top left corner, near the left side of the pancreas. The portal vein is near the top center, pointing to the upper part of the pancreas. The right gastric vein is on the right side, pointing to the right side of the pancreas. The posterior superior pancreaticoduodenal vein is also near the top center, pointing to the upper part of the pancreas. The superior mesenteric vein is situated on the left side, pointing to the left side of the pancreas. The anterior superior pancreaticoduodenal vein is positioned near the bottom left, pointing to the lower part of the pancreas. The right gastroepiploic vein is on the right side, pointing to the right side of the pancreas. The anterior inferior pancreaticoduodenal vein is found on the bottom left, pointing to the lower part of the pancreas. The splenic vein is positioned on the right side, pointing to the right side of the pancreas. The left gastroepiploic vein is on the left side, pointing to the left side of the pancreas. The caudal pancreatic vein is on the right side, pointing to the right side of the pancreas. The great pancreatic vein is also on the right side, pointing to the right side of the pancreas. The inferior mesenteric vein is located on the right side, pointing to the right side of the pancreas. The middle colic vein is positioned on the right side, pointing to the right side of the pancreas." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/3ccf4a620a33> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/2bf68010fbea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "In the center of the image, the stomach is depicted as a large, rounded organ with a smooth, pinkish surface. To the left of the stomach, the liver is shown as a large, brown organ positioned above and slightly behind the stomach. Below the liver, the gallbladder appears as a small, green, pear-shaped structure. An arrow points from the gallbladder towards the epiploic foramen, indicating the direction of movement or flow. The text \"Epiploic foramen\" is written in black near the gallbladder, pointing directly at it. Additional structures resembling parts of the intestines or other abdominal organs are shown in a lighter color below the stomach. The lower part of the image displays a yellowish-brown area, likely representing fat tissue or another type of connective tissue within the abdominal cavity." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the human digestive system with a focus on the liver and its surrounding structures, including the gallbladder, bile ducts, lymph nodes, blood vessels, pancreas, and spleen." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
