<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p58_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the abdominal cavity, with the inferior vena cava positioned on the left side, extending upwards. Near the center-left, the duodenum is depicted as a yellowish structure with a circular opening. The abdominal aorta, colored blue, runs vertically through the center of the image. The splenic artery is shown as a red structure branching off from the abdominal aorta, directed towards the spleen. The stomach, rendered in pink, is displayed with an open section revealing its interior, situated above the pancreas. The spleen is a dark purple organ located on the right side. The left kidney, appearing reddish-brown, is placed below the stomach and to the left. The jejunum, shown as a coiled structure with a circular opening, is positioned below the pancreas. The duodenojejunal flexure, a curved section, connects the duodenum to the jejunum. The root of the mesentery and the attachment of the transverse mesocolon are also depicted, connecting the jejunum to the abdominal wall. Leader lines are used to connect labels to the corresponding anatomical structures, with labels placed around the periphery of the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
