<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large, reddish-brown liver occupies the center of the image, with a cutaway section revealing its internal structure. Adjacent to the liver, a greenish-yellow, pear-shaped gallbladder is visible. Blue and red tubes represent bile ducts and blood vessels branching out from the liver and gallbladder. Small, yellowish lymph nodes are scattered throughout the liver and surrounding areas. Red and blue tubes symbolizing arteries and veins interconnect the liver and other organs. A pinkish pancreas is partially visible behind the liver, with its ducts and blood vessels depicted. To the left of the liver, a dark, irregularly shaped spleen is connected by blood vessels. The right side of the image features a magnified inset providing a closer view of the liver's internal structure, including lymph nodes and blood vessels. A watermark reading \"www.keenpub.com\" appears in the background." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s20> .
