<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p5_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two main sections: an upper section featuring the ribcage and a lower section focusing on the pelvic region. The ribs are light beige, while the muscles are shaded in pink. The pelvic region is outlined in blue, and the pelvic inlet is highlighted by a dashed red line. The twelfth rib on the left side is labeled \"Rib XII,\" and the lower edge of the ribcage is marked as the \"Costal margin.\" The iliolumbar ligament is positioned near the lumbar spine, connecting the ilium to the lumbar vertebrae, and the inguinal ligament is located at the lower part of the pelvis, connecting the anterior superior iliac spine to the pubic tubercle." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s1> .
