<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a detailed view of the human body in median section, focusing on the thoracic and pelvic areas. The thoracic region is shaded light pink and includes the thoracic diaphragm, a curved muscle at the base, and the thoracic cage, which is the bony framework enclosing the thoracic cavity. A dashed red line marks the plane of the superior thoracic aperture at the top of the thoracic cavity. In the abdominal area, a vertical dashed line divides the region into left and right halves. The pelvic region is colored green and features the plane of the superior pelvic aperture, marked by another dashed red line, indicating the upper boundary of the pelvic cavity. The pubic symphysis is shown at the front where the two pubic bones meet. A vertical dashed line, the pelvic axis, runs centrally through the pelvic cavity. The lower boundary, the pelvic outlet, is also delineated by a dashed red line, and the pelvic diaphragm is visible at the base. Various arrows and leader lines connect labels to the corresponding anatomical features, such as the thoracic diaphragm, thoracic cage, abdominal axis, pelvic structures, and the abdomino-pelvic cavity, which lies between the thoracic and pelvic cavities." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p90_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/113343008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p5_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/51185008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p87_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A diagram of a human torso is shown from the front view, focusing on the upper body up to the waist. The costal margin is labeled at the top, just below the ribcage. In the lower abdomen, three levels of enlargement are indicated: 'Tip enlargement' points to a small shaded area, 'Moderate enlargement' to a larger shaded area above 'Marked enlargement', which is the largest shaded area at the bottom. The areas of enlargement are shaded in progressively darker shades of light pink, from the costal margin to the marked enlargement. A blue arrow curves downward from the costal margin to the marked enlargement, highlighting the progression. The diagram also outlines the abdominal quadrants: Right Upper Quadrant (RUQ), Left Upper Quadrant (LUQ), Right Lower Quadrant (RLQ), and Left Lower Quadrant (LLQ)." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s1> .
