<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p74_b19> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large, reddish-brown organ resembling a kidney is positioned on the left side of the image. The adrenal gland is labeled at the top-left corner, pointing to a small, brown, irregularly shaped structure attached to the upper part of the kidney. On the right side, a square box provides a close-up view of the adrenal gland, divided into two parts: the adrenal medulla and the adrenal cortex. The adrenal medulla is indicated by a label at the bottom-right corner, pointing to the darker, central region, while the adrenal cortex is labeled at the bottom-left corner, highlighting the lighter outer layer. The text \"Pheochromocytoma\" is positioned at the top-right corner of the zoomed-in view, pointing to the adrenal medulla. The Cleveland Clinic logo is located in the bottom-left corner of the main image, with the copyright notice \"©2021\" placed next to it." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s17> .
