<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p87_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a detailed layout of the sympathetic nervous system's innervation, with the renal ganglia positioned at the top near the kidneys, depicted as small, oval-shaped structures. On the left side, the lumbar sympathetic ganglia are shown as a series of four stacked oval shapes. The pre-aortic plexus is represented by a network of yellow lines surrounding a red aorta. The superior hypogastric plexus is located below the aorta on the right, also shown in yellow. The ovarian plexus is near the ovaries, indicated by yellow lines. The hypogastric nerve extends from the lumbar sympathetic ganglia, depicted as yellow lines on the left. At the bottom, the sacral sympathetic ganglia are shown as another series of stacked ovals. The pelvic plexus is near the pelvic area, shown in yellow, while the nervi erigentes are represented by blue lines extending from the sacral sympathetic ganglia." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s17> .
