<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p73_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features the suprarenal gland positioned at the top right, near the kidney, which is a large, bean-shaped organ on the right side. The ureter is a tube extending from the kidney down towards the bladder, situated at the bottom. Different lymphatic regions are color-coded: lumbar in green, celiac in red, hepatic in yellow, common iliac in orange, internal iliac in purple, and external iliac in blue. Arrows indicate the direction of lymph flow within these regions. A key on the right explains the colors and arrows corresponding to the lymphatic regions and flow direction, showing branches and connections between these regions." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s17> .
