<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p70_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The central part of the image displays internal organs such as the heart, lungs, liver, and kidneys, alongside parts of the digestive system. Nerves and blood vessels are color-coded: red for arteries, blue for veins, and yellow for nerves. Specific structures are labeled, including the right and left phrenic nerves, the right and left inferior phrenic artery and plexus, the right and left suprarenal glands, the right and left greater, lesser, and least thoracic splanchnic nerves, the right and left renal ganglion and plexus, and the left and right sympathetic trunks, along with the first lumbar splanchnic nerves on both sides." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/475edcf39cfe> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s17> .
