<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/8d954cc1ea9c> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized into four distinct layers, each labeled with a green text box. At the top, the Mucosa appears as a light brown layer with small, irregularly shaped structures filled with blue dots. Below it, the Submucosa is also light brown but with a different texture, containing larger, more rounded structures filled with blue dots. The Cartilage Ring, situated beneath the Submucosa, is depicted in blue with numerous circular holes filled with white circles. Finally, the Adventitia at the bottom is a smooth, light brown layer without internal structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/113192009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/54066008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/243949006> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/34c21e033282> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/29dbd1764439> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/48077000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The esophagus is positioned vertically in the image, with the oesophageal mucosa and submucosa labeled at the top left. The diaphragm stretches horizontally across the middle, dividing the thoracic and abdominal cavities. Above the diaphragm, the supradiaphragmatic fascia is labeled on the right, while below it, the infradiaphragmatic fascia is also labeled on the right. The phreno-oesophageal ligament is shown in two parts: the ascending or upper limb extends upwards from the diaphragm towards the upper part of the esophagus, and the descending limb extends downwards towards the lower part. The subhiatal fat ring is depicted on the left, encircling the lower end of the esophagus. The zigzag (Z) line, marking the junction of the esophageal and gastric mucosa, is labeled on the left. The peritoneum is shown on the right, surrounding the stomach, with the cardiac notch labeled near the stomach's indentation. The cardiac part of the stomach is labeled on the right, and the gastric folds (rugae) are indicated at the bottom, representing the inner surface of the stomach." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the thoracic cavity and its contents from two different perspectives, detailing the branching of the common carotid artery, the positioning of the trachea and esophagus, and the structures around the diaphragm and heart." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/62834003> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/362884007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1ddf954b2ae2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/68959004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/32849002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/51185008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed anatomical illustration of the posterior view of the neck and pharynx. Specific structures are labeled throughout the image, including the superior, middle, and inferior pharyngeal constrictors, the glossopharyngeal nerve (CN IX), the internal jugular vein, the internal carotid artery, the styloid process, the digastric (posterior belly), the stylopharyngeus, the medial pterygoid, the pharyngeal plexus of nerves, the greater horn of the hyoid bone, the pharyngeal raphe, the cricopharyngeal part of the inferior constrictor, the thyroid gland, the inferior thyroid artery, the right recurrent laryngeal nerve, and the esophagus. The layout is oriented with the back of the neck facing the viewer, as indicated by the label \"(A) Posterior view\" at the bottom left corner." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/8d954cc1ea9c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
