<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents detailed anatomical views, with the anterior and posterior aspects of the thoracic region clearly displayed. The nervous system and related structures are the primary focus, depicted with precision and clarity. The layout is organized to highlight the key elements of the thoracic anatomy, ensuring that each component is distinctly visible." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The esophagus is centrally positioned in the image, with the throat located above it and the stomach situated below. The upper esophageal sphincter is near the top center, pointing to the upper part of the esophagus, while the lower esophageal sphincter is near the bottom center, pointing to the lower part. The diaphragm is shown below the esophagus, and the trachea is depicted to the right. The stomach is at the bottom center, connected to the lower end of the esophagus." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
