<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure consists of two labeled anatomical illustrations, \"a\" and \"b,\" each providing a different view of the thoracic cavity. In illustration A, the top left region features the common carotid artery branching into the internal jugular vein and subclavian artery. The middle region shows the esophagus, cervical part, and brachiocephalic trunk. At the bottom, the right and left main bronchi and the thoracic aorta are visible. The bottom left region details the diaphragm, including the central tendon, caval opening, right crus, lumbar part, inferior phrenic arteries, aortic hiatus, coeliac trunk, and abdominal aorta. The bottom right labels the stomach, cardiac part, and oesophageal hiatus. Illustration B, in the top left, labels the common carotid artery, internal jugular vein, subclavian artery and vein, and the right brachiocephalic vein. The center region shows the tracheal cartilages, aortic arch, ligamentum arteriosum, and left brachiocephalic vein. On the right side, the pharyngeal muscles, thyroid gland, right lobe, common carotid artery, internal jugular vein, subclavian artery and vein, and the central tendon are labeled. The illustrations use color-coded reds and blues to differentiate between arteries, veins, and other tissues." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/5798000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s13> .
