<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed anatomical illustration of a human skull viewed from the side, with labels pointing to specific parts of the bone structure." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/89546000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a side view of a human skull, with labels strategically placed to identify various anatomical features. The parietal bone is labeled on the large, flat sections on either side of the skull. The dorsum sellae is shown as the roof of the sella turcica, which houses the pituitary gland. The temporal bone is labeled on the side of the head, with the groove for the inferior petrosal sinus and the internal acoustic meatus also indicated on this bone. The mastoid foramen is shown as an opening in the mastoid process. The occipital bone is labeled at the back of the skull, with the occipitomastoid suture marking the line where it meets the mastoid process. The groove for the sigmoid sinus and the groove for the transverse sinus are both shown on the occipital bone. Finally, the occipital condyle is labeled." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
