<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents an anatomical illustration of the anterior surface of the sphenoid bone. At the top, the superior orbital fissure is labeled, indicating a narrow opening in the bone. In the center, the sphenoidal sinus appears as a dark cavity within the bone. The lesser wing extends laterally from the body of the sphenoid bone and is labeled on the right side. The orbital surface of the greater wing is also labeled on the right side. Near the bottom, the pterygoid canal is marked, pointing to a small channel, with the pterygoid process labeled below it." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
