<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a superior view of the sphenoid bone, centrally positioned and colored green. The frontal bone is at the top, shown in light blue. The ethmoid bone is centrally located above the sphenoid, featuring the crista galli, olfactory foramina, and cribriform plate. The temporal bone, in orange, is situated below the sphenoid, with the petrous portion and jugular foramen marked. The parietal bone, in purple, is above the sphenoid, showing the squamous suture. The occipital bone, in yellow, is at the bottom, featuring the foramen magnum and lambdoid suture. A transverse plane line is present at the top left corner." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/272676008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/56329008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/e852a53b0f14> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.8"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the pituitary gland and its surrounding structures, including various tracts and arteries that connect to and supply the gland." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1f3b90fe60e7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/272676008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
