<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1f3b90fe60e7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caused_by> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The main diagram presents a cross-sectional view of the brain and pituitary gland, with the pituitary gland appearing as a brown, oval-shaped structure connected to the hypothalamus. The pituitary gland's main parts are labeled: Infundibulum, Pars tuberalis, Pars intermedia, and Pars distalis. The Hypothalamus is situated above the pituitary gland, with the Mammillary body on the right side and the Optic chiasm above. An inset diagram in the top left corner provides a closer look at the pituitary gland and its connection to the hypothalamus, highlighting the Hypophyseal fossa within the Sella turcica of the Sphenoid bone. On the left side of the main diagram, a text box lists the three parts of the anterior pituitary gland: Pars tuberalis, Pars intermedia, and Pars distalis. On the right side, another text box lists the two parts of the posterior pituitary gland: Infundibular stalk and Pars nervosa. Arrows and leader lines connect these text boxes to specific parts of the pituitary gland in the main diagram. The background includes additional surrounding structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s5> .
