<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p66_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a detailed cross-sectional view of the lower jaw area. The masseter muscle is positioned at the top, colored red and textured, indicating its location in the cheek and jaw region. On the right side, the mucosa of the floor of the mouth is labeled, pointing to the inner lining near the bottom teeth. The sublingual ducts are depicted as yellow tubes extending from the sublingual gland towards the mucosa. Similarly, the submandibular duct is shown as a single yellow tube leading from the submandibular gland to the mucosa. The sublingual gland appears as a cluster of small, white, rounded structures situated below the tongue and near the bottom teeth. Beneath the sublingual gland and above the submandibular gland lies the mylohyoid muscle, illustrated as a yellow, flat structure. Finally, the submandibular gland is another cluster of small, white, rounded structures located below the mylohyoid muscle and above the mandible." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
