<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a pink, striped digastric muscle running vertically through the center. Near this muscle, a red line points to a yellow oval structure, the jugulodigastric node, situated within a blue area representing the carotid sheath. Below the jugulodigastric node, a series of interconnected yellow ovals signify the deep cervical chain. On the right side, small yellow ovals labeled as submental nodes are positioned above the larger submandibular nodes, which are located beneath the mandible. Arrows indicate lymph flow from the jugulodigastric node to the deep cervical chain and then to the submandibular and submental nodes. The background includes a simplified representation of the skull and surrounding soft tissues, with a color scheme of shades of blue, pink, and yellow." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
