<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a close-up of an eye, with the text \"Orbital part\" situated at the top, slightly left of center. The eye is partially closed, and the eyelashes are clearly visible. Above the eye, the eyebrow is shown with individual hairs discernible. The skin surrounding the eye appears smooth, suggesting a light complexion. The background has a textured appearance, resembling fabric or paper with a subtle pattern." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed anatomical illustration of the head and neck region, focusing on the parotid gland and surrounding structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/f4c9d0ddbd8f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/235595009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
