<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A close-up view of an eye with the text \"Orbital part\" positioned above it." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the head and neck, with the parotid gland prominently displayed. Facial muscles such as the orbicularis oris at the mouth and the buccinator near the cheek are included, alongside the masseter and medial pterygoid muscles flanking the mandible's ramus. The submandibular and sublingual glands are shown below the mandible and beneath the tongue, respectively. Cervical lymph nodes are labeled with deep and superficial groups. Red arrows point downward from the second maxillary molar tooth. Muscles are colored in shades of red and brown, glands and nerves in yellow and green, and blood vessels in blue." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the mouth and throat, with labels for the hard palate, soft palate, pharynx, uvula, and tongue. The hard palate is positioned at the top of the mouth, forming the roof, while the soft palate extends behind it. The pharynx is shown as the area behind the soft palate and tongue, and the uvula is depicted hanging from the back of the soft palate. The tongue is situated at the bottom of the mouth. The labels are written in black text and are placed near their corresponding anatomical features, maintaining a symmetrical layout." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/774007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
