<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The palatine process of the maxilla is highlighted by a red arrow pointing to the central region of the maxilla, forming part of the hard palate. Another red arrow indicates the horizontal plate of the palatine bone, situated at the lower part of the maxilla, contributing to the bony structure of the roof of the mouth. The teeth are depicted in a simplified manner, with some showing roots extending into the jawbone, and the maxilla is displayed symmetrically with clear markings for the palatine process and horizontal plate." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s10> .
