<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The spleen is shown in a pinkish-purple hue, with distinct areas labeled: the gastric area at the upper left, the renal area centrally below it, and the colic area at the lower right. White lines represent the short gastric vessels and left gastro-omental vessels extending from the gastric area toward the center. A green line indicates the splenorenal ligament containing the splenic vessels and the tail of the pancreas on the lower left side. A small black arrow points to the hilum in the central area, while the posterior extremity is labeled on the left side, pointing to the upper left corner. Borders are color-coded: the anterior extremity in red along the upper edge, the inferior border in green along the lower edge, and the superior border in blue along the upper edge. The legend explaining these color codes is positioned in the bottom right corner." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p72_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/38848004> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p82_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/10200004> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p76_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The liver is the central focus of the illustration, with its right lobe positioned on the left side and the left lobe on the right side. The gallbladder, depicted in green, is located above the liver and is divided into the Fundus, Body, and Neck. The bile duct is shown as a blue tube extending from the Porta Hepatis towards the gallbladder, while the portal vein is also a blue tube entering the Porta Hepatis. The hepatic artery proper is represented by a red tube entering the same area. The anterior and posterior regions of the liver are clearly marked, and labels are placed around the periphery, with leader lines or arrows pointing to the corresponding parts." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s20> .
