<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p72_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The pancreas is depicted in a cross-sectional view, colored pink with a layered appearance. It is labeled with different parts: A for the Uncinate process, B for the Head, C for the Neck, D for the Body, and E for the Tail. The main pancreatic duct is shown extending from the pancreas into the duodenum, while the accessory pancreatic duct branches off from it. The bile duct is also shown entering the duodenum near the major duodenal papilla. The duodenum is labeled with numbers 1 through 4, indicating different sections, and features the minor and major duodenal papillae at the junction with the pancreas. A legend on the right provides a key for the labels, listing the parts of the duodenum and pancreas. An inset image in the bottom left corner offers a close-up of the minor duodenal papilla. Arrows and leader lines connect the labels to specific anatomical parts." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s20> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p83_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/28273000> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s20> .
