<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p82_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a detailed anatomical illustration with the liver positioned at the top and depicted in green. The left hepatic artery and right hepatic artery are both labeled at the top left, branching from the hepatic artery proper. The left gastric artery is labeled at the top right, and the cystic artery is near the bottom left. The supraduodenal artery and gastroduodenal artery are positioned near the middle, while the right gastric artery is also labeled in the middle section. The abdominal aorta is at the bottom right, with the superior mesenteric artery and splenic artery nearby. All arteries are shown in red, while other organs are in pink." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s20> .
