<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a detailed anatomical illustration focusing on the lower portion of the human digestive system, particularly the ileocecal region. The ileocecal fold is positioned at the top left corner, while the ascending colon is labeled near the top on the upper right side. The ileum is labeled on the right side, and the ileocecal fold flaps are centered in the middle of the image. Below these flaps, the cecum is depicted as a large, pouch-like structure, with the appendix shown as a small, finger-like extension at the bottom right." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s15> .
