<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p58_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The table is organized into two main columns, with \"Jejunum\" on the left and \"Ileum\" on the right. Each column is divided into rows that list specific attributes such as color, caliber, wall thickness, vascularity, vasa recta, arcades, fat in mesentery, and circular folds. The characteristic row is highlighted in a purple shade, while the Jejunum and Ileum rows alternate between orange and white backgrounds for clarity. There are no leader lines or arrows connecting the text to any parts of the image." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s15> .
