<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed anatomical illustration with a white background and light brown-colored bones. Leader lines connect labels to various parts of the cervical spine, including the axis and atlas vertebrae. The top center highlights the odontoid process, axis, posterior articular facet, and anterior tubercle of the axis vertebra. On the middle left, the alar ligament, anterior arch, transverse ligament, and posterior arch of the atlas are labeled. The middle right shows the sulcus of the spinal nerve, transverse foramen, and posterior tubercle of the atlas. At the bottom center, the lateral mass of the atlas, atlanto-occipital joint, and lateral atlantoaxial joint are depicted. The diagram is well-organized, with clear labels and leader lines for each part." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s11> .
