<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a side profile of a human head and upper neck, with the background in light gray. The skull is colored in a light pinkish-white, forming the outer boundary of the head. Muscles are depicted in red, with lines indicating the direction and flow of muscle fibers. Thin, red lines extend from the muscles to small white boxes, which are placeholders for labels. Facial muscles around the mouth, cheeks, and jaw are prominently displayed with fibers running horizontally and vertically. Neck muscles are highlighted, extending from the base of the skull to the shoulders, with similar lines showing fiber direction. The external ear, including the ear canal and auricle, is outlined in a lighter shade of red. The layout is symmetrical along the vertical axis, focusing on the left side of the face and neck." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s11> .
