<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large, reddish-brown organ, likely the liver, is positioned in the upper left portion of the image with a smooth surface and visible folds. Blue lines, representing veins, run thickly and prominently through the lower part of the image, while green lines, possibly arteries, branch out from these blue lines and extend towards the lower right side. To the right of the liver, several lighter red structures, resembling parts of the digestive system like the stomach and intestines, are depicted with a more complex, convoluted appearance. Below the liver, layers of light brown muscle tissue, arranged in a grid-like pattern, suggest the abdominal wall. On the far left, a section of bone, possibly the ribcage or part of the spine, is shown in a light yellowish-brown color, partially visible and connected to the abdominal cavity. On the far right, two blue tubes, potentially the ureters or related ducts, are connected to the main organ, indicating a functional relationship with the urinary system." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s9> .
