<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p61_b14> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large, reddish-brown organ, likely the liver, is positioned at the top left of the image. Several muscles are visible in shades of red and pink, arranged in layers throughout the pelvis. Blue lines represent blood vessels, likely veins, distributed throughout the image and connecting to the tissues and organs. Green lines indicate nerves branching out from larger nerve trunks into the surrounding tissues. A light blue structure, probably the bladder, is located towards the bottom right. A darker blue structure, likely the rectum, is situated below the bladder. Other tissues, such as the sigmoid colon and possibly the uterus or ovaries, are also present but not clearly labeled. The image is oriented with the top representing the upper part of the body, the bottom the lower part, the left side the lateral aspect, and the right side the medial aspect of the pelvis." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s9> .
