<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p48_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is composed of six panels arranged in two rows of three. Each panel provides a close-up view of a child's mouth and nose area, with the lips slightly parted. In the top row, the first two panels show the child's mouth with slightly parted lips, while the third panel also displays a small amount of saliva or moisture at the corner of the mouth. The bottom row mirrors this layout, with each panel showing a small protrusion or bump on the lower lip. The third panel in the bottom row also has some saliva or moisture visible near the corner of the mouth. There are no labels, text, or arrows present in the image, focusing solely on the visual details." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s9> .
