<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p48_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two parts. On the left, there is a close-up view of a baby's face, showing a cleft lip, with the baby's eyes closed and smooth skin, and short, sparse hair. On the right, there is a magnified view of the inside of the baby's mouth, focusing on the palate, which reveals a cleft. The palate's cleft appears as a dark-colored split against the pinkish-red surrounding tissue. There are no texts, labels, or arrows in the image, and the two parts are presented side by side without any connecting lines or labels." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s9> .
