<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the mechanoreceptor positioned at the top right corner, pointing downward. Below it, the hypothalamus is shown, also pointing downward. Oxytocin is placed beneath the hypothalamus, directing towards the center of the diagram. Prolactin is situated above the central area, pointing downward. The myoepithelial cell is depicted as a cell layer surrounding the central area, with an arrow indicating its location. The alveolar epithelial cell is shown at the bottom of the central area, also labeled with an arrow. An arrow represents milk ejection, pointing from the duct to the central area, indicating the direction of milk movement. The duct is illustrated as a curved line extending from the left side of the diagram, pointing to the central area. The central area of the diagram, labeled as milk secretion, is the focal point where all arrows converge." <urn:graph:endocrine/s5> .
