<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the paraventricular nucleus and supraoptic nucleus positioned at the top left, both within the hypothalamus. The optic chiasma is centered, with the hypothalamus situated above it. Below the hypothalamus, the infundibulum is depicted as a small, conical structure, followed by the hypothalamo-hypophyseal tract. The anterior pituitary is shown at the bottom left, while the posterior pituitary is at the bottom right. An orange box at the top right indicates that ADH and oxytocin are produced in the paraventricular and supraoptic nuclei, and another orange box at the bottom right shows that these hormones are released into the bloodstream via the hypothalamo-hypophyseal tract." <urn:graph:endocrine/s5> .
