<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A cross-sectional view of the brain is presented, with the hypothalamus positioned at the top and the pituitary gland below it. An arrow connects the hypothalamus to the pituitary gland, indicating the direction of communication. The main section of the image zooms in on the pituitary gland and its connections, with the hypothalamus at the top right corner. The pituitary gland is centrally displayed, with several parts labeled: the infundibulum, median eminence, short portal vessels, hypothalamo-pituitary portal vessels, anterior pituitary, posterior pituitary, and endocrine cells. Leader lines guide the viewer to these specific parts. Red lines represent the arterial blood supply, while blue lines indicate venous circulation throughout the structures." <urn:graph:endocrine/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p70_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the hormonal pathways from the hypothalamus through the neurosecretory cells, posterior pituitary, and anterior pituitary, showing the release of hormones into the bloodstream and their target organs." <urn:graph:endocrine/s5> .
