<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p70_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a green, irregularly shaped structure at the top representing the hypothalamus. These cells are connected by lines to a yellow, bulbous structure below, which is the posterior pituitary gland. Beneath the posterior pituitary sits a pink, rounded structure, the anterior pituitary gland. A curved line, labeled as a blood vessel, connects the posterior pituitary to the anterior pituitary, with arrows indicating the direction of flow. The pathways from the posterior pituitary are labeled with oxytocin, pointing towards the uterine muscles and mammary glands, while ADH is labeled on the pathway from the anterior pituitary to the kidney tubules." <urn:graph:endocrine/s5> .
