<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is titled \"Flow Chart Representing Growth Hormone Production,\" with the title in white text on a blue background at the top. The Hypothalamus is positioned at the top of the flowchart, connected to the Pituitary by two arrows labeled \"GHRH\" and \"GHIH.\" Below the Hypothalamus, the Pituitary is connected to the Liver by an arrow labeled \"GH.\" The Liver is situated below the Pituitary and is connected to Muscle, Bone, and Fat Cells by arrows labeled \"IGF-1\" and \"Somatomedin-C.\" These cells are located at the bottom of the flowchart. Ellipses represent organs, while rectangles represent hormones or substances, and arrows indicate the direction of flow or influence between components." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s9> .
