<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p88_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a green dashed arrow pointing to the para-aortic lymph nodes near the aorta, and another green dashed arrow indicating the internal iliac lymph nodes near the internal iliac artery. A green dashed line connects the para-aortic lymph nodes to the internal iliac lymph nodes via the infundibulopelvic ligament. Another green dashed line links the internal iliac lymph nodes to the superficial inguinal lymph nodes through the ovarian ligament, with an additional green dashed line connecting the ovarian ligament to the superficial inguinal lymph nodes via the round ligament. The superficial inguinal lymph nodes are marked by a green dashed arrow near the groin area. The aorta is colored red, the internal iliac artery is blue, the uterus and fallopian tubes are pink and red, and the ovaries are pink." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s9> .
