<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p83_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the female pelvic region, with the aorta positioned at the top left and the inferior vena cava situated below it. The renal vein is at the top right, while the ovarian artery and vein are located near the kidneys. The psoas major muscle is depicted on either side of the spine, and the common iliac artery is shown between these muscles. The rectum is placed below the bladder, and the corpus uteri is centrally located, representing the uterus. The bladder is shown below the corpus uteri. Near the bladder, the vaginal artery and the superior vesical artery are illustrated. The external iliac artery and vein are depicted on both sides, while the internal iliac artery, anterior branch, is situated near the bladder. The inferior epigastric artery is shown on both sides, and the obturator artery is positioned near the bladder. The uterine artery and vein are displayed on both sides." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s9> .
