<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents two distinct views of a structure, with the anterior view on the left and the posterior view on the right. In the anterior view, the structure is triangular with a pointed tip, featuring a blue area labeled \"Suprarenal vein\" near the top-center and a larger, rounded section labeled \"Hepatic area\" at the bottom-left. The posterior view shows a similarly triangular structure but with a wider base. Here, the \"Diaphragmatic area\" is labeled at the top-center, the \"Renal area\" at the bottom-right, and an arrow indicates the \"Area in contact with IVC\" just below the \"Diaphragmatic area.\"" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p88_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/59441001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s9> .
