<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b14> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a full-body outline on the left side, showing a standing human figure in yellow underwear, highlighting the genital area. On the right, a detailed cross-sectional view of the lower abdomen and pelvis is displayed, with the spine at the center, labeled from L1 to L5. Various muscles and nerves are highlighted in different colors: the quadratus lumborum muscle in yellow, the psoas muscle in front of the lumbar spine, and the iliacus muscle near the iliac crest. The abdominal muscles are shown in a cutaway view, revealing internal organs. The inguinal ligament runs horizontally across the inguinal region, while the external inguinal ring and the spermatic cord are also depicted. The testicle and scrotum are shown within the scrotal sac, both highlighted in yellow. Nerves, including the iliohypogastric nerve near the iliac crest and the genitofemoral nerve with its femoral and genital branches, are labeled. Each structure is connected to its label by a leader line or arrow." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s9> .
