<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a cross-sectional view of the head, with the zygomatic bone positioned at the top left corner and the maxilla bone below it. The submandibular gland is located near the lower jaw, while the facial artery is shown as a red, curved line running upwards from the submandibular gland. The mylohyoid muscle appears as a white, horizontal band situated beneath the mandible." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
