<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p5_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The skull is divided into several sections, each represented by a different color. Leader lines connect labels to their corresponding bones. The frontal bone is positioned at the top of the skull, forming the forehead. The maxilla and mandible are depicted with their teeth sockets. The superior orbital fissure and optic canal are marked above the eye socket. The vomer and nasal conchae are within the nasal cavity, and the alveolar margins are shown at the edges of the maxilla and mandible where the teeth are seated." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
