<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/48477009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p61_b13> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed cross-sectional view of the lower face and jaw area. At the top, the maxilla is labeled, indicating the upper jawbone. Above the maxilla, the zygomatic bone is labeled, pointing to the cheekbone. Below the mandible, near the angle of the jaw, the submandibular gland is labeled with an arrow. A red line represents the path of the facial artery, running from the submandibular gland towards the lower jaw. At the bottom, the mylohyoid muscle is labeled, showing a horizontal muscle beneath the mandible. The labels are placed directly next to the corresponding anatomical features, with arrows pointing to specific parts." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://snomed.info/id/90780006> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <http://snomed.info/id/68426009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p61_b13> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomical structures of the lower face and jaw, including the maxilla, zygomatic bone, submandibular gland, facial artery, and mylohyoid muscle." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
