<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1eff3e24c72b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/91609006> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/23074001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/278412004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the human face, with the facial muscles displayed in shades of pink and the bones in a lighter, more translucent color. The eyebrows are shown with the superior portions of the facial muscles, including the brow raising muscles and the frontalis muscle. The eyes are depicted with closed eyelids, revealing the orbital cavity around the eye sockets. The nasal cavity is visible, featuring the nasal septum and nasal cartilage forming the bridge of the nose. The mouth is portrayed with the lips in a relaxed position, showcasing the orbicularis oris muscle. The cheeks are illustrated with the zygomaticus major and minor muscles, which control smiling and frowning. The lower jaw, or mandible, is partially visible at the bottom, showing the attachment of the masseter muscle. The neck muscles, including the sternocleidomastoid, are visible at the base of the skull. The image lacks labels or text, providing a clear view of the facial anatomy from the front." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/54019009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p55_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the facial region, with the parotid gland as the central focus. The lateral view provides a side-oriented depiction, while the horizontal section offers a cross-sectional insight into the structures involved." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/c4210f5ebc07> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p77_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/64131007> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/19602e665df3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/244949003> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p77_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/35532006> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/795a0d3a3056> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/84820005> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/c4210f5ebc07> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caused_by> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the human abdomen, with the inferior vena cava positioned at the top-center, pointing upwards. Just below it, the esophagus is shown pointing downwards. On the left side, the portal vein points towards the center, while the right suprarenal gland is situated near the top-left corner, pointing right. The duodenum's superior part is near the center, pointing slightly upwards, with the gallbladder situated below it, pointing right. The right kidney is on the left side, pointing towards the center, while the pancreas is in the center, pointing slightly upwards. The left kidney is on the right side, also pointing towards the center. The superior mesenteric vein and artery are near the pancreas, pointing towards the center. The descending colon is on the right side, pointing downwards, while the duodenum's descending and inferior parts are near the center, both pointing downwards. The ascending colon is on the left side, pointing downwards, and the duodenum's ascending part is near the center, pointing upwards. The abdominal aorta is at the bottom, pointing upwards. The skeletal structure of the pelvis is visible at the bottom of the image." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/795a0d3a3056> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/795a0d3a3056> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is composed of three labeled diagrams separated by vertical lines. The left diagram shows a cross-sectional view with the skin in blue as the outermost layer, followed by the superficial fascia in light pink, the fatty layer in yellow, and the membranous layer in purple. The penis is depicted in blue extending downward, with the pubic symphysis shown as a curved shape at the base. The middle diagram focuses on the scrotum, also in blue, with the dartos fascia beneath it in purple, and the pubic symphysis again as a curved shape. The right diagram presents a lateral view, featuring the aponeurosis of the external oblique as a blue line on the left, the inguinal ligament as a curved blue line connecting to the pubic symphysis, and the fascia lata of the thigh in yellow extending downward." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p48_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/69695003> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/19602e665df3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/795a0d3a3056> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/d3bfceba7311> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p48_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/65784005> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
