<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/113343008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p75_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The liver is shown in a reddish-brown color and is divided into a left and right lobe. The gallbladder is depicted in green, positioned below the liver, with distinct parts labeled as the Fundus, Body, and Neck. A white, ribbon-like structure called the Falciform Ligament extends from the top of the liver towards the bottom left corner. On the left side of the liver, there is a white, triangular structure labeled as the Left Triangular Ligament, while on the right side, a similar structure is labeled as the Right Triangular Ligament. The Anterior Coronary Ligament is a white, curved structure on the front of the liver, and the Posterior Coronary Ligament is another white, curved structure on the back. A small, unmarked area at the top of the liver is labeled as the Bare Area. Running vertically through the center of the liver is a blue, cylindrical structure labeled as the Inferior Vena Cava. Depressions on the liver's surface are labeled as the Suprarenal Impression on the top, the Renal Impression on the back, the Colic Impression also on the back, and the Esophageal Impression on the front." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/06a1f01eddab> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/a9527716591f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/68a343d7f1c4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p48_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/280119005> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p77_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The liver is depicted in a reddish-brown color and is divided into several lobes: the left lobe is on the left side, the right lobe is on the right side, the caudate lobe is near the inferior vena cava, and the quadrate lobe is between the left and right lobes. The gallbladder is a green, pear-shaped structure positioned below the liver and connected to it via the cystic duct. The inferior vena cava is a blue, cylindrical structure located behind the liver. The falciform ligament is a white, curved structure connecting the liver to the abdominal wall. The left triangular ligament is a white, triangular structure on the left side of the liver, while the right triangular ligament is on the right side. The anterior coronary ligament is a white, curved structure on the front side of the liver, and the posterior coronary ligament is on the back side. A small bare area is shown on the surface of the liver, free from ligaments. A depression labeled as the suprarenal impression is located above the liver, near the inferior vena cava." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
