<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The stomach is positioned at the center of the image, colored in a light pinkish-orange with a smooth, rounded shape. A slightly darker area at the bottom represents the pylorus. The abdominal aorta is shown at the bottom, depicted as a cylindrical structure with a smooth surface. Various arteries are connected by leader lines or arrows pointing to their corresponding labels. The labels are placed around the periphery of the image, with some pointing directly to the arteries and others to specific parts of the stomach. The arteries are rendered in a slightly darker hue compared to the stomach, and the labels are black text on a white background." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s17> .
