<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "In the top-left region, the genital branch of the genitofemoral nerve is labeled as it exits the abdominal wall, alongside the cremasteric vessels near the testis, the coiled ductus deferens, the artery to the ductus deferens, and the inferior epigastric vessels. The top-center region features the testicular artery and pampiniform plexus of veins, the parietal peritoneum, extraperitoneal fascia, transversalis fascia, ilioinguinal nerve, external oblique aponeurosis, and internal oblique muscle. The center region highlights the deep inguinal ring as a circular opening in the transversalis fascia, the superficial inguinal ring in the superficial fascia, the conjoint tendon, and the external oblique aponeurosis." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s18> .
