<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p19_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with densely packed cells, where the nuclei are dark purple against a lighter pink cytoplasmic background. The section is labeled with several markers: 'A' is positioned towards the upper middle, 'B' towards the lower left, 'CP' near the upper right, 'Ca' near the center-right, and 'Cp' near the bottom left. Arrows connect these labels to distinct regions within the tissue, highlighting areas of interest that exhibit varying sizes and shapes of nuclei." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s4> .
