<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with a central pinkish area labeled \"Co\", which appears to be a cavity or lumen. The nuclei of these cells are dark purple due to hematoxylin staining. The outermost layer of the tissue is composed of a lighter pink, dense, fibrous material. The text \"Co\" is positioned centrally above the pinkish area, without any arrows or leader lines connecting it to specific parts of the image." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s4> .
