<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p20_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure presents two anatomical illustrations side by side, each depicting the pelvic floor muscles in cross-section. Both illustrations are oriented with the top facing upwards. In the left illustration, the bulbospongiosus muscle is labeled at the top left, the ischiocavernosus in the middle left, and the superficial transverse perinei at the bottom left. The right illustration mirrors this layout, with the bulbospongiosus at the top right, the ischiocavernosus in the middle right, and the superficial transverse perinei at the bottom right. The muscles are shown in red, while the surrounding structures are in a lighter color, providing a clear view of the pelvic floor anatomy from different angles." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the pelvic floor's second layer, with labels and lines connecting to different anatomical structures and muscles." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s9> .
