<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p20_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/7295002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents two diagrams labeled A and B, each offering a distinct view of the pelvic region. Diagram A provides a side view, with the sacrum positioned at the top, the ilium on either side, and the pubis at the bottom. Key anatomical features like the sacrum, ilium, pubis, obturator internus muscle, obturator foramen, tendinous arch of pelvic fascia, and genital hiatus are also labeled. Diagram B offers a posterior view, showcasing the acetabulum, ischial tuberosity, and coccyx. The pelvic diaphragm is again labeled, including the same muscles as in Diagram A. Additional structures in Diagram B include the ischiocavernosus muscle, urogenital diaphragm, perineal body, superficial transverse perineal muscle, and various ligaments such as the sacrospinous, sacrotuberous, and anococcygeal. The obturator internus and piriformis muscles are shown cut in this view. Leader lines connect labels to the corresponding anatomical parts in both diagrams." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s9> .
<http://snomed.info/id/244962004> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#connects_to> <http://snomed.info/id/34402009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s9> .
