<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the pelvic floor, with various muscles and openings clearly marked. The rectal hiatus is positioned at the bottom center, while the vaginal canal is on the left side, and the urethral hiatus is above it. The pre-rectal fibers and puborectalis are located at the top center, with the puborectalis depicted as a horizontal band. The pubococcygeus is a large, fan-shaped structure on the right, and the iliococcygeus is a smaller, triangular structure below it. The coccygeus is at the very bottom, forming a small triangle. Each muscle is color-coded: puborectalis in green, pubococcygeus in yellow, iliococcygeus in pink, and coccygeus in purple." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s9> .
