<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed anatomical illustration of the peritoneal cavity. At the top of the image, the hepatic recesses are positioned towards the upper right side, near the liver, which is colored in darker pink. On the right side, the splenic recess is indicated near the spleen, shown in purple. The epiploic foramen is located on the left side, near the small intestine, depicted in green. In the center, the ligament sac is highlighted in blue, situated within the peritoneal cavity, surrounded by the mesentery. At the bottom right, the omental recess is labeled, pointing to the lower right side of the cavity. The peritoneum, a light pink membrane, lines the abdominal cavity and covers most of the abdominal organs, with the large intestine shown in yellow." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s2> .
