<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p86_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The top section of the image presents a detailed anatomical diagram of the abdominal and pelvic region, featuring the inferior vena cava, right and left kidneys, renal artery and vein, superior mesenteric artery, abdominal aorta, ureter, common iliac artery, external iliac artery and vein, ovary, uterus, internal iliac artery and vein, ovarian artery and vein, and inferior mesenteric artery. Leader lines connect these labels to the corresponding parts of the diagram, such as the renal arteries branching off from the abdominal aorta. The bottom section offers a cross-sectional view of the pelvic area, focusing on the blood vessels. It labels the ovarian artery, uterine artery, internal iliac artery, and vaginal arteries. The ovarian artery is highlighted in green, the uterine artery in yellow, the vaginal arteries in red, and the internal iliac artery in pink, branching into the other vessels. The cross-section also includes a depiction of the surrounding tissue and nerves in grayscale." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s2> .
