<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p28_b13> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed cross-sectional view of the skull base, with the cavernous sinus as the central focus. Various cranial nerves and related structures are labeled throughout the illustration. At the top left, a label points to the sixth cranial nerve (CN6) exiting the cavernous sinus through the superior orbital fissure. Near the lateral side, the label \"Cavernous sinus, lateral dural wall\" indicates its position. The first, second, and third divisions of the trigeminal nerve (CN5) are labeled in sequence below their respective divisions. The trigeminal ganglion is situated within the Meckel cave, and a label points this out. The sixth cranial nerve (CN6) is shown within the Dorello canal, and the diaphragma sellae is indicated at the top right. The pituitary gland, or hypophysis, is labeled near the center-right, alongside the internal carotid artery. The oculomotor nerve (CN3) is shown within a cistern, and the cisternal portions of the fourth and fifth cranial nerves (CN4 and CN5) are also labeled." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/a5a779648c68> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/56329008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s2> .
