<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/27398004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top of the diagram, the hypothalamus is positioned, featuring two labeled nuclei: the paraventricular nucleus and the supraoptic nucleus. A green line, representing the hypothalamo-hypophyseal tract, extends downward from the hypothalamus to the pituitary gland. Along this tract, three parts are labeled: cell body, axon, and terminal. Near the terminal, there is a label indicating that it releases a signal to stimulate release. The pituitary gland itself is shown with the posterior lobe at the bottom and the anterior lobe at the top. A blue line, representing a vein, extends from the pituitary gland toward the right side of the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s2> .
