<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/312535008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/244785008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a detailed anatomical illustration with the Styloloid Process labeled on the left side, pointing to an elongated structure extending from the skull. The Styloglossus muscle is shown in red, extending from the Styloloid Process to the base of the tongue. The Hyoglossus muscle, also in red, runs horizontally across the base of the tongue, connecting the hyoid bone to the tongue. The Genioglossus muscle is depicted in red, originating from the chin bone and extending to the base of the tongue. The Geniohyoideus muscle, shown in red, connects the chin bone to the hyoid bone. The Stylopharyngeus muscle is in red, extending from the Styloloid Process to the pharynx. The Hyoid Bone is labeled at the bottom center, pointing to a U-shaped bone below the larynx. The muscles are highlighted in red, while the rest of the image is in black and white, and the tongue is depicted semi-transparently, allowing the underlying muscles to be seen." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p6_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/49370004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The tongue is shown in a side view, with the top part colored pink to represent the general surface area. Four distinct colored regions are mapped on the tongue: blue at the top for bitter, yellow below for sour, green further down for salty, and red at the bottom for sweet. A legend is positioned to the right of the tongue diagram, listing the tastes associated with each color: blue for bitter, yellow for sour, green for salty, and red for sweet. The colors are distributed across the tongue in a way that suggests a mapping of taste sensitivity from top to bottom." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p24_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/71616004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/30305004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the muscles involved in tongue movement, highlighting their relationships with the bones and each other." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/80243003> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/246254000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p24_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A human skull is shown from the side, with muscles highlighted in shades of pink and red. The first muscle group is a large, fan-shaped muscle on the side of the head, extending from the lower part of the skull near the ear to the upper part, with a gradient from light pink at the base to darker pink at the top. Below this, a smaller muscle group is depicted in the jaw area, also in shades of pink and red, with a more compact shape. The muscles are shown with color gradients suggesting different layers or depths, and there are no labels, text, or arrows in the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/30206001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/263352000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/71616004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a detailed depiction of the muscles and structures associated with the tongue and throat. The stylomandibular process is positioned on the left side, near the ear, while the dorsum of the tongue is at the top. The styloglossus, hyoglossus, and genioglossus muscles are all shown in red, extending from their respective origins to the base of the tongue. The symphysis is located at the bottom right, indicating the lower jaw joint, and the hyoid bone is centered at the bottom, with the great cornu marked on its left side. The stylopharyngeus muscle is also depicted in red, extending from the stylomandibular process down to the pharynx. The background provides a simplified outline of the head and neck, with the tongue and other structures shaded in white, presenting a cross-sectional view that highlights the relationships between the muscles and bones involved in tongue movement." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/72914001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the human tongue, highlighting various anatomical structures and papillae types." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is composed of three photographs and a central circular diagram. The top-left photograph shows a close-up of a person biting into a slice of pizza against an outdoor green background. To the top-right, another photograph captures a person holding and biting a hamburger, set against a plain white background. At the bottom, a third photograph displays a person in a white shirt and dark tie holding a green apple, also with a plain white background. The central circular diagram is divided into three sections labeled 1, 2, and 3. Section 1 is on the left, Section 2 is on the right, and Section 3 is at the bottom. Arrows connect these sections, forming a continuous loop." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p6_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the head and neck muscles, with labels strategically placed to identify each muscle. The epicranial aponeurosis is positioned at the top of the head, while the frontal belly of the occipitofrontalis is shown on the forehead. The corrugator supercilii is located above the eye, and the orbicularis oculi surrounds the eye. Near the nose, the procerus is depicted, and below the nose, the nasalis is visible. The levator labii superioris is situated above the upper lip, and the zygomaticus minor and major are shown below the eye. The orbicularis oris is around the mouth, and the mentalis is below the chin. The depressor labii inferioris is placed below the lower lip, and the depressor anguli oris is at the corner of the mouth. The temporoparietalis is shown cut and reflected on the side of the head, revealing underlying structures, and the temporalis is also on the side of the head." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p24_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/89546000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A diagram of an anatomical structure, possibly related to the eye, with labeled parts resembling ocular features." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/52738005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/48477009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p6_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the muscles of the head and neck from a lateral view, with labels indicating specific anatomical structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/244784007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p6_b4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A close-up view of an eye with the eyelid partially closed, focusing on the palpebral part." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p6_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/71616004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/71616004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents the human tongue with the epiglottis at the top, pointing towards the upper center. Near the top-center, slightly to the left, are the lingual follicles. A red arrow marks the foramen cecum as a small, circular opening near the center of the tongue. Above the palatine tonsil, a red arrow indicates the palatopharyngeal arch, which appears as a fold or arch. The palatine tonsil is situated near the center of the tongue, slightly to the right. A red arrow points to the palatoglossus muscle on the side of the tongue, near the palatine tonsil. Another red arrow highlights the sulcus terminalis, a groove on the tongue's surface, located below the palatine tonsil. The sections labeled \"Papillae\" include vallate papillae in the center, forming a V-shape, foliate papillae along the sides, long filiform papillae distributed across the surface, conical papillae among the long filiform papillae, and fungiform papillae scattered across the surface, appearing rounded and mushroom-like. The tongue's overall shape is oval, with a slightly raised central area and a flatter outer edge, using shading and color to differentiate structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/113192009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p6_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/774007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/21974007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a top-down view of the human mouth and throat, with the superior lip positioned at the top and the inferior lip at the bottom. The gingivae are shown along the inner edges of the upper and lower teeth, while the superior and inferior labial frenula are depicted between the lips and the gums. The tongue is prominently displayed in the center, with the lingual frenulum connecting it to the floor of the mouth. The sublingual gland is positioned beneath the tongue, and the duct of the submandibular gland is shown leading from it. The palatoglossal and palato-pharyngeal arches are illustrated on the sides of the tongue and throat, respectively, with the palatine tonsils situated near the back of the mouth. The posterior wall of the oropharynx is visible at the back. The vestibule, the space between the lips and teeth, is also depicted. The diagram uses color-coding, with the tongue in orange, the gums and lips in pink, and other tissues in shades of red and orange." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p24_b12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/81745001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/113279002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
