<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image zooms in on the area just below the eyebrow and around the eye, with the eyelashes visible along the lower edge of the eyelid. The skin around the eye is light-colored, and the eyebrow is visible above the eye. The label \"Palpebral part\" is positioned in black text at the top of the image, centrally located but not directly connected to any specific part of the eye. The background has a textured appearance, suggesting a fabric or paper surface." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A diagram of the tongue showing different regions colored to represent taste buds sensitive to bitter, sour, salty, and sweet tastes." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the muscles and structures related to the tongue and throat, including the stylomandibular process, dorsum of the tongue, styloglossus, hyoglossus, genioglossus, symphysis, hyoid bone, great cornu, and stylopharyngeus." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/81745001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomical structures of the human mouth and throat, including the lips, gums, palate, tongue, and associated glands and arches." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/4442007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
