<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a circular structure with concentric layers, suggesting a cross-section of an organ or biological structure. The layers are shaded with horizontal lines, indicating different tissue layers or compartments. A central area with a lighter color might represent a cavity or specific region within the structure. Near the center, a small, elongated shape extends towards the right side of the image, potentially representing a canal, duct, or another anatomical feature. The structure is surrounded by a darker outline, which may indicate the boundary of the organ or structure being depicted. The labels \"O\" are positioned at the top and bottom of the structure, while the label \"P\" is located in the middle, slightly below the center. The image also includes a label \"(A)\" in the bottom left corner, suggesting it is part of a series or set of images." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/123851003> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s6> .
