<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with a variety of cells and structures. Nuclei are stained dark purple, while the cytoplasm and muscle fibers are lighter pink. Larger, rounded structures resembling muscle fibers have a pale pinkish hue with a darker outline. Two labels, \"1\" and \"2,\" are circled with arrows pointing to specific areas within the tissue, highlighting particular cells or structures of interest. The labeled areas are scattered throughout the image, with arrows directing attention to these regions." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s10> .
