<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into two parts, labeled \"a\" and \"b\". In part a, a cross-sectional view of the pituitary gland is shown, with the anterior lobe colored purple at the bottom and the posterior lobe in pink at the top. In part b, a more detailed diagram is presented, with the hypothalamus at the top, featuring the paraventricular nucleus and supraoptic nucleus. Yellow lines connect these nuclei to the median eminence, which in turn leads to the infundibulum. The pituitary gland itself is divided into the pars nervosa at the top, the pars intermedia in the middle, and the pars distalis at the bottom. Leader lines point out additional structures such as the mamillary body and optic chiasma." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s3> .
