<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed microscopic view of the pituitary gland, with labels pointing to different structures via black lines or arrows. Basophils and acidophils, both indicated by their pinkish coloration, are found within the gland. Capillaries and blood vessels are depicted as thin, elongated structures scattered throughout the gland. The pars distalis is located towards the bottom left, while the infundibulum, a stalk-like structure, extends upwards from the gland. The pars tuberalis is situated at the top right, and the pars nervosa is at the bottom right. The pars intermedia, located centrally and slightly to the right, contains large, irregularly shaped colloid vesicles. The labels are aligned vertically on the right-hand side of the image, corresponding to the numbered parts." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/9941e152b586> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s3> .
