<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/6baa9800a605> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/62818001> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section of the pituitary gland, with the three main parts labeled: Pars distalis, Pars intermedia, and Pars nervosa. Sinusoidal capillaries are depicted as irregularly shaped, thin-walled blood vessels with a pinkish hue in the Pars distalis. Chromophobe cells, scattered throughout the Pars distalis and Pars intermedia, have a pale cytoplasm and are less densely stained compared to other cell types. Acidophils, found in the Pars distalis, are characterized by a more intensely stained, darker pink cytoplasm. Nuclei of pituicytes are elongated and aligned along the nerve fibers in the Pars nervosa. Follicles in the Pars intermedia are oval-shaped with a central lumen filled with a pinkish substance. The labels for the three parts of the pituitary gland are positioned above the corresponding regions of the tissue section, with leader lines connecting them to specific areas in the image." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p28_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure shows a histological section of the pituitary gland, highlighting its three main parts: Pars distalis, Pars intermedia, and Pars nervosa." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s3> .
