<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the hypothalamus at the top, depicted as a pink brain-like structure with a blue outline. Below the hypothalamus, GnRH is positioned, with a blue arrow pointing downward from the hypothalamus, indicating the release of GnRH. The pituitary gland is shown as a light blue box directly below GnRH, with two arrows coming from GnRH: one labeled with a plus sign for stimulation and another with a minus sign for inhibition. Below the pituitary, two arrows labeled FSH and LH point downward. The testes are located on the left side of the diagram, and the ovaries are on the right, both represented by light blue boxes. Arrows from FSH and LH point to the testes and ovaries, indicating stimulation. Androgens are connected to the testes on the left, and estrogens are connected to the ovaries on the right. Both androgens and estrogens have arrows pointing back to the hypothalamus, indicating feedback loops. A dashed arrow labeled with a minus sign points from the hypothalamus to the left side, suggesting a negative feedback loop." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s11> .
