<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p117_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a dense arrangement of cellular structures, with acinar cells forming clusters and centroacinar cells interspersed among them. Intercalated ducts are narrow and elongated, connecting the acini to larger ducts. A centrally located blood vessel, appearing as a circular structure with a lumen, is surrounded by these structures. Arrows point to specific areas within the tissue, labeling acinar cells, centroacinar cells, intercalated ducts, and the blood vessel." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
