<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized from top to bottom, starting with the \"Ingest\" label at the top left, pointing to the mouth, where it indicates \"1,200 mL water\" and \"800 g food.\" To the right of the mouth, an arrow points to the saliva glands, labeled \"Saliva 1,500 mL pH 6.8–7.0.\" Below the mouth, the esophagus leads down to the stomach, labeled with \"Gastric secretions 2,000 mL pH 1.5–3.0.\" To the right of the stomach, the liver and gallbladder are depicted, with the gallbladder connected to the small intestine via the bile duct, labeled \"Bile 500 mL pH 7.8–8.0.\" Below the liver and gallbladder, the pancreas is shown, connected to the small intestine, labeled \"Pancreatic secretions 1,500 mL pH 8.0–8.4.\" The small intestine is positioned below the pancreas, labeled \"Small intestine absorbs 8,500 mL.\" The large intestine is shown below the small intestine, labeled \"Large intestine absorbs 400 mL.\" At the bottom of the diagram, the \"Excreted\" label appears." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
