<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/3860a4f8e726> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p111_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is a rectangular cross-section of the intestinal wall, with labels distributed across different sections. At the top left, the simple columnar epithelium is labeled, pointing to tall, column-shaped cells. Below it, the lamina propria is labeled, indicating a pinkish area with small blood vessels and connective tissue. In the middle section, diverticula or crypts are labeled, pointing to small, blind-ended pouches. Near the bottom left, elastic fibers and nerves are labeled, showing wavy structures and nerve fibers within the lamina propria. Connective tissue is labeled at the very bottom left, pointing to a dense, fibrous layer. At the top right, mucosal folds are labeled, indicating ridges on the tissue surface, with diverticula or crypts labeled again in this area. Venule and arteriole are positioned near the top right, pointing to small blood vessels. Smooth muscle fibers are labeled at the bottom right, showing layers within the intestinal wall. Artery and vein are near the bottom right, pointing to larger blood vessels. Serosa is labeled at the very bottom right, indicating the outermost layer." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/b926b440ecf1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/86355000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
