<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p111_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed cross-sectional diagram of intestinal tissue, illustrating various layers and structures such as the simple columnar epithelium, lamina propria, diverticula, elastic fibers, nerves, connective tissue, mucosal folds, venule and arteriole, smooth muscle fibers, artery and vein, and serosa." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the digestive process in humans, showing the flow of ingested substances through various organs and the amount absorbed or excreted at different stages." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/36f81b57084f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/298225002> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p80_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a liver cell with distinct organelles and structures. At the top, the sinusoidal lining cell is depicted as a yellowish region with small protrusions, forming the outer boundary. Near the top right, an erythrocyte in the hepatic sinusoid is shown as a red, oval-shaped structure. On the left, a large, rod-like structure with a dark interior represents the mitochondrion. Below it, the smooth ER is illustrated as a series of interconnected, flattened sacs with a smooth surface. The rough ER, positioned below the smooth ER, is shown as similar sacs but with a rough surface due to ribosomes. To the right, the Golgi complex is a stack of flattened, membrane-bound sacs. Adjacent to it, the bile canaliculus is a small, tubular structure. The Space of Disse is depicted as a light-colored space on the left, between the sinusoidal lining cells and the hepatocyte." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s9> .
