<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p47_b13> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a microscopic view labeled \"LM 100x\" in the bottom right corner. On the left side, an arrow points to a thin, elongated structure filled with red blood cells, labeled as a capillary. Near the middle-left, an arrow indicates a cell with a large, round nucleus and a prominent nucleolus, labeled as a chief cell. At the bottom-left, another label points to cells with dense, granular cytoplasm, identified as oxyphil cells. The cells are distributed throughout the field, with variations in size and staining characteristics, suggesting a stained slide, likely using hematoxylin and eosin (H&E), which highlights the nuclei in blue/purple and the cytoplasm in pink/white." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/29a2b2d380ad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/1895> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
