<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p48_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the regulation of calcium levels in the body through the parathyroid hormone (PTH), showing the flow of calcium ions and PTH molecules among the parathyroid gland, bloodstream, bone, kidney, and intestine." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/29a2b2d380ad> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/691f8618820b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/1894> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is divided into two sections. On the left, the term \"Normoparathyroidism\" is positioned at the top, followed by an illustration of a thyroid gland with four distinct lobes, all colored orange. A leader line extends from the thyroid gland to the text \"Surgical Resection,\" which is placed below the illustration. Another leader line points downward to a box listing \"Normocalcaemia,\" \"Normophosphataemia,\" and \"Normal PTH levels.\" On the right, the layout mirrors the left side, with \"Hypoparathyroidism\" at the top and an identical illustration of the thyroid gland. The leader line again points to \"Surgical Resection,\" and a box below lists \"Hypocalcaemia,\" \"Hyperphosphataemia,\" and \"Low/absent PTH levels.\" Both thyroid illustrations are the same in shape and color, and the surgical resection is indicated by a scalpel icon." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/73514614d6d1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#stimulates> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
