<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure compares the conditions of Normoparathyroidism and Hypoparathyroidism, illustrating the effects of surgical resection on calcium and phosphorus levels and PTH levels in each condition." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/ea04a860eee4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p78_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a network of blue lines forming a web-like pattern at the top left, representing the pampiniform plexus. A prominent red line runs vertically along the right side of the testicle, indicating the testicular artery. Another red line, slightly more curved, runs alongside it, marking the deferential artery. A smaller, more delicate red line branches off from the deferential artery at the bottom right, representing the cremasteric artery. The testicle is depicted as an oval shape with a network of smaller red lines inside, symbolizing the branches of the testicular artery." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/85efef0563ff> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/691f8618820b> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p47_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The connective tissue capsule of the parathyroid gland is positioned at the outer boundary, appearing as a thin, continuous band encircling the gland. Oxyphil cells are scattered throughout the glandular tissue, with a darker, more granular cytoplasm compared to the other cells. Each of these elements is labeled with a leader line pointing to specific instances within the tissue." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/29a2b2d380ad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#stimulates> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
