<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A red, exposed area of tissue is visible, indicating a surgical incision. A metallic instrument with a pointed tip is inserted into the incision, pointing towards the center. Another metallic instrument, possibly a scalpel or forceps, is partially visible on the right side. Two hands wearing surgical gloves are visible at the top, holding the edges of the tissue. The tissue appears inflamed and reddened. A black arrow points from the left side towards the center of the incision." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s12> .
