<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p53_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features the human lymphatic system with various organs and structures labeled. The right lymphatic duct is shown entering a vein in the thoracic cavity. Lymph nodes are scattered throughout the body, connected by lymph vessels. The thymus is located in the upper chest, behind the sternum, and the spleen is in the upper left abdomen, below the diaphragm. Bone marrow is depicted within the lower left leg's bone structure. Lymph vessels are represented by a network of thin green lines, and the organs are colored in shades of pink, red, and gray. The diagram includes a zoomed-in view of the thymus and a detailed cross-section of a lymph node, showcasing the internal composition with clusters of cells." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p51_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is composed of three diagrams. Diagram A is positioned at the top left and offers a side view of the thoracic cavity, where the thyroid gland is situated at the top with its tubular structure extending downward. Below the thyroid gland, the trachea is slightly curved to the right, and the lungs are displayed on either side, with the right lung appearing larger. Diagram B is located at the top right and provides a close-up of the thymus gland, showing it divided into two lobes: the right lobe and the left lobe. Within each lobe, smaller structures labeled as \"Septae\" and \"Lobule\" are visible. Diagram C is at the bottom and presents a detailed cross-sectional view of the thoracic region, with the thymus at the center. The lower horns of the thymus extend downward, and various anatomical structures are labeled around it, including the superior vena cava, right subclavian vein, right internal mammary artery, right internal mammary vein, left brachiocephalic vein, left subclavian vein, left internal mammary artery, left internal mammary vein, left phrenic nerve, and pericardial fat with ectopic thymic tissues. Leader lines connect each label to the corresponding structure in the diagram." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s13> .
