<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top of the image, a large, cylindrical structure colored blue represents the trachea. Extending downward from it are two blue branches, signifying the right and left primary bronchi. From these primary bronchi, smaller branches, also in blue, spread out further, depicting the secondary bronchi. At the bottom of the diagram, the smallest branches, colored light brown, represent the bronchioles. The image lacks labels or text, presenting a straightforward visual representation without additional annotations or arrows." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s13> .
