<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/a92943855a80> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/260642009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s13> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large, reddish-brown liver is positioned at the top left of the image, above the stomach. Near the bottom left of the liver, a green, teardrop-shaped gallbladder is connected to the common bile duct. The common bile duct, a green tube, extends towards the pancreas. The pancreas, an elongated yellowish-brown organ, is situated below the stomach and behind the duodenum. A yellowish-brown pancreatic duct runs along the pancreas. The stomach, a pink, rounded organ, is in the middle right of the image, below the liver and above the duodenum. The duodenum, a pink, curved section, is located below the stomach and connects to the small intestine. The small intestine, a pink, coiled section, is positioned below the duodenum. A small, circular area where the common bile duct and pancreatic duct join is labeled \"Ampulla of Vater.\" A thin, white esophagus is seen at the top of the image, connecting the mouth to the stomach. Each label is accompanied by a black arrow pointing to the corresponding anatomical structure. The overall layout shows the organs in a cross-sectional view, with the liver and gallbladder on the left, the stomach and pancreas in the center, and the small intestine on the right." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s13> .
