<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration is divided into two sections: one for a newborn and one for an adult. In the newborn section, the thymus is shown as a reddish-brown organ situated above the heart. The thyroid gland is positioned at the top of the neck, with the trachea visible just below it. The lungs are depicted on either side of the heart, which is centrally located. The diaphragm is shown beneath the heart and lungs, and the liver is positioned at the bottom right. In the adult section, the thymus appears as a smaller, lighter-colored organ above the heart, with the same surrounding organs labeled as in the newborn section. Each organ is labeled with a black line pointing to its location, including \"Thyroid,\" \"Trachea,\" \"Thymus,\" \"Lung,\" \"Heart,\" \"Diaphragm,\" and \"Liver.\"" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s13> .
