<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into four quadrants labeled A, B, C, and D. In quadrant A, a 3D rendering of a human neck is displayed from the front view, with the neck slightly tilted upward and three orange arrows pointing downward toward the lower part of the neck. Quadrant B shows a cross-sectional CT scan of the neck oriented horizontally, with two white arrows pointing to a darker region within the scan. In quadrant C, a 3D model of a bone structure, likely the hyoid bone, is presented in an anterior view, with two white arrows highlighting the upper ends of the bone. Finally, quadrant D features a photograph of a dissected anatomical specimen, probably a hyoid bone, on a green background with a ruler for scale, and two white arrows pointing to the upper ends of the specimen." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s1> .
