<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b18> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a detailed anatomical illustration of the neck muscles, with different colors used to distinguish muscle groups. A yellow box on the left lists the triangular regions: submental, submandibular, carotid, and muscular triangles. The muscular triangle is highlighted with a yellow box at the bottom left, while the submental triangle has a purple box at the top left. The carotid triangle is marked with a dashed box at the top right. Specific muscles are labeled: the anterior and posterior bellies of the digastric muscle, the digastric triangle between them, the carotid triangle, the sternocleidomastoid muscle, and the superior and inferior bellies of the omohyoid muscle. The submandibular triangle is not explicitly labeled but can be inferred from the surrounding muscles. The layout is a cross-sectional view, with labels and boxes strategically placed to identify areas of interest." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s1> .
