<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p120_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into four quadrants, each highlighting different structures within pancreatic tissue. In the top-left quadrant, an intercalated duct is labeled, pointing to a small duct-like structure. The bottom-left quadrant features endocrine cells of the pancreatic islet and capillaries, with arrows indicating cells within a cluster and small blood vessels, respectively. The top-right quadrant showcases centroacinar cells in serous acinus and a connective tissue capsule, with the cells marked within the acini and the connective tissue layer surrounding it. In the bottom-right quadrant, additional centroacinar cells in serous acinus are labeled, also pointing to cells within the acini. The tissue is stained, using different colors to distinguish various cell types and structures, presenting a clear cross-section of the pancreas." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s8> .
