<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p113_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into three sections labeled (a), (b), and (c). In section (a), the pancreas is depicted in a cross-sectional diagram within the human body, with labels for the head, body, and tail of the pancreas, as well as the common bile duct, accessory pancreatic duct, duodenum, and duodenal papilla. Leader lines connect these labels to specific parts of the pancreas. This section also labels the ducts and connective tissue septum, with leader lines pointing to the corresponding structures. Section (c) offers a higher magnification microscopic image of the pancreas, focusing on the pancreatic islet (endocrine) and pancreatic acini (exocrine). Leader lines in this section point to these areas, and a scale bar is present indicating \"LM × 75,\" suggesting a magnification of 75 times the actual size." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s8> .
