<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p120_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The intercalated duct is situated at the top left corner of the image, appearing as a small, tubular structure with a lumen. Centrally in the upper portion, the connective tissue capsule is visible as a network of fibrous tissue surrounding the pancreatic islets and acinar cells. Centroacinar cells are distributed throughout the lower half, larger than the acinar cells with more prominent nuclei, positioned near the intercalated ducts. The labels are on the left side, pointing to these structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s8> .
