<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p82_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the female reproductive system, with labels pointing to specific anatomical structures. At the top right, the Mesosalpinx is indicated near the upper part of the uterine tube. Near the top middle, the Mesovarium is shown adjacent to the ovary area. The Ovarian Artery is positioned slightly below the Mesovarium, directing attention to the blood vessel that supplies the ovary. Directly below this, the Ovarian Vein is marked, pointing to the vein that drains the ovary. Centrally positioned, the Uterine Tube is labeled, pointing to the fallopian tube. The Ovary is situated in the middle of the diagram, with the Broad Ligament extending from it down to the uterus. The Round Ligament is depicted curving from the ovary to the lower abdomen. The Ovarian Ligament is shown as a small structure connecting the ovary to the uterus. The Vagina is labeled at the bottom, pointing to the vaginal canal." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p76_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/87644002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/a958528b04de> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/386045008> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/c46af5c1ff28> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/6384> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/901994dc4bcf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/10379> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p78_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the male reproductive system, with the internal iliac artery and vein positioned at the top left, depicted as large red and blue vessels branching off. The deferential artery and vein extend downward and slightly to the right from these. Near the middle left, the inferior epigastric vessels and external spermatic vessels are shown branching off. The testis is located at the bottom left, with its surface texture and shape clearly depicted. Surrounding the testis, the cremaster muscle and internal spermatic fascia are labeled near the middle right. Within the testis, the testicular arteries and venous plexus are represented by networks of small red and blue vessels, respectively. The deferential artery and vein are also shown extending upward and to the right from the testis. The vas deferens, a tube-like structure, extends from the testis, with a branch to the epididymis and the coiled epididymis itself labeled nearby." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
