<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p77_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The testis is positioned at the bottom right of the image, appearing as a round, pinkish structure with a network of smaller branches inside, representing the seminiferous tubules. The tunica albuginea is depicted as a thin white boundary around the testis. Above the testis, the epididymis extends upwards and slightly to the left, with its head, body, and tail clearly labeled. The vas deferens is a long, coiled tube that starts from the epididymis and extends upwards and to the left, with the pampiniform plexus shown surrounding it. Additional labels include \"efferent ductules\" near the head of the epididymis, \"septa\" within the epididymis, and \"lobules\" within the testis. The overall layout reveals the testis in cross-section, while the epididymis and vas deferens are depicted in a three-dimensional manner, highlighting their coiled nature. Leader lines connect the labels to the corresponding structures in the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
