<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b13> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the male pelvic region, with the pelvic bones forming the outer boundary of the pelvic cavity. The bladder, rectum, and prostate gland are clearly visible within this space. At the top right, the pelvic parasympathetic roots are labeled, indicating a network of nerves extending from the sacral region into the pelvic area. The obturator nerve is shown running through the obturator foramen near the left side, pointing to the lower part of the pelvic cavity. The hypogastric nerves are labeled in the middle-left section, near the bladder and prostate gland. The rectum is depicted as a tube-like structure in the central part of the image. The prostate gland is shown as a small, oval-shaped structure below the bladder. The dorsal nerve is labeled at the bottom left, near the penis. The pudendal nerve is labeled in the lower right section, pointing to the area near the anus and penis. The cavernous nerve is also labeled in the lower right section, near the penis. The posterior scrotal nerve is labeled in the lower right section, pointing to the scrotal area." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/66124a93dc38> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
