<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/4100> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#stimulates> <http://snomed.info/id/35039007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p76_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The testis is depicted as a large, oval-shaped organ with a smooth surface. At the top of the testis, a network of intertwined red lines represents the testicular blood supply. The caput epididymis is shown as a small, rounded area at the top of the testis, with the straight portion of the vas deferens extending vertically from it. The corpus epididymis is illustrated as a series of loops and curves, while the convoluted vas is tightly coiled tubes extending from the corpus epididymis." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s15> .
