<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p89_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features bile canaliculi as thin, green, branching structures that extend throughout the liver tissue. Bile canals of Hering are also thin, green, branching structures, connecting the bile canaliculi to the bile ductules. Cholangiocytes are elongated, columnar cells with nuclei at the base, lining the bile ductules. The bile ductule is a larger, oval-shaped structure containing cholangiocytes. Leader lines from the bottom left corner indicate the locations of bile canaliculi, hepatocytes, and bile canals of Hering, while leader lines from the bottom right corner point to cholangiocytes and the bile ductule." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
