<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p92_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section of liver tissue stained with hematoxylin and eosin, featuring a portal triad with labeled structures including the bile duct, intrahepatic bile ductule, hepatic artery, periportal space, portal vein, and portal canal." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/8cdcd4809451> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/42a643e52ea2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p82_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a microscopic cross-section of liver tissue, with various structures labeled for identification. On the left side, an interlobular septum appears as a thin, fibrous layer, and another instance is seen at the bottom left. Central to the image is the portal vein, a larger blood vessel branching into smaller tributaries. Hepatic arteries, appearing as smaller blood vessels, branch out from the central vein area. Blood cells are scattered throughout the sinusoids, which are the spaces between these plates of hepatic cells. The central vein, a large vessel, is situated towards the right side, surrounded by the plates of hepatic cells." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p82_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed microscopic view of liver tissue, highlighting its internal structure and various components involved in its function." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p103_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/262151005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/16f98c05f73a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/38848004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p89_b7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p94_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/70150004> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/0c515b2289f1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p103_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a liver cell with the endothelial cell positioned at the top left, forming the outermost layer around the sinusoid. Within the cytoplasm, the smooth endoplasmic reticulum appears as a network of tubular structures extending from the endothelial cell toward the center. Collagen fibers are scattered throughout the cytoplasm as long, thin, white strands. The lumen of the hepatic sinusoid is labeled at the bottom left and right, representing the area where blood flows. The Golgi apparatus is located near the center, appearing as a stack of flattened, membrane-bound sacs. Lipid droplets are depicted as yellow, spherical structures, particularly near the Golgi apparatus. The Ito cell is labeled near the center-right, involved in lipid metabolism. Mitochondria are small, rod-shaped organelles scattered throughout the cytoplasm. Glycogen is shown as a granular structure near the bottom left, indicating carbohydrate storage. The bile canaliculus is represented by small, branching channels at the bottom left, connecting to the space of Disse. The zonula occludens is a band-like structure at the bottom center, signifying tight junctions between hepatocytes. The space of Disse is the area between hepatocytes, labeled at the bottom center, where bile canaliculi are located. Red blood cells are also depicted within the lumen of the hepatic sinusoid, indicating blood flow through this region." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/d40238842645> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
