<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p88_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is laid out horizontally, with hepatocytes scattered throughout, forming a network. The bile canals of Hering are depicted as thin, green, branching structures extending from the hepatocytes towards the bile ductule. Cholangiocytes, the cells lining the bile ductules, are shown as elongated, columnar cells with nuclei positioned at the base. The bile ductule is a wider, curved structure filled with bile, positioned distinctly on the right side of the image. Leader lines point to the bile canals of Hering, the cholangiocytes, and the bile ductule, indicating their respective labels." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
