<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p106_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features several hexagonal shapes connected at their vertices, with pink outlines. At the center, a blue hexagon is shaded and includes two labels: \"central vein,\" pointing to a small dot near the center, and \"portal canals,\" pointing to a dashed line encircling the hexagon. The surrounding white hexagons form a network-like structure around the central blue hexagon." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
