<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p92_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The histological section displays a portal triad within liver tissue. The bile duct is positioned on the left side of the image, appearing as a circular structure with a darker lumen. Below the bile duct is the intrahepatic bile ductule, which is smaller and also circular, with a lighter lumen. The hepatic artery is a thin, elongated structure located above the bile duct, pointing towards the center-right of the image. Surrounding these structures is the periportal space, which appears as a lighter region with scattered cells. At the bottom of the image, the portal vein is a large, oval-shaped structure, surrounded by the other components. The portal canal encompasses the area surrounding the portal vein, bile duct, and hepatic artery. The liver parenchyma is composed of densely packed cells with dark blue nuclei, and the overall coloration is pinkish due to the staining." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
