<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p81_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed view of liver tissue, with the central vein positioned at the center, marked by a white circular area. The spaces between these plates are the irregularly shaped, lighter-colored areas known as hepatic sinusoids. The portal area, which surrounds the central vein, contains the bile duct, hepatic artery, and portal vein, all depicted in blue branching out from the central vein. The image is divided into two main sections, both labeled \"Portal area,\" one on the left and one on the right, each highlighting the components of the portal triad." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
