<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p95_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section of liver tissue with a portal triad at the center. At the top, the periportal space surrounds the central vein and extends into the liver parenchyma. The bile duct is positioned on the left side, branching off from the central bile ductule. The intrahepatic bile ductule is situated below the bile duct in the lower part of the image. The portal vein is at the bottom of the portal triad, adjacent to the bile duct and hepatic artery. The surrounding tissue, composed of hepatocytes, appears as dark blue nuclei scattered throughout pink-stained cytoplasm, typical of H&E staining." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p92_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/362193005> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s7> .
