<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a side view of a human head, with the skull partially removed to expose the underlying muscle structures. The muscles are labeled with text and arrows pointing to specific areas. The frontalis muscle is positioned at the top of the head, above the eyebrows, while the corrugator is near the inner corners of the eyebrows. The risorius is positioned on either side of the mouth, near the corners, while the masseter is on the sides of the jaw, below the eye sockets. The depressor labii is below the lower lip, and the depressor anguli oris is near the corners of the mouth. The labels are written in various colors—green, blue, red, pink, and orange—and are connected to the corresponding muscle regions by lines or arrows. The overall layout highlights the muscles in a three-dimensional perspective, showing their arrangement and location within the face." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a profile view of the head, with labels pointing to specific facial muscles. The frontalis is situated at the top, indicating the forehead area. Near the eyebrows, the corrugator is marked, pointing to the region above the eyes. Below the corrugator, the nasalis is located, highlighting the area around the nose. The orbicularis oculi is shown around the eye, emphasizing the circular muscle in that region. Each label is connected by a leader line or arrow to the corresponding muscle on the head. The image is labeled \"anatomical head in profile\" in the top-left corner." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s3> .
