<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a table with three columns and four rows, each column dedicated to a different muscle group: Compressor nares, Dilator nares, and Procerus. The header row labels these columns, and the subsequent rows provide information about the origin, insertion, and action of each muscle. At the bottom left corner, a small diagram illustrates a section of the face, with a label pointing to the Procerus muscle area above the nose, near the bridge, highlighting its location in a cross-section view of the facial muscles." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s3> .
