<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration focuses on the facial nerve pathway, with the facial nerve entering the skull through the stylomastoid foramen and traveling through the petrotympanic fissure into the middle ear cavity. The submandibular gland is shown beneath the mandible, and the sublingual gland is situated below it. Blue arrows point to the geniculate ganglion, stylomastoid foramen, and superior salivatory nucleus. Dashed lines indicate the parasympathetic pathway connecting the superior salivatory nucleus to the submandibular ganglion, while red dashed lines indicate the sympathetic pathway connecting the superior cervical ganglion to the submandibular ganglion. Various text labels are placed near the corresponding anatomical structures, including \"geniculate ganglion of Facial nerve,\" \"superior salivatory nucleus,\" \"stylomastoid foramen,\" \"petrotympanic fissure,\" \"sup. cervical ganglion,\" \"lingual/ facial a.,\" \"submandibular gland,\" and \"submandibular ganglion.\"" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/362884007> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s3> .
