<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/fbeb8bddb6e9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/32849002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration is presented in a side view, with a detailed cross-section of the throat and esophagus on the left side. The esophagus is depicted as a long, tube-like structure extending from the throat down to the stomach. The throat, or pharynx, is shown as a narrow passage at the top of the esophagus. The upper esophageal sphincter is a circular muscle ring located at the top of the esophagus, near the throat. The trachea is illustrated as a tube branching off from the throat, leading downward. The lower esophageal sphincter is another circular muscle ring situated at the bottom of the esophagus, near the stomach. The diaphragm is portrayed as a large, dome-shaped muscle that separates the chest cavity from the abdominal cavity. The stomach is shown as a large, sac-like organ at the end of the esophagus. The background of the diagram is a light blue gradient, and the internal structures are depicted in shades of pink and red." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/5e38a9926f8a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/89187006> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p42_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the thoracic region's blood vessels and surrounding structures, including the aorta and its branches, the esophagus, and related organs." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
