<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the internal structures within the thoracic and abdominal cavities. The trachea is labeled at the top left, positioned as a central tube-like structure running vertically through the chest. The arch of the aorta is labeled at the top right, depicted as a curved section arching over the trachea and esophagus. The thoracic esophagus is also labeled at the top right, showing the segment of the esophagus that passes through the thoracic cavity. The right crus of the diaphragm is labeled at the bottom left, illustrating a muscular structure on the right side of the spine. The abdominal esophagus is labeled at the bottom right, indicating the lower portion of the esophagus that extends into the abdomen. The aorta is labeled at the bottom right, shown as a large blood vessel running alongside the spine in the abdominal region. The ribs are visible, forming the bony framework of the chest, and the diaphragm is depicted as a dome-shaped muscle separating the thoracic and abdominal cavities." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
