<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the thoracic cavity, with the esophagus positioned at the top center, running vertically through the middle of the chest. Above the esophagus, the trachea is depicted as a slightly wider tube-like structure. On the left side, the left common carotid artery and the left subclavian artery are shown branching off from the arch of the aorta, alongside the brachiocephalic trunk. On the right, the right main bronchus branches off from the trachea, while the left main bronchus is positioned on the left. The arch of the aorta is located at the top center, with the thoracic aorta extending downward below it. At the bottom center, the dome-shaped diaphragm is visible, separating the thoracic cavity from the abdominal cavity. The ribcage is labeled, and the spine is visible at the bottom. Muscles and other soft tissues are depicted in shades of pink, while the bones are shown in white. The layout is symmetrical, with corresponding structures on the left and right sides." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
