<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p30_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The diagram illustrates the blood supply to the thyroid gland and surrounding structures, including the inferior thyroid artery, thyrocerical trunk, subclavian artery, and various bronchial arteries branching from the descending thoracic aorta." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/1a997bc7932b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the thoracic cavity, with the thoracic duct positioned on the left side of the spine, extending from the upper chest down to the abdomen. Paratracheal nodes are situated along the trachea, just above the carina, while the superior and inferior tracheobronchial nodes are around the trachea and bronchi. Posterior parietal nodes are positioned along the posterior wall of the thoracic cavity, and the superior phrenic nodes are near the diaphragm, above the phrenic nerve. The left gastric nodes are situated near the stomach, particularly around the cardiac region, and the juxtaesophageal and superior phrenic nodes are close to the esophagus and above the phrenic nerve. Each structure is clearly labeled with leader lines or arrows pointing to the corresponding anatomical feature, providing a clear spatial arrangement within the thoracic cavity." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s9> .
