<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a clear layout of the arterial system, with the main trunk positioned at the top and branching out into several smaller arteries. The IMA is shown branching off to the right side of the main trunk, while the SRA is depicted as a distinct section of the artery. The internal iliac artery is a prominent branch that splits into smaller branches, including the middle rectal artery and the inferior rectal artery, which are positioned at the bottom of the diagram. The shapes are smooth and tubular, representing the blood vessels, and the spatial arrangement shows branches extending downward and to the sides." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s4> .
