<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a side view of the anal canal, which is illustrated as a vertical tube-like structure at the center-right of the image. Surrounding the anal canal, the internal anal sphincter is depicted in green and positioned closer to the canal. The external anal sphincter is shown in blue, forming the outermost layer around the internal sphincter. Black arrows point to each labeled part: the anal canal, the internal anal sphincter, and the external anal sphincter. The internal anal sphincter is located lower-left, while the external anal sphincter is indicated lower-right. The diagram is credited to \"TeachMeAnatomy,\" as shown by the logo and text at the bottom right corner." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s4> .
