<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p42_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the rectum and its surrounding structures. At the top left, the superior rectal artery, a branch of the IMA, is labeled in red. The inferior rectal artery, a branch of the internal pudendal artery, is positioned at the bottom right, also in red. The superior rectal vein is labeled at the top right in blue, while the inferior rectal vein is at the bottom right, showing arrows indicating its flow into the internal pudendal vein, then into the internal iliac vein, common iliac vein, and finally into the inferior vena cava. Green-colored lymphatic vessels are shown draining into the internal iliac lymph nodes. The nerves are colored yellow, with visceral innervation at the top left and somatic innervation at the bottom left, specifically mentioning the pudendal nerve (S2-4). A dashed horizontal line marks the pectinate line, dividing the rectum into regions above and below. The rectum is depicted in cross-section, with external layers in pink and the internal lining in a lighter shade. Directional arrows indicate the flow of blood and lymphatic drainage." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s10> .
