<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the blood vessels associated with the rectum, including the superior, middle, and inferior rectal arteries and veins, along with their origins and destinations." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a large pink vein running vertically through the center, labeled as the inferior vena cava. On either side of this central vein, blue and green veins branch out, representing the common iliac vein and its tributaries. Within the pelvic region, a network of smaller blue veins, the internal iliac vein and its tributaries, is depicted. An orange vein, the femoral vein, extends from the pelvis down towards the knee. The background includes the skeletal structure of the pelvis and lower limbs, providing context for the vein locations. The veins are shown in different colors to distinguish between the main veins and their tributaries, and the overall layout presents a cross-sectional view of the venous paths and connections." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/13c1cc0f0f8e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/87612001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the blood supply to the large intestine, highlighting various arteries and their branches." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a central pinkish-red structure representing the rectum, with blood vessels branching out from it. The superior rectal artery is depicted as a red line at the top left, extending from the superior mesenteric artery, while the superior rectal vein is shown as a blue line below it. The middle rectal artery is positioned near the middle of the image, slightly to the left, as a red line extending from the internal iliac artery, with the middle rectal vein directly beneath it. The inferior rectal artery is located at the bottom left, shown as a red line extending from the internal pudendal artery, and the inferior rectal vein is positioned below. Labels indicate the origins and destinations of these vessels: the superior rectal artery and vein are from and to the inferior mesenteric artery and vein, the middle rectal artery and vein are from and to the internal iliac artery and vein, and the inferior rectal artery and vein are from and to the internal pudendal artery and vein. The surrounding area of the illustration shows the pelvic bones and soft tissue in a light beige color, with labels and arrows clearly indicating the direction of blood flow." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s10> .
