<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p41_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram provides a side view of the lower body, focusing on the venous system. At the top right, the vein labeled IMV branches off from the main vein. The internal iliac vein, depicted as a large blue vein, branches off from the IMV. The middle rectal vein is a smaller vein branching off from the internal iliac vein, and the inferior rectal vein branches off from the middle rectal vein. Near the rectum, the internal hemorrhoidal plexus is shown as a network of interconnected veins, while the external hemorrhoidal plexus is near the anus. The liver is represented as a brown organ at the top left corner of the diagram. Internal structures are shaded in blue, representing the veins and plexuses, and arrows indicate the direction of blood flow through the veins." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s10> .
