<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p80_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a diagram of the human thorax with a transparent overlay of the rib cage and internal organs. At the top right corner, the label 'Full expiration' points to the uppermost part of the lungs, indicating the position when the lungs are fully exhaled. Slightly below this, 'Neutral respiratory position' directs attention to the middle section of the lungs, representing the resting position during normal breathing. Near the lower right side, 'Right costal margin' indicates the outer edge of the rib cage on the right. Horizontally across the midline of the chest, '4–8 cm in midline' highlights the distance from the midline to the right lung. Further down, '6–12 cm in right midclavicular line' points to the area on the right side of the chest, closer to the clavicle, indicating the distance from the midclavicular line to the right lung. At the bottom right, 'Inspiration' labels the lower part of the lungs, showing the position when the lungs are fully inflated. Arrows and lines connect these labels to specific areas of the lungs and chest wall, with a light beige background." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s7> .
