<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/bada23d3b9ba> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/66475004> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p44_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the visceral peritoneum at the top, depicted as an orange layer surrounding a circular shape with a hollow center. Below it, the mesentery is shown as a light brown, ribbon-like structure extending downward. At the bottom, the parietal peritoneum is represented by two beige, flat, triangular structures on either side, forming a base. Leader lines connect these components: one from the right side to the visceral peritoneum, another from the bottom of the visceral peritoneum to the mesentery, and a third from the bottom of the mesentery to the parietal peritoneum. The background is white, and no additional elements or labels are present." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/01b52828f200> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s7> .
