<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure comprises two labeled diagrams, A and B. Diagram A is circular with a central hollow area, while Diagram B is rectangular with a similar hollow center. In both diagrams, the outermost layer is light beige, the middle layer is orange, and the innermost layer in Diagram A is lighter orange. Diagram A includes labels for \"Parietal peritoneum\" at the bottom left, \"Visceral peritoneum\" at the top right, and \"Mesentery\" below the center, each with leader lines pointing to their respective layers. Diagram B has labels for \"Parietal peritoneum\" at the bottom right and \"Visceral peritoneum\" at the top right, also with leader lines. Both diagrams are marked with the letter \"A\" on the left side and \"B\" at the bottom left corner." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s7> .
