<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/ec1715168202> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#regulates> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p77_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into three panels. The left panel displays a cross-sectional diagram of an adrenal gland, with the outer \"Adrenal cortex\" and the inner \"Adrenal medulla\" labeled. A red arrow connects the adrenal cortex to the adrenal medulla, indicating the transition between these regions. The middle panel provides a microscopic view of the adrenal cortex, showing the \"Capsule\" at the top, followed by the \"Zona glomerulosa,\" \"Zona fasciculata,\" and \"Zona reticularis.\" The zona glomerulosa has smaller, more densely packed cells compared to the other zones, while the zona fasciculata has larger, more elongated cells arranged in parallel bundles, and the zona reticularis has the smallest, most densely packed cells. The right panel offers a microscopic view of the adrenal medulla, with the \"Capsule\" at the top and the \"Adrenal medulla\" below. The cells in the adrenal medulla are more uniform in size and shape, appearing as small, round nuclei surrounded by cytoplasm, and the tissue is less organized than the adrenal cortex. A scale bar labeled \"35x\" is present in the right panel, indicating the magnification level." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s7> .
