<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a microscopic view of tissue, likely stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E). The cells are arranged in a layered pattern, with some appearing elongated and others more rounded. The nuclei are stained a dark purple or magenta, while the cytoplasm has a lighter, bluish tint. The overall appearance suggests a section of biological tissue, possibly from an organ." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s7> .
