<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p74_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a detailed anatomical illustration of the left adrenal gland, depicted as a reddish-brown, oval-shaped structure situated above the kidney. The left inferior phrenic artery is shown at the top-left, represented by a red vessel running along the diaphragm. Near the top-center, the left superior suprarenal arteries are indicated by a network of smaller red vessels branching off from the main artery. Slightly below these, the left middle suprarenal artery is marked by another set of smaller red vessels. The left inferior suprarenal arteries are labeled below the adrenal gland, pointing to additional smaller red vessels. The left suprarenal vein is positioned below the inferior suprarenal arteries, shown as a blue vessel that appears to be draining blood from the adrenal gland. At the bottom-left, the abdominal aorta is labeled, pointing to a large blue vessel running vertically through the abdomen. The diagram uses color coding, with red for arteries and blue for veins, to clearly differentiate the blood vessels." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s7> .
