<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p82_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a tissue sample densely packed with cells, particularly in the upper and lower regions. Numerous small, round nuclei, stained dark blue/purple, are distributed throughout the field. The central and lower regions contain larger, irregularly shaped spaces labeled \"V,\" which contrast with the more cellular regions. The letter \"R\" points to an area at the top-center with a higher density of nuclei and less extracellular space. The \"M\" label is positioned near the center, indicating a darker, roughly circular area distinct from the surrounding tissue. The cytoplasm and extracellular spaces are stained pink/red due to the eosin component of the H&E stain." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s7> .
