<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p76_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with a dense, tightly packed topmost layer labeled 'Cap', featuring pinkish nuclei. Below the Cap, a layer labeled 'C' shows a more loosely packed structure with nuclei, but less dense than the Cap. The bottom layer, labeled 'M', is the least dense, showing large spaces between cells and fewer visible nuclei, indicating a more fibrous or connective tissue component. The overall coloration of the tissue sections varies from light blue to pink, with pink areas representing nuclei and blue areas representing cytoplasmic regions." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s14> .
