<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-section of the stomach wall, with multiple layers distinctly labeled. At the top-left, a text mentions that the stomach's surface area is increased by invaginations called gastric glands. Near the top-center, small openings within the tissue are labeled as the \"Opening to gastric gland,\" while the outermost layer of cells is labeled as \"Epithelium.\" Moving towards the middle-left, a green line within the tissue is labeled as \"Lymph vessel,\" and the layers beneath the epithelium are sequentially labeled as \"Lamina propria,\" \"Muscularis mucosae,\" and \"Submucosa.\" Further down, muscle fibers are labeled as \"Oblique muscle,\" \"Circular muscle,\" and \"Longitudinal muscle.\" Near the bottom-left, the outermost layer is labeled as \"Serosa.\" On the right-center, blood vessels are labeled as \"Artery and vein,\" and near the bottom-right, a network of nerves is labeled as \"Myenteric plexus.\"" <urn:graph:digestive_system/s2> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/a20af25a3aa1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/68439008> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s2> .
