<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a yellow box at the top left corner with the label 'Taenia coli', connected by an arrow to a part of the large intestine. Near the bottom left, an arrow points to a pouch-like structure labeled 'Caecum'. Below this, another label 'Retrocaecal' indicates an area behind the caecum. Towards the upper right, 'Preileal' points to a section before the ileocecal valve, while 'Postileal' is slightly below, pointing to the section after the valve. Near the lower right, 'Ileum' labels the small intestine, and at the bottom right, 'Promonteric' points to a section near the rectum." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s2> .
