<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p16_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features the salivary glands and their ducts, with the salivary gland ducts appearing as pink tubes at the top. The parotid gland is shown as a large, oval-shaped gland near the ear on the right side. Below it, the submandibular gland is depicted as a smaller, elongated gland under the jaw. At the bottom left, the sublingual gland is a small, rounded gland beneath the tongue. The glands are light pink, while the ducts are darker pink. The background provides a simplified outline of the head and neck with the skin removed, and the Cleveland Clinic logo and copyright information are in the bottom right corner." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s2> .
