<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/7c5fceb2bace> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#composed_of> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram centers on the peritoneal cavity, with the intraperitoneal space depicted in the central circular area, labeled with a red box and arrow. The parietal peritoneum is indicated on the left side, while the visceral peritoneum is shown on the right. The mesentery is also labeled on the right, pointing to a structure that suspends the small intestine. Retroperitoneal space is highlighted with a blue box and arrow at the lower part of the diagram, with labels for primarily and secondarily retroperitoneal organs positioned above and below the \"Retroperitoneal\" text. The abdominal aorta and lumbar spine are labeled near the bottom, with the retroperitoneal space surrounding these structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s7> .
