<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p12_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure shows two anatomical illustrations side by side, depicting the abdominal cavity with different structures labeled according to their location relative to the peritoneum." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the perineal region, with the anus positioned at the bottom center. The label \"Anus\" points directly to the anal opening. To the left and right of the anus, orange-brown structures, likely muscles or fascia, are visible. These structures are labeled \"Anocutaneous line,\" which runs horizontally across the lower part of the image, near the anus. The background features a network of lines and shading, representing underlying tissue layers, including skin and subcutaneous fat. The color scheme includes shades of beige, brown, and orange, with darker areas indicating deeper tissues and lighter areas representing the skin and subcutaneous fat." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s7> .
