<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a variety of cells depicted in different colors and sizes. At the top left, a large purple Gamma (γ) cell with a prominent nucleus is highlighted. Near this, a network of irregularly shaped red structures, resembling blood vessels, is labeled as Sinusoid. In the upper central area, an Alpha (α) cell, also a large purple cell but with a smaller nucleus, is indicated. The Epsilon (ε) acidophil cell, a large pinkish-purple cell with a granular texture, is situated in the upper right. The Delta (δ) basophil cell, a large blue cell with a smaller nucleus, is located in the lower right. Finally, at the bottom right, a Beta (β) cell, another large pinkish-purple cell with a smaller nucleus, is pointed out. The background of the diagram shows a network of sinusoids and other cellular structures, providing context for the cells' locations." <urn:graph:endocrine/s7> .
