<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a nephron with three main parts: the loop of Henle, the distal tubule, and the collecting duct. The distal tubule is depicted as a curved blue tube at the top center, while the collecting duct is a larger blue tube on the right. The loop of Henle is shown on the left as a curved section of the blue tube. Green arrows indicate water reabsorption from the distal tubule into the collecting duct, and orange arrows show solute movement towards the medulla. Aquaporins, represented by green structures, are located within the collecting duct. Yellow dots symbolize solutes within the loop of Henle. The medulla is positioned at the bottom right, and the cortex at the top right. A yellow box at the bottom reads \"Small volume of concentrated urine.\"" <urn:graph:endocrine/s7> .
