<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The loop of Henle is situated on the left side of the image, shaped like a U with the upper part extending horizontally and the lower part curving downward. It is filled with light blue liquid, and yellow dots are scattered throughout, indicating solutes. Above the loop of Henle is the distal tubule, a straight, vertical tube also filled with light blue liquid and containing yellow dots. On the right side, the collecting duct is a long, narrow tube extending from the distal tubule, similarly filled with light blue liquid and yellow dots. The cortex surrounds these structures and is labeled at the top-right corner, while the medulla is below the collecting duct, labeled at the bottom-right. At the bottom of the image, a label points downward toward the medulla, indicating a large volume of dilute urine. Within the loop of Henle, green arrows show the direction of fluid flow, orange arrows indicate solute movement, and blue arrows show water movement." <urn:graph:endocrine/s7> .
