<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The graph displays two hormones, ACTH and cortisol, with time on the x-axis marked at Noon, Midnight, 4 am, and 8 am. A horizontal line labeled \"Sleep\" stretches from 4 am to 8 am. The y-axis on the left measures ACTH concentration in picograms per milliliter, while the y-axis on the right measures cortisol concentration in micrograms per deciliter. A solid purple line represents cortisol levels, and a dashed gray line represents ACTH levels." <urn:graph:endocrine/s7> .
