<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features the hypothalamus at the top, colored light pink, with the optic chiasm, a yellowish structure, positioned near the center-left and connected by a black line to the hypothalamus. On the right side of the hypothalamus, two small, rounded structures are depicted: the mammillary body and the median eminence. A red artery extends from the hypothalamus towards the anterior pituitary, connecting to the primary capillary plexus. This plexus, a network of capillaries, surrounds the median eminence and is linked to the hypothalamic-hypophysial portal vessels, shown as blue tubes. These vessels extend downward to the anterior pituitary, which is colored light brown and positioned below the hypothalamus. Beneath the anterior pituitary is the posterior pituitary, colored light pink. A blue vein extends from the anterior pituitary, connecting to the sinuses, which are a network of blue tubes surrounding the posterior pituitary. Each label is placed adjacent to its corresponding anatomical feature, with lines or arrows directing to the relevant part of the diagram, illustrating the flow of blood and neural signals between the structures." <urn:graph:endocrine/s7> .
