<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the hypothalamus positioned at the top left corner, depicted as a small, rounded structure with a pinkish hue. An arrow labeled \"TRH\" extends from the hypothalamus to the pituitary gland, which is situated directly below. The pituitary gland is also a small, rounded structure with a pinkish hue. From the pituitary gland, an arrow labeled \"TSH\" points towards the centrally located thyroid gland. The thyroid gland is the largest structure in the diagram, irregularly shaped with a reddish hue. Three hormones are represented as spheres emerging from the thyroid gland: a green sphere labeled \"T₃,\" a purple sphere labeled \"T₄,\" and a gray sphere labeled \"Calcitonin.\" A curved red arrow labeled \"Negative feedback inhibition\" loops back from the thyroid gland to the hypothalamus, indicating the regulatory feedback mechanism. The legend is placed in the top right corner, defining the abbreviations TRH, TSH, T₃, and T₄." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s16> .
