<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a horizontal cross-section of the neck, viewed from the front. At the top center, the isthmus of the thyroid gland is labeled. Above it, the investing layer of deep cervical fascia is positioned. On the left side, the sternocleidomastoid muscle is marked, while near the center, the sterno-hyoid muscle is indicated. The omohyoid muscle is also on the left. On the right side, the pre-tracheal fascia is labeled. The internal jugular vein is on the left side, and the common carotid artery is on the right. Muscles are depicted in green, veins in blue, and arteries in red." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s16> .
