<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p45_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure presents a detailed cross-sectional view of the neck and upper thoracic region from a posterior perspective. The muscles are rendered in a reddish-brown hue, with a textured appearance that suggests muscle fibers. The trachea is positioned at the bottom, featuring a circular opening, while the esophagus is situated above it, also with a circular opening. The thyroid gland is displayed on either side of the trachea, with its posterior aspect clearly labeled. Small, oval-shaped parathyroid glands are attached to the thyroid gland. The pharynx is labeled at the top, extending upwards toward the back of the head. Each label is connected to its corresponding structure via a leader line or arrow, with the text in black. In the top left corner, there is a smaller inset image, providing a simplified view of the back of a person's head and neck, focusing on the area around the thyroid gland and pharynx." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s16> .
