<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p46_b12> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into two sections. The top section presents a labeled diagram showing the posterior view of the thyroid gland, with various anatomical structures such as the superior thyroid artery, inferior constrictor muscle, left lobe of the thyroid gland, middle thyroid vein, cricopharyngeus, inferior thyroid vein, inferior thyroid artery, thyrocervical trunk, internal carotid artery, external carotid artery, superior thyroid vein, internal jugular vein, right superior parathyroid, right inferior parathyroid, common carotid artery, oesophagus, and subclavian artery. Each structure is labeled with a text box connected by a leader line or arrow pointing to the corresponding part of the thyroid gland. The bottom section provides a detailed anatomical illustration of the recurrent laryngeal nerve and the superior laryngeal nerve in relation to the thyroid gland. This illustration includes the superior laryngeal nerve, vagus nerve, left lobe of thyroid gland, superior parathyroid gland, inferior parathyroid gland, and recurrent laryngeal nerve. The nerves and glands are depicted in a cross-sectional view, with the left side showing a posterior view and the right side showing a lateral view. Leader lines connect the labels to specific parts of the nerves and glands within the illustration." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s16> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomical structures of the neck region, including blood vessels, nerves, muscles, and the thyroid gland." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s16> .
