<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a simplified brain with the hypothalamus at the top, connected by blue arrows labeled \"TRH\" to the anterior pituitary below. An orange arrow labeled \"Negative feedback inhibition\" runs from the thyroid gland back to the hypothalamus. The anterior pituitary is depicted as a small, rounded structure, with blue arrows pointing from the hypothalamus indicating stimulation. Orange arrows labeled \"TSH\" point from the anterior pituitary to the thyroid gland at the bottom, indicating inhibition. Red arrows labeled \"TSH\" also point from the anterior pituitary to the thyroid gland, indicating stimulation. Blue arrows labeled \"TH\" extend from the thyroid gland to target organs, indicating the action of thyroid hormone. Five numbered text boxes are positioned around the diagram, each describing a step in the process." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s16> .
