<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of the neck region, with the external carotid artery on the left side pointing upwards, adjacent to the internal carotid artery which also points upwards. Near the thyroid gland, the superior thyroid artery and vein are depicted, with the artery branching off from the internal carotid artery. The superior laryngeal nerve is shown pointing towards the larynx, featuring both an internal and external branch. The thyroid cartilage, forming the Adam's apple, is situated at the top of the thyroid gland, while the median cricothyroid ligament is located below it, connecting the cricoid cartilage to the thyroid cartilage. Cricothyroid muscles are displayed on either side of the median cricothyroid ligament. The cricoid cartilage, positioned below the thyroid cartilage, forms a ring-like structure. The internal jugular vein is on the right side, pointing downwards, while the middle thyroid vein is found within the thyroid gland, draining into the internal jugular vein. The ascending cervical artery branches off from the common carotid artery, and the inferior thyroid structures are also depicted." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s16> .
