<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/86570000> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a superior view of the liver, with the right lobe positioned prominently at the top left and the left lobe at the top right. The inferior vena cava is situated at the top-center, depicted as a blue structure entering the liver. Adjacent to the IVC, the caudate lobe is located at the top-center of the liver. Two areas labeled as \"Bare area\" are shown, one at the top-center and another at the bottom-center of the liver. Ligaments are illustrated around the liver: the right triangular ligament is on the left side, the left triangular ligament on the right side, the coronary ligament also on the left, and the falciform ligament at the bottom-center. Leader lines with arrows connect the labels to their corresponding parts, providing clear identification of each structure." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/949cd23bb8fa> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/113343008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p64_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The large intestine is depicted in a semi-transparent manner, allowing the viewer to see the branching pattern of the arteries within its walls. The arteries are shown in red, with yellow arrows indicating the direction of blood flow. The superior mesenteric artery is positioned at the top left, branching into the middle colic artery and ileocolic artery. The arteria recta is at the top right, while the inferior mesenteric artery is at the bottom right, branching into the left colic artery, sigmoid arteries, and superior rectal artery. The right colic artery is shown at the bottom left, branching from the ileocolic artery. The marginal artery branches from the left colic artery and is also positioned at the top right." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/277967008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/949cd23bb8fa> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/52515009> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/7a5d78cc2536> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/52515009> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/7a5d78cc2536> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p86_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomy of the biliary and pancreatic ducts, including the gallbladder, hepatic ducts, cystic duct, bile duct, and main pancreatic duct, in relation to the duodenum." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p86_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a green, oval-shaped gallbladder positioned at the top left. Extending from it are two green ducts: the right hepatic duct, which points downward and to the right, and the left hepatic duct, which points downward and to the left. The cystic duct branches off from the common hepatic duct, pointing downward and to the left, and continues as the bile duct. The bile duct merges with the main pancreatic duct, which is depicted in pinkish-orange and loops around the descending part of the duodenum, forming a U-shape. Leader lines connect labels to the corresponding anatomical structures, with arrows indicating the direction of the connections." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p86_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/28231008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p86_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/34707002> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/113276009> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/52082005> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the blood supply to the small intestine, focusing on the superior mesenteric artery and its branches, the jejunal and ileal arteries." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed cross-section of the intestine, revealing the internal structures with the outer layers removed. The vasa recta are depicted as a network of small, branching blood vessels extending from the main artery into the intestinal tissue, shown as thin, red lines branching outwards. Above the vasa recta, the arterial arcades are represented by larger, curved blood vessels forming an arch-like pattern, also in red." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A labeled diagram showing a superior view of the liver and its surrounding structures, including the right and left lobes, the inferior vena cava, and various ligaments." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s6> .
