<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p40_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed cross-section of the anal canal. The anal valve is depicted as a small, greenish-yellow structure at the base of the anal canal, situated on the left side of the image. The anal column is shown as a larger, darker area within the anal canal, appearing as a vertical, columnar structure that occupies most of the upper portion and is labeled on the right side. The pectinate line is represented by a horizontal blue dashed line running across the bottom of the anal canal, positioned on the lower right side of the image, dividing the anal canal into upper and lower sections." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s8> .
