<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p69_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a pink spleen in the upper right section, with a blue short gastric vein branching towards it from the splenic vein. A large blue hepatic portal vein runs vertically through the center, connecting various smaller veins. Several small blue pancreatic veins extend from the main hepatic portal vein towards the pancreas. The splenic vein, a large blue vein, runs horizontally across the lower left side, connecting to the inferior mesenteric vein. Near the bottom center, a small, curved structure labeled as the uncinate process of the pancreas is visible. The superior mesenteric vein runs horizontally across the lower center, connecting to the inferior mesenteric vein. Leader lines with arrows indicate the names of these parts, showing their relationships within the abdominal cavity." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s4> .
