<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p67_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents an elongated, bean-shaped organ, likely a kidney, with several labeled parts. At the top, the 'Upper Pole' label points to the uppermost part of the kidney. On the right side, the 'Diaphragmatic Surface' label indicates the flat surface facing the diaphragm. Near the center-left, the 'Hilum' label marks the area where blood vessels enter and exit. Below the hilum, the 'Visceral Surface' label points to the curved surface facing other organs. At the bottom, the 'Lower Pole' label points to the lowermost part of the kidney. Within the hilum, red and blue lines represent arteries and veins, respectively. The visceral surface is smooth and rounded, while the diaphragmatic surface appears slightly more irregular." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p67_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The diagram illustrates the various labeled parts of a kidney, including the upper pole, diaphragmatic surface, hilum, visceral surface, and lower pole." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s4> .
