<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-sectional view of the pelvic region, focusing on the anal area. The anal aperture is centrally located at the bottom of the diagram, marked by an arrow. Surrounding this central opening, the ischioanal fossa is depicted as a recessed, triangular-shaped area extending towards the sides of the pelvis. The external anal sphincter is shown as a ring-like muscle structure encircling the anal aperture, positioned just below it. The overall shape of the pelvic region in the illustration is roughly triangular, with the apex pointing upwards." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s1> .
