<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p1_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a side view of a person's torso alongside a detailed cross-sectional view of the lower abdomen and pelvis. Different colors are used to distinguish between the thoracic, abdominal, and pelvic cavities. The thoracic cavity is positioned above the spine, followed by the abdominal cavity, and the pelvic cavity is highlighted in green. The pelvic brim (inlet) is marked with an arrow just above the pelvic cavity, while the area inferior to the pelvic floor is indicated at the bottom. The cross-sectional view displays internal organs such as the liver, stomach, and intestines, providing a clear view of the internal anatomy." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_pelvic_floor/s1> .
