<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p74_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-sectional view of the abdominal cavity, with the liver depicted as a large, irregularly shaped organ with a pinkish hue on the left side of the image. The diaphragm is shown as a thin, curved structure in light purple, positioned above the liver and kidney. The subphrenic recess appears as a small, triangular area in light blue, located below the diaphragm and to the right of the liver. The hepatorenal recess is also a small, triangular light blue area, situated between the liver and the kidney. The kidney is represented as a bean-shaped organ with a pinkish hue on the right side of the image. Leader lines connect labels to their respective structures: \"Liver\" to the upper left portion of the liver, \"Diaphragm\" to the upper central region of the diaphragm, \"Subphrenic recess\" to the lower right corner of the subphrenic recess, \"Hepatorenal recess\" to the lower left corner of the hepatorenal recess, and \"Kidney\" to the lower right portion of the kidney. The background features a gradient of colors representing different tissues and spaces, with the liver and kidney being the most prominent structures." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p16_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/59380008> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p88_b4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the pelvic region, highlighting the pelvic bone, ala of sacrum, LV, SI, and pelvic inlet." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s9> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/818fbdfe6c87> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s9> .
