<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a detailed anatomical illustration of the pelvic region. At the top left, the pelvic bone is labeled, pointing to a large, curved structure forming the upper part of the pelvis. On the right side, the ala of sacrum is labeled, indicating the wing-like extensions from the sacrum. Near the center, the label \"LV\" points to the left side of the sacrum, while \"SI\" is slightly below, marking the sacroiliac joint area. At the bottom right, the \"Pelvic inlet\" label points to the opening at the base of the pelvis. The overall shape of the pelvis is roughly triangular, with the wider part at the top and the narrower part at the bottom." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s9> .
