<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p88_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A human torso is depicted from the waist down, with the lower abdomen and upper thighs visible. A vertical dashed line, the median plane, runs through the center of the body, dividing it into left and right halves. A horizontal dashed line, the transumbilical plane, runs across the body just below the navel, dividing it into upper and lower sections. The anterior superior iliac spine is marked by a label pointing to the bony prominence on the front of the pelvis on both sides near the hip area. The inguinal ligament is shown as a curved line connecting the anterior superior iliac spine to the pubic tubercle, labeled on the left side. The torso is divided into four quadrants: the right upper quadrant (RUQ) in pink, the left upper quadrant (LUQ) in green, the right lower quadrant (RLQ) in gray, and the left lower quadrant (LLQ) in beige." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s9> .
