<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with sensory and mental inputs positioned in the top-left corner, marked by a blue number \"1\" and an arrow pointing towards the brain. The brain is centrally located at the top of the image, depicted in profile with shades of orange and pink. Extending from the brain is a yellow line labeled \"Vagus nerve,\" which travels downwards to the stomach. The stomach is displayed in the lower-center, colored blue with a yellow outline, and the word \"Stomach\" is written inside it. Within the stomach area, \"Gastrin (↑gastric acid)\" and \"CCK (↑digestion)\" are noted in red text. On the right side of the image, the process of \"Vagal activation of gastric motility and gastric juice secretion\" is described, marked by a blue number \"2\" and a black arrow pointing from the vagus nerve to the stomach. A curved red arrow within the stomach indicates the direction of action from the vagus nerve." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s9> .
