<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p72_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a diagram of the adrenal gland, split into a cross-sectional view on the right and a side view on the left. In the cross-sectional view, three layers are differentiated by texture and color: the outermost Glomerulosa appears thin and orange, the middle Fasciculata is thicker and yellowish, and the innermost Reticularis is dense and brownish. A blue vein-like structure runs through the Reticularis, suggesting blood vessels. The side view highlights the gland's three-dimensional shape, with labels for four hormones: Aldosterone at the outermost layer, Cortisol slightly inward, Androgens further in, and Catecholamines at the innermost layer. Arrows point to the respective hormone locations within the gland." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s14> .
