<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p69_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the blood vessels and structures around the kidneys and adrenal glands, including the celiac trunk, various suprarenal veins and arteries, the renal artery and vein, the superior mesenteric artery, and the inferior vena cava." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s14> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure presents two anatomical illustrations of the adrenal glands side by side, with the anterior view on the left and the posterior view on the right. In the anterior illustration, the gland is shown with a curved, kidney-shaped appearance. The top left portion is labeled \"Gastric area,\" and the bottom right portion is labeled \"Pancreatic area.\" A blue tube-like structure extends from the lower left side, labeled \"Suprarenal vein.\" In the posterior illustration, the gland also appears curved and kidney-shaped. The top right portion is labeled \"Diaphragmatic area,\" and the bottom left portion is labeled \"Renal area.\" Another blue tube-like structure extends from the lower right side, also labeled \"Suprarenal vein.\" Leader lines connect the labels to their respective areas on the gland." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s14> .
