<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p57_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The left kidney is more visible than the right, which is partially obscured by the pancreas. The spleen is located on the left side, adjacent to the left kidney and depicted in dark purple. The inferior vena cava branches into the abdominal aorta at the bottom, while the portal vein and hepatic artery are connected to the liver. The common bile duct runs alongside the pancreas, and the splenic artery connects to the spleen. The adrenal glands are situated above the kidneys, and the superior mesenteric vein and artery are connected to the small intestine. Various arteries and veins are labeled, including the IVC, portal vein, hepatic artery, splenic artery, and superior mesenteric artery and vein. The common bile duct runs along the posterior surface of the pancreas, and the major and minor papillae are labeled on the right side of the pancreas." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s14> .
