<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p67_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The main image presents the human body from the waist down, focusing on the adrenal glands. Two adrenal glands are positioned above the kidneys, with the right adrenal gland shown on the right and the left adrenal gland on the left. Arrows point to these structures, labeling them as \"Right adrenal gland,\" \"Left adrenal gland,\" and \"Left kidney.\" The adrenal glands are depicted in a light pinkish color, while the kidneys are in a darker pinkish hue. Blood vessels and nerves connecting the adrenal glands to the kidneys are also shown. In the top-left corner, an inset diagram provides a cross-section of the adrenal gland, dividing it into the \"Adrenal cortex\" at the outer layer and the \"Adrenal medulla\" at the inner layer. The title \"Anatomy of the Adrenal Gland\" is displayed at the top of the image, and a copyright notice appears at the bottom-right corner." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s14> .
