<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p69_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a large blue vessel, the aorta, running vertically through the center. Branching off from the aorta at the top-center is the celiac trunk, also in blue. The R. suprarenal vein, in red, extends from the celiac trunk towards the right side. The superior suprarenal arteries, also red, branch off from the celiac trunk, pointing towards the upper right. The inferior phrenic artery, in red, branches off from the superior suprarenal arteries, moving towards the right. The middle suprarenal arteries, in red, stem from the inferior phrenic artery, pointing towards the middle right. The inferior suprarenal arteries, in red, branch off from the middle suprarenal arteries, heading towards the lower right. The L. suprarenal vein, in red, branches off from the inferior suprarenal arteries, pointing towards the left. The renal artery, in red, branches off from the aorta, moving towards the right. The renal vein, in blue, branches off from the renal artery, pointing towards the bottom right. The superior mesenteric artery, in red, branches off from the aorta, moving towards the left. The inferior vena cava, in blue, branches off from the aorta, pointing downwards. Two kidneys are depicted, with the right kidney on the left side and the left kidney on the right side. The adrenal glands are shown above the kidneys, with the right adrenal gland connected to the right kidney by the R. suprarenal vein and the L. suprarenal vein connecting to the left kidney. The inferior phrenic artery and its branches are positioned above the kidneys, while the renal artery and vein are shown below the kidneys. The superior mesenteric artery and inferior vena cava are located below the aorta." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s14> .
