<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into three sections labeled a, b, and c, each separated by dashed vertical lines. In section a, a single cell is displayed with a purple nucleus, green mitochondria, and white organelles. Below this cell, there is a red elongated structure containing black dots, with a black arrow pointing towards it from the bottom left corner. Section b shows two identical cells side by side, similar to the cell in section a, with additional smaller structures at the bottom that resemble the main cell, complete with purple nuclei, green mitochondria, and white organelles. A black arrow connects the red elongated structure in section a to these smaller structures in section b. In section c, a single cell is shown with a purple nucleus, green mitochondria, and white organelles, and a circular arrow above it suggests rotation or movement. A black arrow in the bottom left corner of section c points to the red elongated structure in section a." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s9> .
