<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p42_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a side view of the head and neck, with lymph node groups shaded in distinct colors. The superior deep cervical nodes are green and positioned at the top of the neck, above the submandibular nodes. The interior deep cervical nodes are blue, located in the middle of the neck, below the superior deep cervical nodes. Red indicates the submental nodes at the very top of the neck, just below the chin. Pink represents the submandibular nodes at the bottom of the neck, below the interior deep cervical nodes. Orange is used for both the prolaryngeal nodes near the larynx and the pretracheal nodes in front of the trachea. Purple marks the paratracheal nodes on either side of the trachea. Arrows in the diagram indicate the flow or direction of lymphatic drainage within these groups. The legend is situated at the bottom left corner, with labels next to corresponding color blocks." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s3> .
