<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two sections. On the left, labeled (a) Negative Feedback, a person is shown eating a sandwich with the label \"Stimulus: rising blood glucose level\" above them. An illustration of a pancreas is positioned with an arrow pointing to the liver, and another arrow points back from the liver to the pancreas. Between them, a circular diagram labeled \"Negative feedback loop\" is placed. Body cells are illustrated with an arrow pointing to the pancreas, and text explains the decline in glucose levels and the cessation of insulin release. On the right, labeled (b) Positive Feedback, a woman is depicted breastfeeding a baby with the label \"Stimulus: baby suckles at nipple.\" An illustration of the hypothalamus is shown with an arrow pointing to the posterior pituitary gland, and another arrow from the posterior pituitary to the breast. A circular diagram labeled \"Positive feedback loop\" is positioned between the posterior pituitary and the breast. An illustration of milk ejection from the mammary gland is shown with an arrow pointing to the baby. Both sections have a copyright notice at the top." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s3> .
