<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The testis is depicted as a blue oval at the bottom left, surrounded by a yellowish area representing the peritoneal sac. Near the top of the peritoneal sac is the circular superficial inguinal ring. Above this ring sits the conjoint tendon, followed by the extraperitoneal fascia and then the parietal peritoneum. The deep inguinal ring is shown as a circular opening near the top right of the image. At the top, the inferior epigastric vessels are illustrated as a network of blood vessels. Arrows in the diagram indicate the direction of flow or connection between these structures." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s14> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/85756007> <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s14> .
