<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p85_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized into three main sections. At the top left, \"Senescent red blood cells\" is positioned, with \"Haemolysis (1)\" at the top right. Arrows from both these sections lead to \"Unconjugated bilirubin + albumin\" in the top center. The central section features \"Uptake (3),\" \"Conjugation (3),\" and \"Excretion (3)\" on the left side, with \"Hepatocyte\" at the bottom right. \"Unconjugated bilirubin\" is shown receiving arrows from \"Unconjugated bilirubin + albumin,\" while \"Biliverdin reductase\" and \"Glucuronyl transferase (2)\" are located within this section, leading to \"Conjugated bilirubin.\" The bottom section includes \"Bile canaliculus,\" \"Bile ducts,\" and \"Duodenum,\" with arrows connecting them sequentially. Red arrows throughout the chart indicate the direction of flow, and numbers in parentheses mark specific steps. A dashed box labeled \"Conjugation (3)\" highlights the conjugation step." <urn:graph:abdominal_wall/s14> .
