<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p78_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E), featuring a label 'Cap' at the top left corner pointing to the outermost layer, likely a capillary network. On the left side, the label 'G' points to a group of cells arranged in a glandular pattern, with darker staining nuclei. Near the right side, the label 'T' indicates a single cell or small cluster of cells, notable for their larger size and prominent nucleus. The background shows a lighter staining matrix, probably representing extracellular matrix or connective tissue." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s2> .
