<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the hypothalamus positioned at the top left, featuring neurosecretory cells in the paraventricular and supraoptic nuclei. Below the hypothalamus, the anterior and posterior pituitary glands are depicted, with the anterior pituitary showing two types of cells: acidophils and basophils. The hypophyseal portal system is represented as a network of blood vessels connecting the hypothalamus to the anterior pituitary, with arrows indicating the direction of blood flow. The posterior pituitary gland is shown releasing oxytocin and antidiuretic hormone (ADH). In the lower left section, the mammary gland and kidney are positioned, illustrating the influence of prolactin and oxytocin on milk secretion and ADH on water absorption, respectively." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s2> .
