<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the hypothalamus at the top, featuring neurosecretory cells in the paraventricular and supraoptic nuclei. Below it, the anterior pituitary gland is depicted with two types of cells: acidophils and basophils. The posterior pituitary gland is also shown below the hypothalamus. A network of blood vessels, the hypophyseal portal system, connects the hypothalamus to the anterior pituitary gland, with arrows indicating the direction of blood flow. Oxytocin and ADH are shown connecting to the uterus, mammary gland, and kidney. The adrenal cortex, thyroid, testis, and ovary are positioned around the main structures, with the adrenal cortex above the kidneys, the thyroid in the neck, the testis in the scrotum, and the ovary in the pelvic cavity." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s2> .
