<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p90_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The top section of the image displays a histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E), featuring a network of sinusoids surrounded by hepatocytes. The sinusoids are irregularly shaped spaces within the liver, with two prominent ones highlighted by green circles; one is larger and centrally located, while the other is smaller and positioned towards the left side. The sinusoids have a distinct red coloration due to the presence of blood cells, likely erythrocytes, within them. The surrounding tissue is composed of pinkish areas representing the cytoplasm of hepatocytes, with nuclei appearing dark blue. The bottom section is an electron micrograph showing a detailed view of the interface between the sinusoid and the hepatocyte. The sinusoid is labeled at the top right corner, while the endothelium of the sinusoid is labeled on the left side, indicating the thin layer of cells lining the sinusoidal lumen. The space between the endothelium and the hepatocyte is labeled as the \"Space of Disse,\" where the exchange of substances occurs between the blood and the hepatocytes. The hepatocyte cytoplasm contains various organelles such as mitochondria and endoplasmic reticulum, visible in the electron micrograph." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s10> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/447746328c7a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s10> .
