<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p84_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents two diagrams side by side, each labeled to guide the viewer through the stages of follicular development and ovulation. The first diagram focuses on the initial stages, while the second highlights the process of ovulation. Each stage is distinctly marked with labels that explain the development and changes occurring in the follicles and ovum. The layout is designed to show a clear progression from one stage to the next, with arrows indicating the direction of development." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
