<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p79_b15> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A detailed anatomical illustration displays the lymphatic system in the pelvic region. The aorta is shown as a blue structure running vertically through the center of the image. Para-aortic lymph nodes are depicted as a cluster of green nodes, with a black arrow pointing to them along the aorta. Pelvic lymph nodes are also shown as green clusters, with another black arrow indicating their position below the para-aortic nodes, closer to the pelvic area. Lymphatic vessels connect the green lymph nodes. The kidneys are portrayed in pinkish-brown on either side of the aorta, while the bladder is shown in pink at the bottom of the image. The pelvic region is highlighted, illustrating the location of the pelvic lymph nodes relative to the bladder and other pelvic structures. The diagram uses a cross-sectional view to depict the internal anatomy, with the aorta and lymph nodes clearly marked." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
