<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p82_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a detailed view of the female reproductive system, with the ovaries positioned on either side of the centrally located uterus. The fallopian tubes extend from the ovaries towards the uterus, illustrating the path an egg takes. The suspensory ligament of the ovary is at the top-left, near the upper part of the ovary, while the fundus of the uterus is at the top-center, pointing to the uppermost part of the uterus. The fallopian tube is shown extending from the upper part of the ovary towards the center. The corpus luteum is located on the fallopian tube, and the egg is depicted at the far right. The fimbria, ovary, ovarian ligament, round ligament, and broad ligament are all positioned at the bottom-left. Developing follicles are near the ovary, and a newly discharged ovum (egg) is at the far right. The uterus is centrally positioned, with the cervix at the bottom-center and the vagina at the bottom-right. Arrows indicate the direction of the egg's journey." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
