<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into three main sections. In the top left, an X-ray image of the thoracic cavity is displayed, showing the lungs, heart, ribs, and spine. On the top right, a diagram labeled \"Myasthenia Gravis\" features the head and neck region, with highlighted structures such as the hyoid bone, cricothyroid ligament, thyroid cartilage, superior and inferior parathyroid glands, trachea, and thymus. Near the thymus, there is a label for \"Cancer.\" At the bottom, two diagrams are placed side by side. The left diagram illustrates the interaction between Thymoma and TAMG (LOMG), depicting thymic epithelial cells, neoplastic cells, myoid cells, CD4+ T cells, acetylcholine receptors, and antibodies, with red crosses indicating defective AIRE expression and other antigens. The right diagram shows the process involving lymph nodes and neuromuscular junctions, including antigen-presenting cells, B cells, T cells, and antibodies, with a close-up of the neuromuscular junction displaying synaptic vesicles and acetylcholine release." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
<http://snomed.info/id/444231005> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#associated_with> <http://snomed.info/id/91637004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomy and pathophysiology related to Myasthenia Gravis, including an X-ray of the thoracic cavity, a diagram of the head and neck region, and detailed interactions at the cellular level." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
<http://snomed.info/id/91637004> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caused_by> <http://snomed.info/id/444231005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/44695005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p82_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/15497006> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/f081530482a7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/85828009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p85_b16> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized into three main sections. At the top left, the Multiplication Phase is labeled with \"I Multiplication Phase\" and \"(Mitotic divisions)\" written vertically, pointing to a series of cells labeled \"P.G.C. Below this, the Growth Phase is marked by \"II Growth Phase\" written vertically, indicating a single cell labeled \"Primary Oocyte (2n)\" undergoing growth. Further down, the Maturation Phase is labeled with \"III Maturation Phase\" vertically, showing a secondary oocyte labeled \"Secondary Oocyte (n)\" resulting from Meiosis I. This secondary oocyte then undergoes Meiosis II, leading to an ovum labeled \"Ovum (n)\" and two polar bodies labeled \"I Polar body (n)\" and \"II Polar bodies (n)\". Arrows connect these stages, illustrating the progression from one to the next, and the cells are depicted as circular with varying levels of detail inside." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/7a8736d4d8b4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/85828009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s19> .
