<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure shows a close-up cross-sectional view of a human nose, with the nasal cavity highlighted in orange and the external features in grayscale." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the soft palate and related anatomical structures, including the nasal septum, middle conchae, and various muscles." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b22> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/49460000> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/59820001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p28_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/74262004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/279549004> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed cross-sectional view of the palate and surrounding structures. At the top center, the nasal septum is shown as a vertical partition dividing the nasal cavity. Near the nasal septum, the middle conchae are depicted as curved structures on either side. On the left side, the levator veli palatini and tensor veli palatini muscles are illustrated, both appearing to be attached to the nasal septum. The auditory tube is labeled on the right side, pointing to a small tube-like structure. The hamulus is a small, hook-like structure located on the left side. The palatine aponeurosis is shown as a broad, flat structure extending across the palate on the right side. Near the bottom left, the musculus uvulae is a small muscle situated near the uvula. The uvula itself is the hanging structure in the back of the throat, labeled at the bottom center. Finally, the palatopharyngeus muscle is positioned at the bottom right, on the right side of the palate." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b22> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/72914001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b22> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a cross-sectional view of the soft palate and pharynx, with muscles depicted in shades of pink and brown, and bones and other structures in blue and black. The middle concha is positioned at the top-center, pointing to a curved structure that seems part of the nasal cavity. The levator veli palatini and tensor veli palatini muscles are labeled on the left side, extending from the top-left corner down towards the center, both pointing to a triangular area near the middle concha. The hamulus, a small, hook-like structure, is labeled on the left, indicating a small protrusion on the soft palate. The musculus uvulae is labeled at the bottom-left, pointing to a small, rounded structure at the back of the soft palate, while the uvula is labeled at the bottom-center, pointing to the same structure. The palatopharyngeus muscle is labeled on the right side, extending from the top-right corner down towards the center, pointing to a triangular area near the uvula. The auditory tube is labeled on the right, indicating a tube-like structure that appears to connect the middle ear with the nasopharynx." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A close-up view of a human nose is presented, with the nasal cavity highlighted in orange. The internal nasal passages and the septum dividing the two nostrils are clearly visible. The external features, such as the bridge and the nostrils, are shown in grayscale, providing a contrast to the highlighted nasal cavity. The diagram is a cross-sectional view, with the nasal cavity occupying the central portion of the image, flanked by the external nose structures. There are no visible labels or text within the image." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a side view of a human figure with the internal organs of the digestive system visible. The mouth, labeled as the oral cavity, is positioned at the top left, with the tongue directly beneath it. The parotid gland is situated above the ear, while the sublingual gland is placed below the tongue, and the submandibular gland is further down, below the sublingual gland. The esophagus is depicted as a long tube extending from the pharynx, which is located above it, down into the abdomen. The stomach is shown as a large, sac-like organ situated below the esophagus. The pancreas is positioned behind the stomach, while the liver is a large organ on the right side of the abdomen, with the gallbladder, a small greenish organ, attached to it. The sigmoid colon and rectum are also labeled as sections of the large intestine, with the vermiform appendix, a small finger-like structure, attached to the cecum." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b22> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/244797009> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_face_and_oral_cavity/s1> .
