<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p3_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features a detailed view of the human head and upper torso, with specific attention to the neck and shoulder areas. The superior nuchal line is positioned at the top of the skull, running horizontally along the back of the head. The mandible, highlighted in yellow, is labeled at the lower jawbone. The clavicle is labeled on the collarbone, extending from the shoulder blade. The manubrium of the sternum, also highlighted in yellow, is shown on the upper part of the sternum. The acromion is labeled on the shoulder blade, pointing to the outer edge. Arrows and lines connect these labels to their corresponding anatomical parts. The background of the illustration is white, and the highlighted areas are in yellow." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s14> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p28_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates two anatomical structures labeled with numbers from 1 to 35, possibly depicting the same bone from different angles, along with the layers of the tracheal wall." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s14> .
