<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b22> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration features the spine with vertebrae labeled C1 through C5, depicted in light beige. The nerves are shown in yellow, with the accessory nerve (XI) positioned at the top right, pointing to the upper part of the spine. Below it, the hypoglossal nerve (XII) directs towards the lower part of the spine. The nerve to the sternocleidomastoid points to the side of the neck, and the ansa cervicalis forms a network branching out to various neck muscles. The transverse cervical nerve extends across the neck, and the nerve to the trapezius points to the back of the neck." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s14> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/314820002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s14> .
