<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p28_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays two structures, each labeled with numbers, positioned side by side. The left structure, labeled Structure A, is marked with numbers 1 through 23, while the right structure, labeled Structure B, is marked with numbers 1 through 35. Both structures share a similar shape, featuring a rounded top and a cylindrical lower section. The numbers are distributed across these structures, with some appearing on the upper part and others on the lower part, indicating different parts or features. There are no leader lines or arrows; the numbers are simply placed next to the corresponding areas. The structures are presented without additional visual aids like arrows or labels, suggesting a straightforward depiction of the features." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s14> .
