<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A simplified, cartoon-like depiction of a stomach is shown, divided into two sections: a lighter pink upper part representing the fundus and a darker pink lower part representing the body. Within the stomach, three distinct yellow regions symbolize different portions of food being digested. An orange arrow labeled \"Gastrin\" points from the right side of the image towards the stomach, while another orange arrow labeled \"arrival causes parietal reflexes & secretion by\" points from the left side. The word \"FOOD\" is written in bold black letters within the lower portion of the stomach, centered on the yellow food regions. The phrase \"arrival causes parietal reflexes & secretion by\" is written in blue text on the left side, pointing towards the stomach." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
