<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p24_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top left, a yellow oval labeled \"Food\" points downward to another yellow oval labeled \"Amino acids or peptides.\" In the central region, the diagram is divided into \"Gastric mucosa\" on the left and \"Enteric plexus\" on the right. Within the \"Gastric mucosa,\" a yellow oval labeled \"Enteric sensory neuron\" sits near the top. Below it, a red diamond labeled \"G cell\" connects to a purple oval labeled \"Gastrin,\" while a \"D cell\" connects to \"Somatostatin,\" an \"ECL cell\" to \"Histamine,\" a \"Parietal cell\" to \"H+,\" and a \"Chief cell\" to \"Pepsinogen.\" The \"Enteric plexus\" section features yellow lines representing nerve fibers. At the bottom left, a purple oval labeled \"H+\" connects to \"Pepsin\" and \"Pepsinogen,\" which in turn connects to the \"Chief cell.\" At the top right, a yellow oval labeled \"Input via vagus nerve\" points downward to a green number \"1,\" which links to the \"Gastric mucosa\" section." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/370853ef2016> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/85e7e644d964> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/68615006> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/c87ca890fa06> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A flowchart is presented with a light blue box at the top left labeled \"Smell, Taste, Mechanical,\" which connects via a green arrow to an orange oval labeled \"Vagus Nerve.\" Below the \"Vagus Nerve,\" another green arrow leads to an \"Enteric Nerve Plexus\" oval. From this plexus, two green arrows extend to two pink ovals: \"G Cell\" on the left and \"ECL Cell\" on the right. The \"G Cell\" sends a green arrow labeled \"Gastrin\" to the \"ECL Cell,\" while the \"ECL Cell\" sends a green arrow labeled \"Histamine\" to a yellow oval labeled \"Parietal Cell.\" Another green arrow labeled \"ACh\" goes from the \"Parietal Cell\" back to the \"ECL Cell,\" and a final green arrow labeled \"HCl\" points downward from the \"Parietal Cell.\" On the right side, two dashed green lines are labeled \"Head\" at the top and \"Stomach\" at the bottom. Additional labels \"ACh,\" \"Gastrin,\" \"Histamine,\" and \"HCl\" appear near their respective pathways." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
