<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized with \"Peptides\" at the top left, leading downward to the \"G Cell\" below. \"Gastric distention\" is positioned at the top center, pointing to the \"Enteric Nerve Plexus,\" while \"Vagal Nucleus\" is at the top right, also connecting to the \"Enteric Nerve Plexus.\" The \"Enteric Nerve Plexus\" is a rounded shape near the center, receiving inputs from both \"Gastric distention\" and \"Vagal Nucleus.\" Below this, the \"G Cell\" is connected by an arrow labeled \"Gastrin\" to the \"ECL Cell,\" which in turn connects to the \"Parietal Cell\" via an arrow labeled \"Histamine.\" The \"Parietal Cell\" is influenced by an arrow labeled \"ACh\" and contains \"HCl,\" indicating hydrochloric acid production. The \"D Cell\" is positioned below the \"Parietal Cell,\" connected by an arrow labeled \"Somatostatin,\" with \"Somatostatin\" pointing upward to the \"D Cell.\" On the far right, a dashed rectangular box labeled \"Stomach\" encloses the \"Parietal Cell\" and \"D Cell.\"" <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/b6278d0d1cf6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/46242002> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s5> .
