<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p51_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "In the center of the image, slightly towards the top, there is a circular area labeled \"Co,\" which appears to represent a cavity or lumen. Surrounding this area, the tissue consists of cells with dark purple nuclei scattered throughout, indicating the presence of hematoxylin staining. Pink-stained areas, representing extracellular matrix or connective tissue, are also visible, stained with eosin. The overall layout shows a layered structure typical of epithelial tissue lining a lumen, with darker-staining cells forming the epithelial layer and lighter areas representing the underlying connective tissue." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s13> .
