<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p53_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with a pinkish hue typical of H&E staining. The section features two main labeled areas: 'T' is centrally located and appears to represent a tissue sample, possibly a tumor or mass, surrounded by a lighter area that might indicate stroma or connective tissue. 'C' is positioned over a cluster of cells at the bottom left, which have darker nuclei and lighter cytoplasm, suggesting they might be cancerous cells or involved in a pathological process. The overall coloration varies in intensity, indicating different tissue densities and cellular components. There are no arrows or leader lines connecting the labels to specific parts of the image." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s13> .
