<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p52_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E). The cells are densely packed, with nuclei stained purple and cytoplasm appearing pinkish-white. Two labeled areas marked with \"L\" are near large, pale-staining spaces, suggesting lumen-like structures. An arrow points to a single cell marked with \"C,\" which has a larger nucleus compared to the surrounding cells. The overall layout shows a dense network of cells with some spaces between them, and there is a \"b\" in the bottom left corner, possibly indicating a specific section or slide identifier." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s13> .
