<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is divided into two main sections. On the left, there's a simplified illustration of the brain with the pituitary gland shown as a small, round structure at the base, connected by arrows from the hypothalamus, indicating hormone release. On the right, a flowchart with six rows details different hormone pathways. Each row features arrows connecting the releasing hormone to the pituitary hormone, then to the target gland, and finally to the effect on the body. The arrows are straight lines with arrowheads pointing from left to right, and the text describing the effects is aligned to the right of these arrows." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/f4b750f45a6c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#stimulates> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/b9ae4f689dbd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/62818001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/264483005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/bea1255030bb> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The hypothalamus is positioned at the top of the diagram, with the supraoptic nuclei located near the top left and the paraventricular nuclei situated slightly below them. The mamillary body is on the right side of the hypothalamus. Directly below the hypothalamus is the median eminence, which connects to the pituitary gland through the infundibulum. The anterior lobe of the pituitary gland is shown below the median eminence and infundibulum, containing endocrine cells depicted in a yellowish color. The posterior lobe of the pituitary gland is situated below the anterior lobe and is connected to the hypothalamus by the hypophyseal vein. Capillary beds are illustrated within the anterior lobe as a network of small blood vessels, and the superior hypophyseal artery is shown supplying blood to the superior part of the pituitary gland. The optic chiasm is located above the hypothalamus, connecting the optic nerves." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/733c5747d119> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/62818001> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/733c5747d119> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/264483005> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomical layout and functional relationships of the hypothalamus, pituitary gland, and adrenal gland." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p8_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed anatomical illustration of the human brain, with the cerebral cortex labeled on the outer surface. Near the base, the amygdala is depicted as a small, rounded structure. The hypothalamus is positioned below the thalamus, appearing as a larger, more complex structure. Within the medulla oblongata, the nucleus ambiguus is shown as a small, oval-shaped structure, while the ventrolateral medulla extends from it. The periaqueductal gray matter is located near the midline of the brainstem, appearing as a darker, textured area, with the parabrachial nucleus situated adjacent to it, also dark and textured. The dorsal motor vagal nucleus is a cluster of cells in the medulla oblongata, and the nucleus of the solitary tract is another small, oval-shaped structure within the medulla. An inset diagram of the heart is placed at the bottom left corner, connected by a red arrow to the ventrolateral medulla." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/cb94d9e1175e> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/c7f4add6d3df> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/bea1255030bb> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#stimulates> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
