<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/f4b750f45a6c> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/ee63e4617629> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the hypothalamic-pituitary-target gland axis, showing the pathways of hormone release from the hypothalamus and their effects on various target glands." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p22_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A side view of the brain is presented, with the hypothalamus highlighted in purple and an arrow pointing to it. The hypothalamus is connected to the posterior pituitary, depicted as a small, bulbous structure, with text indicating their connection. The anterior pituitary is shown as a round, granular structure positioned below the hypothalamus. On the right, the adrenal gland is illustrated as a triangular structure with a central medulla, both labeled accordingly. Sympathetic preganglionic axons are depicted extending from the hypothalamus towards the adrenal gland, emphasizing the connection between these structures." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/216fea4b0c37> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p7_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a cross-sectional view of the brain, with various structures labeled using arrows and text boxes. The septum pellucidum is positioned at the top left, while the pellucidum is near the top center. The hypothalamic sulcus is on the right side, and the choroid plexus is located towards the upper right. The interventricular foramen is on the left side, and the hypothalamus is situated centrally. Below the choroid plexus is the aqueduct, and at the bottom left is the lamina terminalis. The mammillary body is at the bottom center. The labels are color-coded in purple, green, yellow, and blue to help distinguish the different anatomical parts." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/216fea4b0c37> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/7824> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/a47b56b4eef0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/a47b56b4eef0> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#stimulates> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure is divided into four sections. In the top left, the title \"Tuberoinfundibular dopamine (TIDA) neurons in the hypothalamus\" is displayed above a tissue section stained red, likely indicating dopamine neurons. A green circle with a plus sign is drawn around a specific neuron, and a black arrow points downward from this circle to a pink circle labeled \"Dopamine secretion in median eminence.\" On the top right, two horizontal lines labeled 1 and 2 are shown; line 1 has a few short vertical lines spaced apart, while line 2 has many closely packed short vertical lines. The bottom left section features a diagram of the dopamine secretion pathway. A green circle with a minus sign is around a neuron, and a red arrow points downward to a blue shape labeled \"Anterior pituitary gland.\" A dotted line extends from the anterior pituitary gland to the median eminence, and a green arrow points downward to the word \"Prolactin.\" In the bottom right, two smaller images labeled 1 and 2 are displayed; image 1 shows a tissue section with a light background and darker areas, while image 2 shows a similar section with numerous dark spots." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s4> .
