<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a pink outer layer representing the gut lumen, containing yellow and brown bacteria rods and spheres. Below this, the epithelial layer is light pink with green, oval-shaped villi extending into the lumen. At the center, a purple subepithelial dome houses a cluster of blue circles with green centers, indicating B cells. Beneath the dome, Peyer's patch appears as a large, light purple circle filled with similar B cells. To the right, a smaller follicle labeled \"follicle (B cells)\" contains more B cells. An isolated lymphoid follicle is positioned on the far right, also containing B cells. The lamina propria, a pink region beneath the epithelial layer, holds the submucosa and muscularis mucosa. The submucosa, a darker pink layer, features a network of blood vessels and connective tissues. The muscularis mucosa is a green circular area with muscle fibers. At the bottom, a mesenteric lymph node is depicted as a green circle with a central blue circle. Arrows indicate movement from the gut lumen to the epithelial layer, while leader lines connect labels to their respective parts." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s7> .
