<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/5e38ff927e89> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/398252006> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p36_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized into three main sections. On the left, glucose polymers are represented by Starch and Glycogen, each depicted as a series of connected hexagons. A curved arrow labeled \"Amylase\" points from these polymers to the middle section, which contains the disaccharides: Maltose, Sucrose, and Lactose. Each disaccharide is shown as two hexagons connected by a single bond. Arrows then lead from the disaccharides to the bottom section, where the monosaccharides are displayed. Each monosaccharide is represented by a single hexagon. The enzymes involved, Amylase, Maltase, Sucrase, and Lactase, are indicated by arrows connecting the sections. The color scheme differentiates the sugars: blue for glucose, pink for fructose, and purple for galactose." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s7> .
<http://snomed.info/id/87311002> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caused_by> <http://snomed.info/id/19655003> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s7> .
