<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p38_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with \"Lumen\" at the top left corner and \"ECF\" at the top right corner. The central part of the diagram is labeled \"Intestinal cell,\" and the cell membrane is depicted as a blue structure. Two green boxes are positioned near the top left and right sides of the diagram, containing the numbers \"1\" and \"2\" respectively. The green box near the top left states \"Na+ enters cells by multiple pathways,\" while the one near the top right says \"The Na+-K+-ATPase pumps Na+ into the ECF.\" Arrows indicate the movement of sodium (Na+), chloride (Cl-), hydrogen (H+), bicarbonate (HCO3-), organic solutes, water (H2O), and potassium (K+) ions across the membrane. An ATP molecule is shown on the right side, and the Na+-K+-ATPase pump is depicted as a mechanism using ATP to move sodium ions out of the cell into the extracellular fluid. A note in the bottom right corner states that water and potassium move through the paracellular pathway, indicated by arrows showing their movement between the cell layers." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s7> .
