<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p42_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The infographic has a teal background and is organized into sections, each focusing on a different component of the immune system's role in the gut. Near the top left, a circular label with a light blue background points to an illustration of the human digestive tract, including the small intestine and large intestine, and reads \"Gut-Associated Lymphoid Tissue.\" Below the main title, another circular label with a light blue background points to a smaller diagram showing various types of immune cells, including a virus and a cell with a nucleus, and reads \"Immune Cells.\" On the bottom right, a similar circular label points to a colorful depiction of different bacteria and microorganisms and reads \"Microbiota.\" Between the \"Immune Cells\" and \"Microbiota\" labels, a white Y-shaped symbol representing antibodies is placed, with the word \"Antibodies\" written in black text below it. The overall layout uses colors like pink, purple, green, and orange to differentiate the various elements." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/20982000> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s7> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features the lumen of the stomach positioned at the top left corner, while the interstitial fluid is situated at the top right. On the far right, a capillary is depicted, representing a blood vessel. The central focus of the illustration is the parietal cell, which is prominently displayed in the main body of the diagram." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s7> .
