<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is divided into three main sections, each with distinct labels: \"Hormonal Feedback,\" \"Neural Feedback,\" and \"Direct Feedback.\" In the Hormonal Feedback section, there are four nodes: \"Thyroid hormone\" at the top-left, \"Anterior pituitary\" at the top-center, \"Thyroid-stimulating hormone\" at the bottom-center, and \"Thyroid gland\" at the bottom-left. Pink and black arrows connect these nodes, indicating the flow of the feedback loop. In the Neural Feedback section, five nodes are present: \"Supraoptic Nucleus Paraventricul Nuc\" at the top-right, \"High Osmolarity\" also at the top-right, \"Lower Blood Osmolarity\" at the bottom-center, \"Increased ADH release\" at the bottom-right, and \"More Water Reabsorption\" at the bottom-center. Again, pink and black arrows show the direction of the feedback loop. Finally, the Direct Feedback section includes three nodes: \"Pancreas (β cells)\" at the top-center, \"High blood glucose\" at the top-right, and \"Increased insulin release\" at the bottom-right, with arrows indicating their connections." <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
