<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p12_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The figure consists of three separate graphs, each labeled with the hormone it represents. The top graph is labeled \"Melatonin\" in red text at the top right, the middle graph is labeled \"Cortisol\" in red text at the bottom left, and the bottom graph is labeled \"Growth hormone\" in red text at the bottom right. Each graph has the x-axis labeled with numbers indicating hours throughout the day, ranging from 6 to 24. The blue shaded areas on the left and right sides of each graph represent nighttime, while the light-colored area in the middle represents daytime. Each graph is separated by a horizontal black line, maintaining consistent blue shaded areas across all three graphs to represent nighttime hours." <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
