<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p16_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is titled \"FEEDBACK CONTROL IN THE ENDOCRINE SYSTEM\" and is organized with the hypothalamus at the top right, connected by arrows to the pituitary gland below it. The pituitary gland is positioned centrally, receiving a neurohormone from the hypothalamus and releasing trophic hormones that stimulate the peripheral glands, which are located below the pituitary gland. The peripheral glands include the thyroid, adrenal cortex, and gonad, and are shown at the bottom of the chart. Arrows indicate short-loop feedback signals from the peripheral glands back to the hypothalamus and long-loop feedback signals to the pituitary gland. On the left side, a separate gland section includes the pancreas and parathyroid, with arrows indicating feedback signals affecting hormone production by the peripheral glands. The flowchart uses blue boxes to represent different organs and systems, with arrows showing the direction of hormonal signals and feedback loops. Text labels are placed within or near the relevant boxes." <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/1e51f9503ba7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#regulates> <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
