<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p46_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with 'Stress' at the top left, directing an arrow labeled 'Excites' toward the 'Hypothalamus' at the top center. From the Hypothalamus, three small circles labeled 'Portal vessel (CRF)' extend downward to the 'Median Eminence'. A dashed line connects the 'Portal vessel (CRF)' to the 'Median Eminence', with 'CRF' noted alongside. A red arrow labeled 'ACTH' points downward from the 'Median Eminence' to the 'Adrenal cortex', which is depicted as a beige, elongated shape. Another red arrow leads from the 'Adrenal Cortex' to 'Cortisol', positioned on the right. A curved red arrow from 'Cortisol' points back to the 'Adrenal Cortex', and a dashed line from 'Cortisol' to the 'Hypothalamus' is labeled 'Inhibits'. At the bottom left, a blue box lists 'Gluconeogenesis', 'Protein mobilization', 'Fat mobilization', and 'Stabilizes lysosomes', each numbered 1 through 4." <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/c4b9edafe7b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
