<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates three types of feedback loops in endocrinology: hormonal, neural, and direct, each with its own set of interconnected nodes and directional arrows." <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/1adba573de92> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p56_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with hypothalamic hormones positioned at the top left corner, connected by dashed lines to the anterior pituitary gland situated just below. The anterior pituitary hormones are displayed centrally, each linked to their respective target glands or tissues through arrows labeled \"Tropin.\" Below these, the target glands are depicted, including the thyroid gland, adrenal cortex, liver, and gonads. Nonendocrine targets, such as the breast, are shown at the bottom left. Near the right side, the endocrine cells of the gonads are illustrated, while germ cells are located at the bottom right. Above the anterior pituitary, neurons secreting trophic hormones are positioned, including TRH and CRH." <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/128136d02cd8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#assertionType> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#stimulates> <urn:graph:endocrine/s4> .
