<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/f6891217ccf3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#secretes> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p60_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed view of glandular tissue, with follicles positioned at the top left, containing a pinkish substance that represents colloid. Near these follicles, capillaries are visible, indicated by their red coloration. Below the capillaries, an arteriole is situated, also marked in red, while a venule is placed beneath the arteriole, appearing slightly less prominent. At the bottom left, follicular cells are closely packed, forming the outer layer of the follicles. A tangential section of follicular cells is shown at the top right, revealing their layered arrangement. Interfollicular connective tissue, indicated by a lighter pink color with scattered cell nuclei, is found between the follicles, containing connective tissue septa that act as fibrous partitions. In the middle right, a tangential section of a follicle is displayed, while on the right, a follicle with retracted colloid shows a noticeable gap in its colloid content. Finally, parafollicular cells are scattered at the bottom right, appearing smaller and individual compared to the grouped follicular cells." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/c1aee851d3a2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p63_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The table is organized into four columns and two rows, with a green header row that labels the columns as \"Hormone,\" \"Composition,\" \"Source,\" and \"Major Functions.\" The rows alternate in background color between light and dark green for improved readability. The text within each cell is aligned to the left, and there are no additional visual elements such as images, icons, leader lines, or arrows." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s5> .
