<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p59_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a detailed microscopic cross-section of tissue, with various labels pointing to different structures. At the top left, an arrow indicates a retracted, distorted colloid, appearing as a collapsed or compressed area. Near the top right, follicular cells are marked, showing clusters of cells with round nuclei and distinct cytoplasmic boundaries. Slightly below these, parafollicular cells are labeled, also appearing as a cluster with similar characteristics. Centrally, a capillary is labeled, appearing as a thin-walled blood vessel surrounded by follicular cells. Another capillary is similarly labeled in the center. At the bottom left, a blood vessel is labeled, showing a larger vessel with red blood cells inside. Near this, follicular cells are labeled again, this time in a tangential section, displaying their layered arrangement. At the top right, follicles containing colloid are labeled. The interfollicular connective tissue is labeled between the follicles. Near the bottom right, more follicular cells are labeled, and at the very bottom right, parafollicular cells are labeled again. The tissue is composed of pinkish regions for the extracellular matrix and blue regions for cell nuclei, with black text labels on a white background." <urn:graph:histology_endocrine/s5> .
