<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/4857607a3520> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/23230007> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a front view of the human digestive system, with the salivary gland labeled on the left side of the face near the cheek. The esophagus is depicted as a straight tube extending from the throat down into the chest cavity, with the upper esophageal sphincter labeled above it and the lower esophageal sphincter below it. The liver is shown in the upper right quadrant of the abdomen, with a distinct shape and color, and the gallbladder is located below it, connected by a duct. The stomach is rounded with a distinct opening to the small intestine, where the pylorus is labeled. The pancreas is positioned behind the stomach, with a curved shape. The small intestine is portrayed as a coiled structure, while the large intestine is shown as a straight tube leading to the rectum. The ileocecal valve is labeled at the junction between the ileum and the cecum, and the rectum is labeled at the end of the large intestine. Finally, the anal sphincters are depicted as two circular structures at the very bottom of the image." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/e7a20c051b19> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.9"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/0f893960b211> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/86355000> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/4857607a3520> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#predicate> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#part_of> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/14cb77147310> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/69695003> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/10200004> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p3_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration is divided into several sections, each focusing on different parts of the digestive system. In the top left, a side profile of a person's head and upper torso is shown, with labels pointing to the oral cavity, salivary glands, and esophagus. The top right section provides a close-up view of the head, highlighting the parotid, sublingual, and submandibular salivary glands. The middle section features a side profile of the upper torso, showing internal organs such as the gallbladder, pancreas, liver, stomach, small intestine, large intestine, and rectum. The bottom left section diagrams the large intestine, detailing its segments like the transverse colon, ascending colon, sigmoid colon, cecum, rectum, and anus, arranged in a curved manner. Finally, the bottom right section offers a detailed cross-sectional view of the small intestine, labeling layers and structures including the mucosa, submucosa, circular and longitudinal muscles, serosa, plica, submucosal glands, and villi." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
