<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents the digestive system with the stomach positioned at the top, appearing as a large, rounded organ with a slightly curved shape. Below the stomach, the small intestine is illustrated as a coiled tube extending downward and to the right, featuring numerous smaller loops and curves. The large intestine is shown beneath the small intestine, depicted as a wider, less coiled tube with more pronounced loops and curves. Throughout the diagram, black arrows point in various directions, indicating the flow of substances through the digestive tract. All elements are rendered in a consistent color scheme, with digestive organs in a light beige or tan shade and arrows in black." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
