<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p13_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a table with four rows and two columns. The first row serves as a header with the column titles \"Secretion\" and \"Digestion.\" The \"Secretion\" column contains the entry \"Mucus (goblet cells),\" while the \"Digestion\" column states \"None (except by bacteria).\" The second row, labeled \"Absorption,\" lists \"Ions, minerals, vitamins. Small organic molecules made by gut bacteria.\" The third row, labeled \"Motility,\" states \"Segmental mixing. Mass movement for propulsion.\" The table is neatly organized with clear separation between rows and columns, and there are no leader lines, arrows, or additional visual elements." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/056a40001019> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/70150004> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram provides a side view of the human body, with labels pointing to different parts of the digestive system. The labels are enclosed in boxes and connected by lines to their respective organs. The mouth and mouth cavity are labeled at the top left corner, with the pharynx positioned above the oesophagus. The oesophagus is shown below the pharynx, leading to the stomach. The liver is placed near the upper right side, with the gallbladder located below it. The pancreas is situated behind the stomach, while the large intestine is on the lower left side. The rectum is at the bottom of the large intestine, and the small intestine is positioned between the stomach and the large intestine. The anus is labeled at the very bottom of the diagram. Different colors are used to distinguish the digestive organs: red for the liver, gallbladder, and pancreas; green for the oesophagus, stomach, large intestine, small intestine, rectum, and anus; and yellow for the mouth and mouth cavity, and pharynx." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s1> .
