<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The esophagus is the central focus of the illustration, running vertically through the center and highlighted in a reddish-pink color. At the top, the pharynx is labeled, pointing to the upper part of the esophagus. On the right side, the cervical part is labeled, indicating the uppermost section extending from the pharynx down to the thoracic inlet. Near the middle, the arch of the aorta is labeled, positioned above the esophagus. The left principal bronchus is labeled on the left side, indicating the main airway of the left lung. The thoracic part is labeled on the right, showing the middle portion of the esophagus passing through the thoracic cavity. Near the bottom, the heart is labeled, pointing below the diaphragm, which is labeled at the very bottom, marking the muscular structure that separates the thoracic cavity from the abdominal cavity. Finally, the abdominal part is labeled on the right, indicating the lower part of the esophagus extending into the abdominal cavity." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/33154002> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p31_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the esophagus divided into cervical, thoracic, and abdominal parts, alongside labeled structures such as the pharynx, arch of the aorta, left principal bronchus, heart, and diaphragm." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
