<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image features a series of five black-and-white sketches arranged horizontally. Each sketch depicts a person's head and neck, with the person having long hair tied back in a ponytail. The first sketch shows the head tilted back with the chin on the chest. The fourth sketch illustrates the head slightly tilted to the side, looking to the right. Finally, the fifth sketch shows the head tilted back again, more pronouncedly than in the first, with the chin on the chest. Beneath these sketches, there is some light gray text reading \"car veins\" followed by a partially obscured word, with no leader lines or arrows connecting the text to the sketches." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
