<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the anatomical features of the back of a person's neck and upper back, including the external occipital protuberance, nuchal groove, C7 and T1 to T4 spinous processes, and the supraspinous ligament." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p4_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-section of the neck with a circular outline symbolizing the skin and subcutaneous tissue. At the top left, the word \"Fascia\" is positioned, with labels for the four main fascial compartments: Pretracheal, Superficial Carotid sheath, Investing, and Prevertebral. The Pretracheal compartment is shown anteriorly, surrounding the centrally depicted trachea. The term \"Anterior\" is centered at the top, indicating the anterior compartment, which includes the visceral and carotid sheath structures. The \"Posterior\" label is at the bottom center, marking the posterior compartment that includes the vascular and vertebral structures. Leader lines connect each label to its corresponding region in the diagram, providing clarity on the placement of each structure." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
