<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a cross-section of the tracheal wall, with the outermost layer appearing as a light pinkish-red ring. Inside this, a darker pinkish-red ring represents the muscular layer, and the innermost layer is a lighter pinkish-red ring, likely the mucosal lining. At the center, there's a circular opening, the lumen, through which air passes. The color gradient moves from light blue at the edges to beige at the center, with small white dots scattered throughout the blue sections, possibly indicating cartilage rings." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
