<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a close-up view of the back of the neck and upper back, with labels pointing to specific anatomical features. At the top center, a label indicates the external occipital protuberance, a small bump at the base of the skull. Just below this, the nuchal groove is labeled, followed by the C7 spinous process, also known as the vertebra prominens. Further down, the T1, T2, and T4 spinous processes are labeled in sequence. The supraspinous ligament is shown as a band-like structure spanning between these spinous processes. All labels are connected to their corresponding features by thin, straight lines." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p29_b8> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A cross-sectional view of the tracheal wall, showing its external, middle, and inner layers, along with the central lumen." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s5> .
