<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/1427222> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized in a circular layout, starting with a box at the top labeled \"↓ Ca++\" connected to another box labeled \"CaSR.\" From the \"CaSR\" box, an arrow points downward to a box labeled \"↑ PTH.\" The \"PTH\" box has arrows extending to three areas: \"Bone\" on the left, \"Kidney\" on the right, and \"Intestine\" below. The \"Bone\" area has an upward arrow indicating \"↑ Bone resorption\" and \"↑ Ca++ efflux.\" The \"Kidney\" area shows two upward arrows for \"↑ 1,25 Dihydroxy-cholecalciferol\" and \"↑ Ca++ reabs.,\" and a downward arrow for \"↓ PO₄ reabs.\" The \"Intestine\" area has upward arrows for \"↑ Ca++ reabs.\" and \"↑ PO₄ reabs.\" An arrow from the \"Kidney\" area points back to a box labeled \"↑ Ca++\" at the bottom, completing the cycle. The diagram includes a reference \"RIS-04/25\" in the bottom-left corner and the number \"22\" in the bottom-right corner." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/1895> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A table with a light pink background is framed by a thin black border. The table has two columns: the first is labeled \"Function\" and the second is labeled \"Example.\" The \"Function\" column lists four categories: structural, neuromuscular, enzymic, and signaling. The title \"Functions of calcium\" is centered above the table in a larger font size. There are no leader lines or arrows." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/adc2a6cf3177> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/90780006> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1cf1d57032ec> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.8"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1cf1d57032ec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://snomed.info/id/4421005> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/b025f0544c13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/adc2a6cf3177> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/312472004> <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A central red cylinder represents circulation, with two white circles and black arrows inside indicating the concentration of calcium ions in the blood. The thyroid gland is a pinkish oval shape with white spots at the top center, while the parathyroid glands are similarly shaped and positioned slightly below and to the right. The kidney is on the left, connected by green arrows to the thyroid gland, small intestine, and bone. The small intestine is below the kidney, and the bone is below the small intestine, both connected by green arrows to the thyroid gland. Green arrows from the thyroid point to the kidney, small intestine, and bone, representing calcitonin's effects, while blue arrows from the parathyroid glands point to these organs, representing PTH's effects. A curved blue arrow loops back from the kidney to the parathyroid glands, suggesting a feedback mechanism. Text labels 'Lower Blood [Ca²⁺]' and 'Raise Blood [Ca²⁺]' are at the bottom left and right of the central diagram, respectively." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p34_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized into sections, starting with a box at the top labeled \"PLASMA CALCIUM CONCENTRATION\" with an arrow pointing downward. This box connects to another labeled \"PARATHYROID HORMONE SECRETION,\" which has an upward arrow. From there, an arrow leads to a box labeled \"PLASMA PARATHYROID HORMONE CONCENTRATION,\" also with an upward arrow. On the left, arrows connect \"PLASMA PARATHYROID HORMONE CONCENTRATION\" to \"RENAL TUBULAR REABSORPTION OF PHOSPHATE,\" then to \"URINARY EXCRETION OF PHOSPHATE,\" and finally to \"PLASMA PHOSPHATE CONCENTRATION,\" which has a downward arrow. On the right, arrows lead from \"PLASMA PARATHYROID HORMONE CONCENTRATION\" to \"FORMATION OF 1,25-(OH)₂ D₃ BY KIDNEYS,\" then to \"PLASMA CONCENTRATION OF 1,25-(OH)₂ D₃,\" which has an upward arrow. At the bottom, arrows connect \"PLASMA PARATHYROID HORMONE CONCENTRATION\" to \"BONE RESORPTION,\" then to \"RELEASE OF CALCIUM INTO PLASMA,\" and finally to \"URINARY EXCRETION OF CALCIUM,\" which has a downward arrow." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
