<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p20_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large bone structure is positioned on the left side of the diagram, containing a note that highlights \"25,000 mmol\" of calcium, with \"100 mmol rapidly exchangeable\" emphasized. Arrows indicate calcium movement: \"exchange 500 mmol/24 h\" from bone to the central rectangular box labeled \"extracellular fluid (ECF)\", \"bone formation 7.5 mmol/24 h\" from ECF to bone, and \"bone resorption 7.5 mmol/24 h\" from bone to ECF. The ECF box, situated centrally, contains \"22.5 mmol\" of calcium and has several arrows indicating different fluxes: \"absorption 12 mmol/24 h\" from gut to ECF, \"secretion 6 mmol/24 h\" from ECF to gut, \"reabsorption 234 mmol/24 h\" and \"glomerular filtration 240 mmol/24 h\" both involving the kidney, and \"skin 0.3 mmol/24 h\" from ECF to skin. Within the ECF box, a smaller rectangle labeled \"plasma\" contains \"9.0 mmol\" of calcium. On the right side, a simplified representation of the gut receives \"25 mmol/24 h\" of calcium from food, with arrows for \"absorption 12 mmol/24 h\" to ECF and \"secretion 6 mmol/24 h\" from ECF. Below the ECF, a simplified kidney is shown with flux arrows." <urn:graph:parathyroid_gland/s4> .
