<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the inferior vena cava positioned at the top left, pointing to a circular opening, while the esophagus is at the top right, extending downward as a tube-like structure. Near the bottom left, the left crus and right crus are depicted as curved structures on either side of the esophagus. The median arcuate ligament is shown near the bottom center as a thin, horizontal structure connecting the two crura. Below this, the celiac axis appears as a small, branching structure, with the larger, branching abdominal aorta situated beneath it." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s12> .
