<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration provides a detailed view of the venous system, with emphasis on the thoracic and abdominal areas. Major veins are clearly labeled and positioned throughout the image, allowing viewers to trace the flow of blood through these regions. The thoracic veins are situated towards the upper part of the image, while the abdominal veins are depicted lower down. The layout is organized to highlight the interconnected nature of the venous network, with key structures like the superior and inferior vena cava prominently displayed." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_neck/s12> .
