<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top left corner of the image, the title \"STRESS RESPONSE SYSTEM\" is displayed. Near the top right, a gray, brain-like structure represents the hypothalamus. An arrow labeled \"CRH\" extends from the hypothalamus to a small, teardrop-shaped structure, the pituitary gland. From the pituitary gland, another arrow labeled \"ACTH\" points towards a yellow, rounded structure, the adrenal gland. A label for \"Cortisol\" directs from the adrenal gland towards a cluster of blue dots labeled \"To immune system.\" A curved red arrow, reading \"The hypothalamus responds to level of cortisol,\" loops back from the adrenal gland to the hypothalamus." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s10> .
