<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p35_b10> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a cross-sectional view of the brain, with the cerebral cortex depicted as a wrinkled, convoluted surface at the top. Near the center-top, the pineal gland is shown as a small, rounded structure below the cerebral cortex. The suprachiasmatic nucleus is positioned near the base, marked by an arrow pointing to a small, oval-shaped structure above the optic chiasm. The optic chiasm is labeled with an arrow indicating the crossing point of the optic nerves below the suprachiasmatic nucleus. The pituitary is a small, round structure located below the hypothalamus, with an arrow pointing to it from the left. The hypothalamus, situated between the pituitary and the thalamus, is indicated by an arrow from the right, appearing as a large, irregularly shaped structure." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s18> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/f0487299a4ab> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s18> .
