<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The sphenoid bone is shown in a light brown color, with a three-dimensional perspective that highlights the central area as the most prominent. The labels are strategically placed around the bone, connected by leader lines to specific areas. The superior orbital fissure is positioned at the top-left corner, while the optic canal is just below it. The foramen rotundum, foramen spinosum, and foramen oval are all located on the lesser wing." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s18> .
