<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a side view of the pituitary gland, with the hypothalamus positioned at the top left, connected to the pituitary gland via the infundibulum. The infundibulum is a narrow, tube-like structure situated below the hypothalamus. The posterior lobe of the pituitary gland is located at the top right, while the anterior lobe is at the bottom. An inset in the top right corner provides a magnified view of the connection between the hypothalamus and the infundibulum, highlighted by a pink square in the main diagram." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s18> .
