<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p27_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-section of the pituitary gland, with the Pars tuberalis positioned at the top, marked by a black line pointing to the uppermost part. The Pars anterior is colored blue and occupies the lower portion of the gland, indicated by a black line. The Pars intermedia is situated between the Pars anterior and the Posterior lobe, colored red and labeled with a black line. The Posterior lobe is colored yellow and is located above the Pars intermedia, also labeled with a black line. The sella turcica, shown in gray on the left side, surrounds the pituitary gland." <urn:graph:anatomy_of_endocrine_glands/s18> .
