<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/a5ee992ef8e2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#Statement> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the neural pathways involved in the cephalic phase of digestion as part of the gastrointestinal reflexes." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/a5ee992ef8e2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#confidence> "0.8"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p7_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A diagram shows a series of smooth muscle cells arranged in a layered pattern. Each cell is elongated and oval-shaped with a nucleus at its center and a pinkish-red cytoplasmic region. Gap junctions are represented as small blue squares located between the smooth muscle cells, indicating points of communication. Nerve fibers are depicted as thin, wavy lines extending from the left side of the image towards the right. The text labels \"GAP JUNCTION,\" \"SMOOTH MUSCLE CELL,\" and \"NERVE FIBERS\" are positioned to point directly to their respective elements in the diagram." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/6699113e3d57> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#extractedBy> "llm-re" <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/921b4d5458bb> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#polarity> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#Uncertain> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure presents a table comparing the Enteric Nervous System (ENS) and the Central Nervous System (CNS), highlighting their intrinsic neurons and the role of extrinsic neurons in the CNS." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/66787007> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
