<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/1bd299c01f4f> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/69854003> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p11_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/417718001> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top of the image, the title \"1. CEPHALIC PHASE\" appears in red text. On the left side, two food items are depicted: a cup with a straw featuring a blue and white striped pattern, and a pastry with red and brown toppings. These food items are connected by dashed black lines to a human head and brain shown in profile on the right side, facing left. A red arrow labeled \"Vagus nerve\" points from the brain down to the stomach, indicating the pathway of the vagus nerve. The stomach is illustrated below the vagus nerve, colored light green with darker shading to represent its walls and contents. Below the food items, the text reads: \"Sight, smell or thought of food.\" At the bottom of the image, it states: \"- Parasympathetic activation of gastric motility & gastric juice secretion.\" A red arrow extends from the stomach to the right, suggesting the direction of action related to the parasympathetic activation." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/47220008> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p10_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is a table with two main columns and five rows. The first column is labeled \"ENS\" for Enteric Nervous System, and the second column is labeled \"CNS\" for Central Nervous System." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/921b4d5458bb> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#target> <http://snomed.info/id/4421005> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p7_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/39822001> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/8215b47c3212> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://snomed.info/id/72167002> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b4> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the cephalic phase of digestion, showing how external stimuli like food sight and smell influence the brain and stomach through the vagus nerve." <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p7_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/71616004> <urn:graph:digestive_system/s8> .
