<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p74_b7> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with several labeled regions. At the bottom left, the label \"Mucus\" points to a lighter pink area. Slightly above and to the right of \"Mucus,\" \"Mucous acini\" indicates a cluster of darker pink structures. \"Serous acini\" is also at the bottom left, pointing to a darker pink region. On the right side, \"Serous demilunes\" highlights a lighter pink area. Near the center-right, \"Intercalated duct\" points to a narrow duct-like structure, while at the bottom right, \"Striated duct\" indicates a larger duct with striated epithelial cells. The inset image labels \"ducts\" within the glandular tissue. The tissue appears densely packed with different cell types and structures, each distinguished by their staining characteristics." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
