<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p75_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a detailed microscopic view of tissue, likely from an exocrine gland, stained with hematoxylin and eosin. Numbers and arrows point to specific structures within the tissue. At the top left, an arrow indicates a crescent-shaped serous demilune. An arteriole is found in the upper central area, while interlobular connective tissue is situated in the middle left. A venule is located near the middle right, and an interlobular excretory duct is at the bottom left. Myoepithelial cells are also at the bottom left, while an intralobular excretory duct is in the top right. Mucous acini are in the top right, and adipose cells are near the top right as well. Serous acini are in the middle right, and another interlobular excretory duct is in the middle right. A serous demilune is in the bottom right. At the bottom of the image, four smaller diagrams labeled I through IV are present: I shows a mucous acinus, II shows a mucous acinus with a serous demilune, III shows an intercalated duct, and IV shows an interlobular excretory duct. Each diagram provides a cross-sectional view of the respective structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
