<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p72_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two sections: the main section (a) at the top and the magnified inset (b) below it. Arrows in the main section point to the central region where narrow, tubular ducts are visible. The magnified inset provides a closer view of the ducts, showing them in cross-section with a circular shape and a central lumen, surrounded by both serous and mucous cells. Text labels near the respective areas indicate the location of ducts, serous cells, and mucous cells, with leader lines connecting them to the relevant structures." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p75_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A detailed microscopic view of an exocrine gland, such as the salivary gland, stained with hematoxylin and eosin, with labeled structures including serous demilunes, intercalated ducts, arterioles, connective tissue, venules, excretory ducts, myoepithelial cells, mucous and serous acini, and adipose cells." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
