<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p66_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents two diagrams, labeled \"a\" and \"b,\" both showing cross-sectional views of glandular structures. Each diagram has a consistent layout with the same labeling and color coding. In both diagrams, the top portion of the cross-section features an outermost layer labeled \"serous demilune.\" Below this layer, there are alternating layers of \"mucous cells\" and \"serous cells,\" with the mucous cells colored yellow and the serous cells colored red. At the bottom of each diagram, there is a long, narrow structure labeled \"intercalated duct.\"" <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
