<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "The figure illustrates the structures within an acinus, likely from a salivary gland, including a serous acinus, intercalated duct, serous demilune of a mixed acinus, striated ducts, basal laminae, and a mucous tubule." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/75535001> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/50292000> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The parotid salivary gland is positioned at the top left, near the cheek, and the parotid duct extends as a curved line towards the mouth. The masseter muscle is a thick, red structure on the side of the jaw, below the ear. The mucosa is shown cut away, revealing internal structures, and the sublingual ducts appear as small, branching tubes within this area. The sublingual salivary gland is depicted with a dotted outline beneath the tongue, and the mylohyoid muscle is a thin, horizontal structure under the mandible." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p72_b9> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#caption> "A histological section stained with hematoxylin and eosin (H&E) showing serous and mucous cells with ducts labeled." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
