<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1b796ced6088> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#object> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/743> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p66_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section with a dense network of acini and ducts. At the top left, a lighter area indicates mucus. Below this, mucous acini appear as rounded shapes with a pale pinkish hue. Serous acini are positioned at the bottom left, showing a darker pinkish-red color and a more compact structure. Scattered throughout are serous demilunes, small crescent-shaped structures appearing as lighter pink areas within the serous acini. In the middle right, intercalated ducts are narrow and elongated with a darker pink coloration. On the far right, the striated duct exhibits a pronounced striated pattern with alternating light and dark bands and a darker pink coloration." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/stmt/1b796ced6088> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#subject> <http://snomed.info/id/45289007> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
