<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p62_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/15152006> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized to show the progression from the acinar cells through the ducts to the mucous tubule. At the top left, the serous acinus is depicted as a cluster of cells with a central lumen, surrounded by myoepithelial cells, and intercellular secretory canaliculi connecting the cells. Below the serous acinus, an intercalated duct is shown as a long, narrow tube with a single layer of cells. On the right side, the serous demilune of a mixed acinus appears as a half-moon shape with myoepithelial cells around the lumen. Intercalated ducts are illustrated as interconnected tubes leading to the striated ducts, which are positioned below and depicted as a coiled tube with a single layer of cells. At the base of the striated ducts, a thin basal lamina is shown. Finally, at the bottom right, the mucous tubule is represented as a circular tube with a single layer of cells." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
