<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p69_b6> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The illustration presents a detailed view of a salivary gland, with multiple lobes visible. On the left side, a pinkish serous acinus is depicted, surrounded by myoepithelial cells, while on the right, a yellowish mucous acinus is similarly encircled by these cells. The connective tissue is shown as a yellowish layer surrounding the ducts and acini. Two zoomed-in sections provide a closer look at the internal structure of the serous and mucous acini, showing the network of cells and myoepithelial cells in each." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
