<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p116_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image displays a histological section of pancreatic tissue with a network of fibrous interlobular connective tissue at the top left. Near this area, a thin-walled blood vessel filled with dark red blood is visible. Scattered throughout the image are clusters of cells with darker nuclei, representing the cells of pancreatic islets. In the lower left, a small, curved intercalated duct connects to the acini. The main glandular units, serous acini and zymogenic cells, are clusters of cells with pale cytoplasm and darker nuclei, located at the bottom left and spread across the image. An interlobular duct, larger in size, is seen branching out into smaller ducts in the upper right. A Pacinian corpuscle, characterized by its spiral arrangement, is located in the upper right. Another blood vessel, similar to the first, is situated in the middle right. Fine, network-like capillaries are present within the pancreatic islets in the lower right." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p68_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#depicts> <http://snomed.info/id/362897009> <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
