<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p63_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the acinus positioned at the far left, depicted as a complex branching structure with a pink central core and yellow and red branches. Below the acinus, the intercalated duct is shown as a long, cylindrical structure with a pink top section and a green lower section. The striated duct is situated below the intercalated duct, also cylindrical, with a green top section and a blue lower section. At the bottom of the diagram, the excretory duct is displayed as a long, blue cylindrical structure. The top-right corner features pie charts above each type of salivary gland, indicating the ratio of cells with pink and yellow/gold sections. On the right side, vertical bar graphs represent the length of salivary ducts, color-coded to match the ducts: pink for the acinus, green for the intercalated duct, blue for the striated duct, and blue for the excretory duct." <urn:graph:histology_digestive_1/s3> .
